Object.assign(window.IND_FEED_BODY, {"hp-fk.tejimola-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tejimola:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tejimola, Who Kept Becoming","text":"कमल की पंखुड़ियाँ सिमट गईं, और पानी में से उड़कर एक मैना उसकी हथेली पर आ बैठी, और घर तक के पूरे रास्ते उसके कंधे से नहीं उतरी। अपने दरवाज़े पर पहुँचकर उसने कहा, \"अब पूरी तरह से। अपने असली रूप में।\" और वहाँ खड़ी थी तेजिमोला — पहले से दुबली, आँखों से कुछ बड़ी, और रूप पूरा बदलने से पहले ही गाने लगी।","lang":"hi","body":"The lotus folded, and a mynah flew up out of the water and landed on his palm, and would not leave his shoulder the whole way home. At his own door he said, \"Now all of it. Your own shape.\" And there stood Tejimola — thinner, older about the eyes, and singing before she was done becoming.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tejimola.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tejimola|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tejimola-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tejimola:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tejimola, Who Kept Becoming","text":"उसने उसे सब कुछ बता दिया, साफ़-साफ़, जैसे वह अपनी हर बात कहती थी। सौतेली माँ को वापस उसके गाँव भेज दिया गया, और बात वहीं ख़त्म हुई — घर को चीखने-चिल्लाने की ज़रूरत नहीं थी, उसे तो अपना खोया हुआ गाना वापस चाहिए था, और वह उसे मिल गया।","lang":"hi","body":"She told him everything, plainly, the way she did all things. The stepmother was sent back to her own village, and that was the whole of it — the house did not need shouting, it needed its singing back, and it got it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tejimola.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tejimola|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bordoisila-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bordoisila:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wind Who Runs Home to Her Mother","text":"असम में ठंड के मौसम के बिल्कुल आख़िर में, जब आम के पेड़ों पर बौर आ जाता है, हमेशा एक ऐसी शाम आती है जब हवा अचानक तेज़ हो उठती है — दरवाज़ों को खटखटाती, बरामदे से बर्तनों को लुढ़काती और सबको सूखते कपड़े समेटने के लिए दौड़ाती हुई। और दादी अपने काम से सिर उठाकर कहेंगी, \"लो आ गई। बोरदोईसिला।\"","lang":"hi","body":"At the very end of the cold season in Assam, when the mango trees are in flower, there always comes an evening when the wind gets up all at once — banging doors, rolling pots off verandas, sending everyone running for the washing. And a grandmother will look up from her work and say, \"There she is. Bordoisila.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bordoisila.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bordoisila|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bordoisila-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bordoisila:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wind Who Runs Home to Her Mother","text":"कहते हैं कि बोरदोईसिला एक बेटी है — जिसकी शादी बहुत दूर हुई थी, जैसे पुराने ज़माने में बेटियों की हुआ करती थी, अपनी माँ के घर से पूरे साल भर के पहाड़ों और नदियों की दूरी पर। साल भर वह अपने ससुराल के गाँव में काम करती है। साल भर वह इंतज़ार करती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Bordoisila, the telling goes, is a daughter — married far away, the way daughters used to be, a whole year of hills and rivers from her mother's house. All year she works in her husband's village. All year she waits.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bordoisila.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bordoisila|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bordoisila-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bordoisila:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wind Who Runs Home to Her Mother","text":"और जब बोहाग आता है — असमिया साल का पहला महीना, बिहू का महीना — तो उसे अपनी माँ के घर जाने की इजाज़त मिल जाती है। वह चलती नहीं है। वह दौड़ती है। नदियों के ऊपर से, बाँसों के बीच से, उड़ते घाघरे और खुले बिखरे बालों के साथ, रास्ते भर चीज़ों को गिराती हुई और एक भी चीज़ उठाने के लिए बिना रुके।","lang":"hi","body":"And when Bohag comes — the first month of the Assamese year, the month of Bihu — she is allowed to go home to her mother. She does not walk. She runs. Over the rivers, through the bamboo, skirts flying, hair loose, knocking things over the whole way and not stopping to pick up a single one of them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bordoisila.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bordoisila|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bordoisila-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bordoisila:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wind Who Runs Home to Her Mother","text":"\"इसीलिए बिहू से पहले छतों को बाँध दिया जाता है,\" दादी कहती हैं। \"इसलिए नहीं कि हवा नाराज़ है। बल्कि इसलिए कि जिस लड़की ने साल भर से अपनी माँ को न देखा हो, वह तुम्हारी बाड़ के आगे अपनी रफ़्तार धीमी नहीं करती।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"That is why the roofs get tied down before Bihu,\" the grandmother says. \"Not because the wind is angry. Because a girl who has not seen her mother in a year does not slow down for your fence.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bordoisila.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bordoisila|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bordoisila-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bordoisila:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wind Who Runs Home to Her Mother","text":"फिर खुद बिहू के दिन आते हैं, और मौसम शांत हो जाता है — क्योंकि बोरदोईसिला घर पर है, अपनी माँ के पास बैठी हुई, माँ के हाथों से खाती हुई, सारी बातें सुनाती हुई, और पूरा आसमान वैसे ही ठहर जाता है जैसे बेटी के वापस आ जाने पर पूरा घर ठहर जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Then come the Bihu days themselves, and the weather goes gentle — because Bordoisila is home, sitting with her mother, being fed, telling everything, and the whole sky settles the way a house settles when the daughter is back in it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bordoisila.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bordoisila|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bordoisila-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bordoisila:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wind Who Runs Home to Her Mother","text":"लेकिन आना तो कुछ ही दिनों का होता है। त्योहार के बाद उसे लौटना ही पड़ता है — और तब एक दूसरी हवा चलती है, धीमी हवा, जो पाँव घसीटती हुई चलती है और बारिश से भीगी होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"But a visit is a visit. After the festival she has to go back — and there is a second wind then, a slower one, that drags its feet and drips with rain.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bordoisila.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bordoisila|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bordoisila-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bordoisila:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wind Who Runs Home to Her Mother","text":"इसलिए असम में कोई भी वसंत के इस तूफ़ान को नहीं कोसता, या कम से कम ज़्यादा देर तक तो नहीं। वे छतों को बाँधते हैं, चटाई पर सूख रही मिर्चें अंदर ले आते हैं, और कहते हैं: उसे आने दो। पूरा एक साल हो गया है।","lang":"hi","body":"So nobody in Assam curses the spring storm, or not for long. They tie the roof, they bring in the chillies drying on the mat, and they say: let her come. It has been a year.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bordoisila.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bordoisila|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.xorai-elephant-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.xorai-elephant:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Frog, and the Very Big Elephant","text":"\"असम के एक जंगल में, सिमलू यानी सेमल के एक पेड़ पर — वही जिस पर पत्ते आने से पहले लाल फूल खिलते हैं — गौरैया के एक जोड़े ने घोंसला बनाया। उसमें अंडे थे, और दोनों बारी-बारी से अंडों को सेते रहते और एक-दूसरे से कहते कि घोंसले की जगह चुनने में वे कितने समझदार निकले।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In an Assamese forest, in a simolu tree — the silk-cotton, the one that flowers red before it leafs — a pair of sparrows built a nest, and there were eggs in it, and the two of them took turns keeping the eggs warm and telling each other how clever they had been about the location.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-xorai-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.xorai-elephant|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.xorai-elephant-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.xorai-elephant:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Frog, and the Very Big Elephant","text":"\"उसी जंगल में एक ऐसा हाथी घूमता था जिसे कभी किसी ने 'ना' नहीं कहा था। \\\"मैं जहाँ चाहूँ, वहाँ जाता हूँ,\\\" वह ज़्यादातर खुद से ही कहता, क्योंकि उसके साथ कोई चलता ही नहीं था। और उसे बिना ऊपर देखे सिमलू के पेड़ से अपनी पीठ रगड़ना पसंद था — ज़ोर-ज़ोर से।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Through that forest walked an elephant who had never once been told no. \"I go where I like,\" he said, mostly to himself, since nobody walked with him. And he liked to scratch his back on the simolu tree — hard — without looking up.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-xorai-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.xorai-elephant|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.xorai-elephant-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.xorai-elephant:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Frog, and the Very Big Elephant","text":"\"पेड़ हिला, डाली झूली, और अंडों समेत घोंसला नीचे आ गिरा। हाथी ने ध्यान तक नहीं दिया। गौरैया ने बाद में कहा, सबसे बुरी बात यही थी — यह नहीं कि हाथी इतना बड़ा था, बल्कि यह कि उसने ध्यान तक नहीं दिया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The tree shook, the branch swung, and the nest came down, eggs and all. The elephant did not notice. That was the worst part, the sparrow said afterwards — not that he was big, but that he did not even notice.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-xorai-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.xorai-elephant|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.xorai-elephant-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.xorai-elephant:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Frog, and the Very Big Elephant","text":"\"वह खाली डाली पर बैठकर रोने लगी, और उसका रोना सुनकर उसके दोस्त आ पहुँचे: कठफोड़वा, नन्हीं मधुमक्खी और काले तालाब का मेंढक। \\\"रोना ठीक है,\\\" मेंढक बोला। \\\"और रोने वाले के दोस्त भी होते हैं। अब सुनो।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"She sat on the empty branch and cried, and her crying brought her friends: the woodpecker, the little bee, and the frog from the black pool. \"Crying is right,\" said the frog. \"And crying has friends. Now listen.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-xorai-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.xorai-elephant|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.xorai-elephant-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.xorai-elephant:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Frog, and the Very Big Elephant","text":"\"मेंढक की तरकीब में किसी के भी ताक़तवर होने की ज़रूरत नहीं थी। दोपहर में, मधुमक्खी हाथी के कानों के पास अपनी सबसे धीमी और मीठी धुन गुनगुनाने लगी, जब तक कि उसकी आँखें भारी न हो गईं और वह सोचना-समझना न भूल गया। शाम ढले, प्यासा और आधी नींद में, उसने मेंढक को सुना — जो बरसात के गहरे दलदल के बीच से ज़ोर-ज़ोर से, खुशी-खुशी टर्रा रहा था। और यह तो सब जानते ही हैं कि मेंढक वहीं बैठते हैं जहाँ अच्छा पानी होता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The frog's plan needed nobody to be strong. At noon, the bee hummed her softest song round the elephant's ears until his eyes went heavy and he forgot to think. At dusk, thirsty and half-asleep, he heard the frog — croaking, loud and happy, from the middle of the deep monsoon bog. And everyone knows frogs sit by good water.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-xorai-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.xorai-elephant|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.xorai-elephant-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.xorai-elephant:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Frog, and the Very Big Elephant","text":"\"वह बिना देखे टर्र-टर्र की आवाज़ की तरफ़ चल पड़ा — बेशक बिना देखे ही — और दलदल ने उसे कंधों तक खींच लिया और एक मुट्ठी की तरह जकड़ लिया। वह रात भर ज़ोर लगाता रहा पर कहीं न पहुँच सका। यह उसकी ज़िंदगी की पहली रात थी जब वह किसी और की दया पर था, और वह रात बहुत लंबी थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He walked toward the croaking without looking — of course without looking — and the bog took him to the shoulders and held him like a fist. He pulled all night and got nowhere. It was the first night of his life at somebody else's mercy, and it was very long.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-xorai-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.xorai-elephant|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.xorai-elephant-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.xorai-elephant:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Frog, and the Very Big Elephant","text":"भोर होते ही गौरैया उड़कर नीचे आई और उसके कान के पास बैठ गई, किसी पत्ते जैसी छोटी। \"क्या तुम मुझे पहचानते हो?\" उसने सोचा। और फिर, ठंड से कांपते, थके-हारे और कंधों तक कीचड़ में धंसे होने के बावजूद उसे सब याद आ गया — वह पेड़, वह डाली, वह घोंसला जिस पर उसने कभी ध्यान ही नहीं दिया था। \"मुझे माफ़ कर दो,\" उसने कहा, और सचमुच दिल से कहा, जो कि अपने आप में पहली बार हुआ था।","lang":"hi","body":"At dawn the sparrow flew down and sat by his ear, small as a leaf. \"Do you know me?\" He thought about it. And then, cold and tired and shoulder-deep in mud, he did — the tree, the branch, the nest he had not noticed. \"I am sorry,\" he said, and meant it, which was another first.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-xorai-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.xorai-elephant|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.xorai-elephant-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.xorai-elephant:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Frog, and the Very Big Elephant","text":"भैंसों को किनारे की मिट्टी रौंदनी पड़ी, उसके पैरों के नीचे डालियां लगानी पड़ीं, और लगभग आधी सुबह बीत गई। वह कीचड़ से मटमैला होकर बाहर निकला, पर पूरी तरह बदल चुका था। उसके बाद से वह हाथी हमेशा धीरे-धीरे चलता, और किसी पेड़ को छूने से पहले ऊपर की तरफ देखता — और लोग कहते हैं कि यह वही हाथी था, जो अपनी सूंड की नोक से गिरे हुए घोंसले को उठाकर वापस डाली पर रख देता था।","lang":"hi","body":"It took the buffaloes treading the bank down, and branches under his feet, and most of a morning. He came out grey with mud and completely changed. Ever after, that elephant walked slowly, and looked up before he touched a tree — and it was that same elephant, people say, who would lift a fallen nest back onto its branch with the tip of his trunk.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-xorai-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.xorai-elephant|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.burhi-aair-sadhu-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.burhi-aair-sadhu:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grandmother's Stories, Written Down","text":"जितने पुराने समय तक कोई याद कर सके, असम की कहानियां बस एक ही जगह बसती थीं: शाम के वक्त में। एक दिया, एक चटाई, और एक दादी-नानी — यानी एक ‘आई’, जो असमिया में माँ को कहते हैं, और ‘बुढ़ी आई’ यानी बूढ़ी माँ — और उनके चारों तरफ धान की फ़सल की तरह बैठे बच्चे, जो तेजिमोला की, चतुर जानवरों की, और नाम वाली हवाओं की कहानियां सुन रहे होते।","lang":"hi","body":"For as long as anybody can count, the stories of Assam lived in one place: the evening. A lamp, a mat, a grandmother — an aai, which is the Assamese word for mother, and a burhi aai is an old mother — and children arranged around her like a rice harvest, being told about Tejimola, about clever animals, about winds with names.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-burhi-aair-sadhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.burhi-aair-sadhu|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.burhi-aair-sadhu-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.burhi-aair-sadhu:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grandmother's Stories, Written Down","text":"फिर छापेखाने आए, और स्कूल की किताबें आईं, और वे किताबें दूसरों की भाषाओं में थीं। और उनके साथ एक अजीब-सा ख्याल चुपके से दाखिल हो गया: कि किताबों की कहानियां ही असली होती हैं, और दादी-नानी की कहानियां छोटी होती हैं — अच्छी, मगर छोटी। किसी ने यह बात खुलकर नहीं कही। यह ख्याल बस धूल की तरह धीरे-धीरे जम गया।","lang":"hi","body":"Then came printing presses, and schoolbooks, and the schoolbooks were in other people's languages. And a strange idea crept in with them: that stories in books were the real ones, and grandmother stories were small — nice, but small. Nobody said it out loud. It just settled, like dust.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-burhi-aair-sadhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.burhi-aair-sadhu|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.burhi-aair-sadhu-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.burhi-aair-sadhu:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grandmother's Stories, Written Down","text":"उन्हीं शामों के बीच बड़ा हुआ एक लड़का आगे चलकर लेखक बना। उनका नाम था लक्ष्मीनाथ बेजबरुआ, और उन्होंने बहुत-सी चीज़ें लिखीं — मगर वे बार-बार एक ही विचार पर लौट आते थे। कि जब भी असम में किसी बूढ़ी औरत की मौत होती, कहानियों की एक पूरी अलमारी उनके साथ जलकर राख हो जाती, और कोई इन आगों की गिनती भी नहीं कर रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"A boy who had grown up inside those evenings became a writer. His name was Lakshminath Bezbaroa, and he wrote many things — but he kept coming back to one thought. Every time an old woman in Assam died, a shelf of stories burned down with her, and no one was even counting the fires.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-burhi-aair-sadhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.burhi-aair-sadhu|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.burhi-aair-sadhu-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.burhi-aair-sadhu:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grandmother's Stories, Written Down","text":"तो उन्होंने तय किया कि वे दादियों-नानियों की सुनाई कहानियाँ बटोरेंगे और उन्हें एक किताब में दर्ज करेंगे। और तुरंत ही उनके सामने एक चुनाव आ गया, जिस पर सब कुछ टिका हुआ था।","lang":"hi","body":"So he decided to gather the tales the grandmothers told and put them in a book. And straight away there was a choice to make, and everything hung on it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-burhi-aair-sadhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.burhi-aair-sadhu|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.burhi-aair-sadhu-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.burhi-aair-sadhu:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grandmother's Stories, Written Down","text":"उन्होंने किताब का नाम रखा 'बुढ़ी आईर साधु' — यानी बूढ़ी माँ की कहानियाँ। 'साधु' असमिया भाषा में लोककथा को कहते हैं; और 'साधु-कथा' वह होती है जो दिया जलने पर दादी-नानी सुनाती हैं। उन्होंने कहानियों पर अपनी कोई होशियारी नहीं थोपी। उन्होंने बस दरवाज़ा खुला रखा और उन्हें वैसे ही भीतर आने दिया जैसी वे थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"He called the book Burhi Aair Sadhu — the Old Mother's Stories. Sadhu is the Assamese word for a folk tale; a sadhu-kotha is what a grandmother says when the lamp is lit. He did not put his own cleverness on top of the tales. He held the door open and let them walk in as they were.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-burhi-aair-sadhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.burhi-aair-sadhu|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.burhi-aair-sadhu-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.burhi-aair-sadhu:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grandmother's Stories, Written Down","text":"और यह बात काम कर गई। सौ से भी ज़्यादा साल बाद आज भी असम का हर बच्चा तेजिमोला से मिलता है — अगर किस्मत अच्छी हो तो घर पर, और अगर चूल्हे का अलाव दूर हो तो उस किताब में। शामों को बसने के लिए एक दूसरा ठिकाना मिल गया।","lang":"hi","body":"And it worked. A hundred years and more later, every Assamese child still meets Tejimola — at home if they are lucky, in that book if the fireside is far away. The evenings got a second place to live.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-burhi-aair-sadhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.burhi-aair-sadhu|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.burhi-aair-sadhu-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.burhi-aair-sadhu:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grandmother's Stories, Written Down","text":"असम उन्हें एक उपाधि से नवाज़ता है: साहित्यरथी, यानी साहित्य का रथी। लेकिन पूछिए कि उन्होंने असल में क्या किया, तो सच्चा जवाब कहीं छोटा और कहीं ज़्यादा खूबसूरत है। उन्होंने दादियों-नानियों को सुना, और उन्होंने माना कि उनकी कही बातें भी छपी हुई किसी भी किताब जितनी ही सँभाल कर रखने के क़ाबिल हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Assam honours him with a title: Sahityarathi, the charioteer of literature. But ask what he actually did, and the honest answer is smaller and better. He listened to grandmothers, and he thought what they said was worth exactly as much care as anything ever printed.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-burhi-aair-sadhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.burhi-aair-sadhu|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bihu-goru-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bihu-goru:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Cows Go First","text":"अप्रैल के बीच में, जब पहले तूफ़ानों ने दुनिया भर की धूल धो दी होती है, असम अपने नए साल का आगाज़ करता है — बोहाग बिहू, यानी रोंगाली बिहू, जो नाच-गाने से रचा-बसा है। और इसकी सबसे पहली सुबह इंसानों की बिल्कुल नहीं होती।","lang":"hi","body":"In the middle of April, when the first storms have washed the dust off the world, Assam begins its year — Bohag Bihu, the Rongali Bihu, the one made of dancing. And the very first morning of it does not belong to the people at all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bihu-goru.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bihu-goru|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bihu-goru-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bihu-goru:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Cows Go First","text":"आज गोरु बिहू है — यानी मवेशियों का बिहू। किसी के भी नए कपड़े पहनने से पहले, हर एक गाय और बैल को नदी या तालाब पर ले जाया जाता है, और उन्हें साल का सबसे बढ़िया स्नान कराया जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"It is Goru Bihu — the cattle's Bihu. Before anyone puts on anything new, the cows and bullocks are taken down to the river or the pond, every one of them, and given the best bath of their year.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bihu-goru.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bihu-goru|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bihu-goru-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bihu-goru:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Cows Go First","text":"एक दादाजी — यानी कोका — एक छोटे लड़के और एक बड़ी-सी गाय के साथ घुटनों तक पानी में खड़े हैं। \"यहाँ मलो। कानों के पीछे। इसने पूरे साल इस परिवार को संभाला है, तो एक सुबह के लिए तुम्हारे दोनों हाथ इसे मिल ही सकते हैं।\" गाय भी, अपनी तरफ से, इस सब के बीच बड़ी ही शान और गरिमा से खड़ी दिखती है।","lang":"hi","body":"A grandfather — a koka — stands knee-deep with a small boy and a large cow. \"Rub here. Behind the ears. She has carried this family all year, she can have your two arms for one morning.\" The cow, for her part, looks extremely dignified about the whole thing.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bihu-goru.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bihu-goru|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bihu-goru-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bihu-goru:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Cows Go First","text":"उन्हें नहलाया जाता है, हल्दी और काली उड़द की दाल का लेप मला जाता है, और खास पत्तियों की टहनियाँ छुआई जाती हैं — हर परिवार जानता है कि कौन-सी पत्तियाँ — और फिर आता है वह गीत, आधा गाया हुआ और आधा बोला हुआ, जिसे पीढ़ियों से बच्चे इस सुबह गायों के आगे गाते आए हैं: \"लाउ खा, बेंगेना खा, बसरे बसरे बाढ़ी जा।\" लौकी खाओ, बैंगन खाओ, साल-दर-साल बढ़ते जाओ।","lang":"hi","body":"They are washed, and rubbed with a paste of turmeric and black gram, and touched with sprigs of the proper leaves — every family knows which — and then comes the song, half-sung and half-said, that children have shouted at cows on this morning for generations: \"Lau kha, bengena kha, bosore bosore barhi ja.\" Eat gourd, eat brinjal, grow year upon year.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bihu-goru.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bihu-goru|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bihu-goru-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bihu-goru:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Cows Go First","text":"लड़का वही सीधा-सा सवाल पूछता है: यह हमारा नया साल है — तो गायों की बारी सबसे पहले क्यों आती है?","lang":"hi","body":"The boy asks the obvious thing: it is our new year — why do the cows go first?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bihu-goru.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bihu-goru|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bihu-goru-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bihu-goru:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Cows Go First","text":"अगला दिन मानुह बिहू होता है — यानी लोगों का दिन। नए कपड़े, और गमोसा भेंट करना: असम का लाल-सफेद बुना हुआ कपड़ा, जिसे किसी के हाथों या कंधों पर रखा जाता है — मानो सम्मान को हाथों में थाम लिया गया हो। छोटे बड़ों के आगे सिर झुकाते हैं और पूरे साल के लिए उनका आशीर्वाद लेते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The next day is Manuh Bihu — the people's day. New clothes, and the giving of gamosas: the red-and-white woven cloth of Assam, laid over a person's hands or shoulders, which is how respect looks when you can hold it. The young bow to the elders and collect their blessings for the year.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bihu-goru.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bihu-goru|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bihu-goru-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bihu-goru:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Morning the Cows Go First","text":"और फिर गाना-बजाना शुरू होता है और रुकने का नाम ही नहीं लेता — ढोल और पेपा (भैंस के सींग की तुरही) लेकर हुसोरी की मंडलियाँ घर-घर जाती हैं और जिस भी आँगन में कदम रखती हैं, उसे आशीर्वाद देती हैं। खुले में होने वाला वह बिहू नाच ही तो है, जिसके लिए लोग समंदर पार से भी अपने घर खिंचे चले आते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"And then the singing starts and does not really stop — husori parties going house to house with dhol and pepa, the drum and the buffalo-horn pipe, blessing each courtyard they land in. The dancing in the open — the bihu naach — is the thing people cross oceans to be home for.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bihu-goru.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bihu-goru|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ali-aye-ligang-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ali-aye-ligang:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day the Sowing Begins","text":"\"ब्रह्मपुत्र के किनारे मिसिंग लोग रहते हैं—नदी के लोग, जिनके घर खंभों पर टिके होते हैं, जिन्हें चांग घर कहते हैं, और बाढ़ का पानी नीचे से ऐसे गुज़र जाता है मानो कोई मेहमान बरामदे से निकल रहा हो। वे अरुणाचल की पहाड़ियों के तानी लोगों के रिश्तेदार हैं, वही जो पहले इंसान आबो तानी की कहानियाँ सुनाते हैं; मिसिंग लोग बहुत पहले वे गीत नीचे मैदानों में लेकर आए थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Along the Brahmaputra live the Mising people — river people, whose houses stand on stilts, the chang ghar, with the flood water allowed to pass underneath like a guest using the corridor. They are kin to the Tani peoples of the Arunachal hills, the ones who tell of Abo Tani, the first man; the Mising carried those songs down to the plains long ago.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ali-aye-ligang.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ali-aye-ligang|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ali-aye-ligang-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ali-aye-ligang:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day the Sowing Begins","text":"\"और जब बसंत आता है, तो मिसिंग लोग आली-आये-लिगांग मनाते हैं। मिसिंग भाषा के तीन शब्दों में ही पूरे त्योहार का सार है—आली यानी जड़ें और बीज, आये यानी अनाज, और लिगांग यानी बुआई की शुरुआत। वही दिन जब साल भर का काम शुरू होता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And when spring comes, the Mising keep Ali-Aye-Ligang. The name is the whole festival in three words of the Mising tongue: ali, the roots and seed; aye, the grain; ligang, the beginning of the sowing. The day the year's work starts.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ali-aye-ligang.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ali-aye-ligang|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ali-aye-ligang-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ali-aye-ligang:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day the Sowing Begins","text":"\"उसी सुबह, परिवार के कोई बड़े खेत में जाते हैं और आहू धान की पहली चुटकी बोते हैं—बस एक चुटकी, जिसे पूरी बुआई शुरू करने से पहले धन्यवाद कहकर धरती में डाला जाता है। मौसम की पहली मुट्ठी फ़सल बनने से पहले एक तोहफ़ा होती है; यह बात पहाड़ियों ने सबको सिखाई थी, और नदी के लोग इसे कभी नहीं भूले।\"","lang":"hi","body":"On the morning itself, an elder of the family goes to the field and sows the first pinch of ahu rice — just a pinch, put into the earth with a word of thanks before anybody sows in earnest. The first handful of the season is a gift before it is a crop; the hills taught everyone that, and the river people did not forget it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ali-aye-ligang.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ali-aye-ligang|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ali-aye-ligang-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ali-aye-ligang:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day the Sowing Begins","text":"\"फिर ढोल निकल आते हैं, और गुमराग नाचा जाता है—नाचने वालों की कतारें, जिनकी एड़ियों की थाप ज़मीन में उतरती है, खुले आसमान के नीचे गोल-गोल घूमते हुए। पत्तों में लपेटकर चावल पकाए जाते हैं, हर घर में दावत होती है, और पूरा गाँव एक-दूसरे के दरवाज़े आता-जाता रहता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then the drums come out, and the gumrag is danced — lines of dancers, the beat going down through their heels into the ground, round and round in the open air. Rice is cooked wrapped in leaves, there is food in every house, and the whole village is in and out of everybody's door.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ali-aye-ligang.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ali-aye-ligang|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ali-aye-ligang-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ali-aye-ligang:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day the Sowing Begins","text":"\"और उन कुछ दिनों के लिए, कई परिवार अपने औज़ारों को पूरी तरह से रख देते हैं। न हल चलाना, न कटाई, न पेड़ों को काटना। धरती पूरे साल आपके लिए काम करने वाली है; अपने त्योहार पर, वही मुख्य मेहमान होती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And for those few days, many families put the tools down entirely. No ploughing, no cutting, no felling. The earth is about to work for you all year; on her festival, she is the guest of honour.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ali-aye-ligang.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ali-aye-ligang|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ali-aye-ligang-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ali-aye-ligang:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day the Sowing Begins","text":"\"बीज ज़मीन में चला गया। बारिश आएगी ही — ब्रह्मपुत्र पर तो वह हमेशा आती है, कभी-कभी तो कुछ ज़्यादा ही — और बाँस के खंभों वाले घर अपनी ही परछाईं के ऊपर खड़े रहेंगे, और पतझड़ आते-आते बसंत में बोई गई वह चुटकी भर धान पूरी फ़सल बन चुकी होगी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The seed goes in. The rains will come — on the Brahmaputra they always come, sometimes far too well — and the stilt houses will stand over their own reflections, and by autumn the pinch of rice given away in spring will have become the harvest.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ali-aye-ligang.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ali-aye-ligang|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ali-aye-ligang-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ali-aye-ligang:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day the Sowing Begins","text":"\"और जब फ़सल सचमुच घर आ जाती है, तो यह साल अपना घेरा अपने एक दूसरे त्योहार के साथ पूरा करता है — क्योंकि जो लोग बुवाई पर नाचते हैं, वे कटाई को तो यूँ ही चुपचाप बीतने नहीं देंगे। शुरुआत और अंत दोनों को ढोल की थाप मिलती है; बस बीच के दिनों को ही काम से गुज़ारा करना पड़ता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And when the harvest does come in, the year closes the circle with a second festival of its own — because a people who dance the sowing are certainly not going to let the reaping pass quietly. Beginnings and endings both get drums; it is only the middle that has to make do with work.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ali-aye-ligang.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ali-aye-ligang|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bwisagu-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bwisagu:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bwisagu and the Butterfly Dance","text":"\"असम किसी एक ही समाज का नाम नहीं है, और अप्रैल का मध्य यह बात बड़े सुंदर ढंग से साबित करता है। जब असमिया गाँवों में बिहू गाया जा रहा होता है, तब बोडो लोग — ब्रह्मपुत्र के मैदानों के सबसे पुराने समुदायों में से एक, जिनकी अपनी भाषा और अपने करघे हैं — सूरज के ठीक उसी मोड़ पर बैसागु मना रहे होते हैं, जो उनका अपना नया साल है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Assam is not one people, and mid-April proves it beautifully. While Assamese villages are singing Bihu, the Bodo people — one of the oldest communities of the Brahmaputra plains, with their own language and their own looms — are keeping Bwisagu, their own new year, at exactly the same turn of the sun.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bwisagu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bwisagu|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bwisagu-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bwisagu:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bwisagu and the Butterfly Dance","text":"\"और बैसागु की शुरुआत भी मवेशियों से होती है — उन्हें नहलाया जाता है, लाड़-दुलार किया जाता है, शुक्रिया कहा जाता है, और एक दिन के लिए किसी फुर्सत पा चुके बुज़ुर्ग की तरह आज़ाद घूमने को छोड़ दिया जाता है। पूरी घाटी में, घर की बोली चाहे जो भी हो, नया साल मेहनत करने वाले जानवरों के साथ नेकी करके ही शुरू होता है। यह बात ध्यान देने लायक है। एक ही दिशा में समझदारी दिखाने के लिए पड़ोसियों का एक जैसा होना ज़रूरी नहीं है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And Bwisagu also begins with the cattle — washed, fussed over, thanked, set loose to wander like retired elders for a day. Across the whole valley, whatever the language of the house, the new year starts by being kind to the animals who work. That is worth noticing. Neighbours do not need to be the same to be wise in the same direction.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bwisagu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bwisagu|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bwisagu-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bwisagu:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bwisagu and the Butterfly Dance","text":"\"फिर लोगों के अपने दिन आते हैं: नए कपड़े, बड़ों के पाँव छूते छोटों के हाथ, मेल-मुलाक़ातें, पकवान और माफ़ कर देना — पुराने झगड़ों को पुराने साल में ही छोड़ देना होता है, जो कहना आसान है और करना मुश्किल, और इसीलिए तो मदद के लिए यह त्योहार बना है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then the people's days: new clothes, the young touching the feet of the old, visits and food and forgiveness — old quarrels are supposed to be left in the old year, which is easier said than done, which is why there is a festival to help.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bwisagu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bwisagu|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bwisagu-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bwisagu:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bwisagu and the Butterfly Dance","text":"\"और फिर वह संगीत, जिसे जिसने भी सुन लिया वह कभी नहीं भूलता: खाम—यानी लंबा ढोल; सिफुंग—बाँस की बाँसुरी, जिसकी धीमी और गहरी धुन ऐसी लगती है जैसे हवा ने खुद गाने की ठान ली हो; और सेरजा—कमानी से बजने वाला छोटा सा साज़। दोखोना—यानी मौसम जैसी ही सुनहरी और नारंगी रंग की बोडो बुनी पोशाक—पहने लड़कियाँ कतारों में खड़ी हो जाती हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And then the music, which nobody who has heard it forgets: the kham, the long drum; the sifung, the bamboo flute, low and breathy like wind deciding to sing; and the serja, the little bowed fiddle. Girls in the dokhona — the Bodo woven dress, gold and orange like the season itself — form up in lines.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bwisagu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bwisagu|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bwisagu-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bwisagu:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bwisagu and the Butterfly Dance","text":"\"यह बागुरुम्बा नाच है, और लोग इसे तितली-नाच कहते हैं—फैली हुई बाहें, घूमती कलाइयाँ, और पूरी कतार ऐसे झुकती और थिरकती है जैसे कोई तितली तय न कर पा रही हो कि किन दो फूलों में से किस पर बैठे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The dance is the Bagurumba, and people call it the butterfly dance — arms wide, wrists turning, the whole line tilting and settling the way a butterfly does when it cannot decide between two flowers.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bwisagu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bwisagu|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bwisagu-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bwisagu:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bwisagu and the Butterfly Dance","text":"\"बाथौ—यानी बोडो लोगों की अपनी पुरानी आस्था—को मानने वाले परिवारों के आँगनों में सिजौ का पेड़ खड़ा होता है, जिसे घर के लोग ही लगाते और सहेजते हैं, और नया साल उसका भी अभिनंदन करता है। अब दूसरे बोडो परिवार दूसरे धर्मों को भी मानते हैं, और ढोलों को इससे कोई फर्क नहीं पड़ता; बैसागु का मतलब है साल का बदलना, और साल तो हर किसी के लिए बदलता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In the courtyards of families who keep Bathou — the Bodo's own old faith — stands the sijou tree, planted and tended by the house, and the new year greets it too. Other Bodo families keep other faiths now, and the drums do not mind; Bwisagu is the year turning, and the year turns for everyone.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bwisagu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bwisagu|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bwisagu-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bwisagu:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bwisagu and the Butterfly Dance","text":"\"शाम होते-होते नाचने वालों की कतारें गोल घेरों में बदल जाती हैं, और सिफुंग एक बजाने वाले से दूसरे के हाथ में थमा दी जाती है ताकि किसी के थकने जैसी छोटी सी बात के लिए धुन कभी रुके नहीं। नए साल का स्वागत तब तक होना चाहिए जब तक स्वागत करने वालों के पैर डगमगाने न लगें; इस बात पर बोडो गाँव और दुनिया का हर दूसरा गाँव पूरी तरह सहमत है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"By evening the lines of dancers have joined into rings, and the sifung is handed from player to player so the tune never has to stop for anything as small as a person getting tired. A new year should be welcomed until the welcomers wobble; on this the Bodo villages and every other village on earth agree.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bwisagu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bwisagu|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sohpetbneng-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sohpetbneng:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Navel of the Sky","text":"\"मेघालय की खासी पहाड़ियों में एक पहाड़ी है जिसे 'उ लुम सोहपेतब्नेन्ग' कहते हैं। इस नाम के एक-एक टुकड़े को वैसे ही समझिए जैसे कोई खासी नानी या दादी समझाएँगी: लुम यानी पहाड़ी, सोहपेत यानी नाभि, ब्नेन्ग यानी आसमान। वह पहाड़ी जो स्वर्ग की नाभि है—वह जगह जहाँ कभी आसमान और धरती आपस में जुड़े हुए थे, बिल्कुल वैसे जैसे कोई नन्हा बच्चा अपनी माँ से जुड़ा होता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In the Khasi hills of Meghalaya there is a hill called U Lum Sohpetbneng. Take the name apart the way a Khasi grandmother would: lum is hill, sohpet is navel, bneng is the sky. The hill that is the navel of heaven — the place where the sky and the earth were once joined, like a baby to its mother.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sohpetbneng.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sohpetbneng|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sohpetbneng-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sohpetbneng:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Navel of the Sky","text":"कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि शुरुआत में, ऊपर आसमान के देश में सोलह परिवार रहते थे। और लुम सोहपेटब्नेन्ग की चोटी से एक सोने की सीढ़ी ऊपर जाती थी — कुछ कहानियों में एक बहुत बड़ा पेड़ — और वे सोलह परिवार उस पर इतनी आसानी से आते-जाते थे, जैसे तुम रसोई और बरामदे के बीच आते-जाते हो।","lang":"hi","body":"In the beginning, the telling goes, sixteen families lived above, in the sky country. And from the top of Lum Sohpetbneng rose a golden ladder — some tellings say a great tree — and the sixteen families went up and down it as freely as you go between the kitchen and the veranda.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sohpetbneng.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sohpetbneng|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sohpetbneng-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sohpetbneng:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Navel of the Sky","text":"यहाँ नीचे वह बगीचा था: नदियों का ध्यान रखना, जंगलों की रखवाली, ढलानों पर झूमती घास, और धरती की सारी हरी-भरी देखभाल। वे परिवार सुबह-सुबह इसकी देखभाल करने नीचे आते और रात को वापस आसमान में अपने घर चले जाते। धरती दिन का काम थी। स्वर्ग रात का खाना था।","lang":"hi","body":"Down here was the garden: rivers to mind, forests to keep, broom-grass bending on the slopes, and the whole green work of the earth. The families would come down in the morning to tend it and climb home to the sky at night. Earth was the day's work. Heaven was supper.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sohpetbneng.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sohpetbneng|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sohpetbneng-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sohpetbneng:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Navel of the Sky","text":"लेकिन जिस बगीचे में सिर्फ़ आने-जाने वाले आते हों, उसे कभी पूरा प्यार नहीं मिल पाता। और फिर वह दिन आया जब यह तय होना था: धरती को सच में कौन अपनाएगा — इस पर रहेगा, इसका होकर रहेगा, और इसे हमेशा के लिए सँभालेगा?","lang":"hi","body":"But a garden tended by visitors is never quite loved. And the day came when it had to be settled: who would truly take the earth — live on it, belong to it, keep it always?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sohpetbneng.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sohpetbneng|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sohpetbneng-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sohpetbneng:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Navel of the Sky","text":"सात परिवार यहीं बसने के लिए नीचे उतर आए। खासी लोग उन्हें 'हिन्यु त्रेप' — यानी सात झोपड़ियों — के रूप में याद करते हैं, और जब कोई खासी बुज़ुर्ग कहते हैं, \"हम सात झोपड़ियों की संतान हैं,\" तो उनका मतलब इसी सुबह से होता है। नौ परिवार ऊपर ही रहे। सात परिवारों ने धरती को धरोहर की तरह संभाल लिया।","lang":"hi","body":"Seven families came down to stay. The Khasi remember them as the Hynñiew Trep — the Seven Huts — and when a Khasi elder says \"we are the children of the Seven Huts,\" this is the morning they mean. Nine families stayed above. Seven took the earth in trust.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sohpetbneng.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sohpetbneng|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sohpetbneng-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sohpetbneng:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Navel of the Sky","text":"और फिर वह सीढ़ी खो गई। यह कैसे हुआ, इस बारे में कहानियाँ अलग-अलग हैं, और बुज़ुर्ग आपको अपने ढंग से और अपनी फ़ुरसत में यह बात बताएंगे। पर हर कहानी जिस बात पर सहमत है, वह है इसका मतलब: धरती और स्वर्ग के बीच का आसान रास्ता बंद हो गया, और उन सात परिवारों ने अपने हाथों से धरती को सँभाला और अपनी यादों में आसमान को बसाए रखा।","lang":"hi","body":"And then the ladder was lost. The tellings differ about how, and elders will tell you in their own way and their own time. What every telling agrees on is what it meant: the easy road between earth and heaven closed, and the seven families kept the earth with their hands and the sky with their memory.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sohpetbneng.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sohpetbneng|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sohpetbneng-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sohpetbneng:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Navel of the Sky","text":"फिर भी, वह पहाड़ी उनसे दूर नहीं हुई। हर साल, जब ठंड ढलने लगती है, लोग साथ मिलकर लुम सोहपेटब्नेन्ग पर चढ़ते हैं — चीड़ के पेड़ों के बीच से होते हुए चोटी तक, ठीक वहीं खड़े होने जहाँ कभी सीढ़ी हुआ करती थी। धरती को छोड़ने के लिए नहीं। बल्कि यह याद रखने के लिए कि वे बहुत ऊँचाई से आए थे, और धरती उनके लिए कोई निर्वासन नहीं, बल्कि उनकी अपनी पसंद थी।","lang":"hi","body":"They did not lose the hill, though. Every year, when winter loosens, people climb Lum Sohpetbneng together — up through the pines to the top, to stand where the ladder stood. Not to leave the earth. To remember that they came from higher up, and that the earth was not an exile but a choosing.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sohpetbneng.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sohpetbneng|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.diengiei-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.diengiei:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree That Shaded the Whole World","text":"\"खासी कथा कहती है कि जब सातों परिवारों ने धरती पर बसेरा कर लिया, तब पश्चिम में एक पेड़ उगने लगा। उसे उ दिएंगिएई कहते थे। वह बढ़ता ही रहा। उसकी टहनियाँ फैलती ही गईं जब तक कि उसकी छाया पूरी दुनिया पर नहीं छा गई, और उस साए तले रोशनी ऐसे बुझने लगी जैसे दिए का तेल खत्म हो रहा हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"After the seven families had settled the earth, the Khasi telling says, a tree began to grow in the west. U Diengiei, it was called. It did not stop growing. Its crown spread and spread until its shadow lay over the whole world, and under that shadow the light died away like a lamp running out.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-diengiei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.diengiei|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.diengiei-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.diengiei:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree That Shaded the Whole World","text":"\"अँधेरे में धान पक ही नहीं रहा था। बच्चे कुकुरमुत्तों जैसे पीले पड़ने लगे। वह कोई गुस्से वाला पेड़ नहीं था — वह तो बस एक पेड़ था, जो बहुत ही विशाल था — मगर उसके नीचे की दुनिया धीरे-धीरे बुझती जा रही थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The rice would not ripen in the dark. The children went pale as mushrooms. It was not an angry tree — it was just a tree, being enormous — but the world underneath it was slowly going out.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-diengiei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.diengiei|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.diengiei-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.diengiei:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree That Shaded the Whole World","text":"\"तो लोगों ने सलाह-मशविरा किया, उसी तरह जैसे खासी लोग करते हैं — सबने सबकी सुनी, कोई चिल्लाया नहीं — और सब मान गए: दिएंगिएई को गिराना ही होगा। वे अपनी कुल्हाड़ियाँ लेकर पश्चिम की ओर गए, और सुबह से शाम तक उसे काटते रहे। रात होने तक घाव गहरा हो चुका था और वे थके-हारे मगर संतुष्ट होकर घर लौटे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"So the people took counsel, the way Khasis take counsel — everybody heard, nobody shouted — and it was agreed: Diengiei must come down. They took their axes to the west, and they cut from morning to dusk, and by nightfall the cut was deep and they went home sore and satisfied.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-diengiei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.diengiei|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.diengiei-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.diengiei:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree That Shaded the Whole World","text":"\"सुबह जब वे लौटे, तो पेड़ की छाल बिल्कुल चिकनी थी। कोई कट नहीं। एक निशान तक नहीं। उन्होंने फिर पूरे दिन कुल्हाड़ी चलाई — और अगली सुबह वह घाव फिर भर गया। दिन पर दिन यही चलता रहा। कुल्हाड़ियाँ तो झूठ नहीं बोलतीं, और पेड़ रातों-रात खुद-ब-खुद ठीक नहीं हो जाते।\"","lang":"hi","body":"At dawn they came back to smooth bark. No cut. Not a mark. They cut again all day — and again the morning healed it. Day after day. Axes do not lie, and trees do not mend themselves overnight.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-diengiei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.diengiei|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.diengiei-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.diengiei:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree That Shaded the Whole World","text":"\"एक छोटी सी चिड़िया — जंगल की सबसे छोटी चिड़ियों में से एक, ऐसी जिससे कोई कुछ नहीं पूछता — फुदकती हुई आगे आई और बोली: \\\"तुम्हें पता है, मैं रात का हाल देखती हूँ। तुम्हारे जाते ही बाघ उ ख्ला आता है। उसे यह घना अँधेरा बहुत भाता है, क्योंकि इस साए के नीचे का पूरा जंगल उसी का है। और वह अपनी खुरदरी जीभ से उस घाव को तब तक चाटता है जब तक कि वह भर न जाए।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"A little bird — one of the smallest in the forest, the kind nobody asks — hopped up and said: \"I see the nights, you know. U Khla the tiger comes when you leave. He loves the great darkness, for the forest under this shadow is all his. And he licks the cut with his rough tongue until it closes.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-diengiei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.diengiei|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.diengiei-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.diengiei:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree That Shaded the Whole World","text":"चिड़िया बोली, \"तो फिर ऐसा करो। आज रात, जब तुम काम रोको, तो अपनी कुल्हाड़ियाँ घर मत ले जाना। उन्हें चीरे में ही सीधा खड़ा छोड़ देना — धार बाहर की तरफ़ करके।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"So do this,\" said the bird. \"Tonight, when you stop, do not carry your blades home. Leave them standing in the cut — edges outward.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-diengiei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.diengiei|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.diengiei-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.diengiei:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree That Shaded the Whole World","text":"उस रात बाघ हमेशा की तरह पेड़ का घाव भरने के लिए अंधेरे में दबे पाँव आया — और कटी हुई मुलायम लकड़ी की जगह उसकी जीभ ठंडी, तेज़ धार से टकराई। अपनी मूँछों पर चोट खाए वह झटके से पीछे हटा, तय किया कि यह पेड़ अपनी देखभाल खुद कर सकता है, और अपनी खूबसूरत, गुस्सैल पूँछ फटकारता हुआ कहीं और चला गया।","lang":"hi","body":"That night the tiger came padding through the dark to mend the wound as usual — and his tongue met cold, sharp edges instead of soft cut wood. He pulled back with his whiskers offended, decided this tree could look after itself, and took his beautiful angry tail elsewhere.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-diengiei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.diengiei|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.diengiei-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.diengiei:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree That Shaded the Whole World","text":"अगले दिन की कटाई पुराने घाव के गहरे अंदर तक उतर गई, और उसके अगले दिन डिएंगिए ऐसे गिरा जैसे कोई पहाड़ी ही उलट कर लेट गई हो। और रोशनी लौट आई — धान के खेतों पर, नदियों पर, हर चीज़ पर, जैसे पूरी दुनिया ने अपनी रोकी हुई साँस एक साथ छोड़ दी हो।","lang":"hi","body":"The next day's cutting went deep into old work, and the day after that Diengiei came down like a hillside lying over. And the light came back — over the paddy, over the rivers, over everything, the whole held breath of the world let out at once.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-diengiei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.diengiei|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.klew-peacock-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.klew-peacock:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Peacock's Tail Is Full of Eyes","text":"खासी कहानियों में, सूरज 'का स्नगी' हैं — 'का' इसलिए, क्योंकि वह स्त्री हैं; खासी भाषा में हर नाम के आगे पुरुष के लिए 'उ' या स्त्री के लिए 'का' लगता है, ताकि आपको हमेशा पता रहे कि बात किसकी हो रही है। और बहुत पुराने ज़माने में, उ क्लेव नाम का मोर ऊपर आसमान के देश में रहता था, और सूरज की अपनी बेटी उससे प्यार करती थी, और वह वहाँ खुश था। ज़्यादातर।","lang":"hi","body":"In the Khasi telling, the sun is Ka Sngi — Ka, because she is a she; in Khasi, every name carries a U for a he or a Ka for a she, so you always know who you are talking about. And in the long-ago, U Klew the peacock lived up in the sky country, and the sun's own daughter loved him, and he was happy there. Mostly.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-klew-peacock.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.klew-peacock|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.klew-peacock-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.klew-peacock:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Peacock's Tail Is Full of Eyes","text":"आसमान में रहने की सबसे बड़ी परेशानी वहाँ का नज़ारा है। बहुत नीचे, उ क्लेव को धरती दिखाई देती थी — गिरे हुए आईनों की तरह चमकते पानी से भरे धान के खेत, तालाब और हरियाली। और उस तक एक फुसफुसाहट पहुँची, जिस तरह बेचैन दिलों तक फुसफुसाहटें पहुँचती हैं, कि नीचे की ज़िंदगी ऊपर की किसी भी चीज़ से कहीं ज़्यादा शानदार है।","lang":"hi","body":"The trouble with living in the sky is the view. Far below, U Klew could see the earth — the flooded paddy fields flashing like dropped mirrors, the ponds, the green. And a whisper reached him, the way whispers reach the restless, that life down there was finer than anything above.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-klew-peacock.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.klew-peacock|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.klew-peacock-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.klew-peacock:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Peacock's Tail Is Full of Eyes","text":"\"बस एक नज़र,\" उसने सूरज की बेटी से कहा। \"बस एक नज़र देख लूँ और मैं सीधे घर लौट आऊँगा।\" उसने कोई बहस नहीं की। जो लोग आपसे प्यार करते हैं, वे आपकी 'बस एक नज़र' वाली बात पर भला कहाँ बहस करते हैं। वह आसमान के छोर पर खड़ी रही और उसे किसी गिरे हुए रत्न की तरह नीचे जाते देखती रही।","lang":"hi","body":"\"One look,\" he told the sun's daughter. \"One look and I will come straight home.\" She did not argue. People who love you rarely argue with your one looks. She stood at the edge of the sky and watched him go down like a dropped jewel.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-klew-peacock.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.klew-peacock|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.klew-peacock-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.klew-peacock:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Peacock's Tail Is Full of Eyes","text":"और धरती बेहद प्यारी थी — यही तो इसका फंदा था। धान के खेत गुनगुने थे, दाना आसानी से मिल जाता था, और हर शांत तालाब में एक सुंदर मोर साफ़ तौर पर उसकी तारीफ़ करता हुआ ऊपर देख रहा था। वह एक दिन रुका। फिर एक मौसम। फिर उसने दिन गिनना ही छोड़ दिया, क्योंकि गिनना अब किसी इल्ज़ाम की तरह लगने लगा था।","lang":"hi","body":"And the earth was lovely — that is the trap of it. The paddy was warm, the grain was easy, and in every still pond there was a handsome peacock looking up at him with obvious admiration. He stayed a day. Then a season. Then he stopped counting, because counting had begun to feel like an accusation.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-klew-peacock.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.klew-peacock|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.klew-peacock-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.klew-peacock:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Peacock's Tail Is Full of Eyes","text":"ऊपर, सूरज की बेटी हर सुबह हवा के रास्ते पर आँखें गड़ाए रहती। वह नहीं आया। लौटने के लिए बहुत दूर निकल जाना, और देर से बेहाल होकर घर लौटते हुए देखे जाने का घमंड — यह एक ऐसी गाँठ है जो कई दिलों ने बाँधी है, और मोर का दिल भी कोई अलग नहीं है।","lang":"hi","body":"Up above, the sun's daughter watched the road of air every dawn. He did not come. Too far gone to return, too proud to be seen climbing home shabby and late — that is a knot many hearts have tied, and a peacock's heart is no different.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-klew-peacock.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.klew-peacock|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.klew-peacock-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.klew-peacock:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Peacock's Tail Is Full of Eyes","text":"तो उसने वही किया जिसके लिए यह कहानी याद की जाती है। वह उसे वापस ला नहीं सकती थी। वह उसे डाँटना भी नहीं चाहती थी। उसके पास बस एक ही चीज़ थी जो अब भी इतनी नीचे तक पहुँच सकती थी — उसकी रोशनी।","lang":"hi","body":"So she did the thing this story is remembered for. She could not fetch him. She would not scold him. She had one thing that could still reach all the way down — her light.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-klew-peacock.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.klew-peacock|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.klew-peacock-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.klew-peacock:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Peacock's Tail Is Full of Eyes","text":"सुबह की धूप के साथ वह नीचे उतरी, और जहाँ-जहाँ वह उसकी पूँछ के लंबे पंखों पर पड़ी, वहीं टिककर रह गई: सुनहरे, हरे और नीले रंग के सौ छोटे गोल निशान। लोग उन्हें आँखें कहते हैं। आसमान के प्यार की सौ नन्ही तस्वीरें, जो उसके साथ ऐसे जड़ दी गईं कि वह उन्हें कभी खो नहीं सकता था और कभी पूरी तरह देख भी नहीं सकता था।","lang":"hi","body":"Down through the morning it came, and where it fell on his trailing tail feathers it settled and stayed: a hundred small round marks of gold and green and blue. Eyes, people call them. A hundred little pictures of the sky's love, pinned to him where he could never lose them and never quite see them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-klew-peacock.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.klew-peacock|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.klew-peacock-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.klew-peacock:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Peacock's Tail Is Full of Eyes","text":"और खासी बुज़ुर्ग कहते हैं कि यही वजह है कि मोर भोर के वक्त ऐसा करता है। वह पूरब की ओर मुड़ता है, जहाँ से सूरज निकलता है, और अपने पंखों का पूरा घेरा फैलाकर थरथराते हुए थामे रखता है — हर सुबह उसे यह दिखाते हुए, कि उसने वे निशान अब भी पहन रखे हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"And that, the Khasi elders say, is why the peacock does what he does at dawn. He turns to the east, where the sun comes up, and spreads the whole fan wide and holds it trembling — showing her, every single morning, that he still wears them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-klew-peacock.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.klew-peacock|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ksew-market-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ksew-market:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Dog Sniffs Everybody","text":"कहते हैं, बहुत पुरानी बात है, खासी की पहाड़ियों में जानवरों ने एक बड़ा 'ईव' लगाया — यानी बाज़ार, क्योंकि बाज़ार के दिन ही इन पहाड़ियों की धड़कन होते हैं — और हर जानवर ने अपनी दुकान लगाई। हिरण ने हरी सब्ज़ियाँ बेचीं। बंदर ने फल बेचे। हर किसी ने कुछ न कुछ बेचा, और हर कोई वहाँ आया।","lang":"hi","body":"Long ago in the Khasi hills, the telling goes, the animals held a great iew — a market, for market days are the heartbeat of these hills — and every animal kept a stall. The deer sold greens. The monkey sold fruit. Everyone sold something, and everyone came.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ksew-market.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ksew-market|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ksew-market-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ksew-market:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Dog Sniffs Everybody","text":"उ क्स्यू कुत्ता भी आया, वही एक चीज़ लेकर जो उसने खुद बनाई थी: खमीरे अचार का एक मर्तबान, गाढ़ा और तीखा — ऐसी महक जिससे या तो आप दिल से प्यार करने लगें, या फिर अपनी पूरी जान लगाकर भाग खड़े हों। उसने कतार के आखिर में उसे बड़े गर्व से रख दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"U Ksew the dog came too, with the one thing he had made himself: a jar of fermented pickle, dark and strong — the sort of smell you either love with your whole heart or run from with your whole legs. He set it down proudly at the end of the row.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ksew-market.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ksew-market|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ksew-market-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ksew-market:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Dog Sniffs Everybody","text":"बड़े जानवर कतार से गुज़रते हुए उसकी दुकान तक पहुँचे और मुँह बनाने लगे। \"यह क्या है?\" हँसी तब अच्छी लगती है जब वह आपके साथ हो। यह उस तरह की हँसी नहीं थी। और धक्का-मुक्की व खिल्ली उड़ाने के बीच, किसी ने मर्तबान को लात मार दी, वह पत्थरों पर गिरकर फूट गया, और पूरा बाज़ार और भी ज़ोर से हँस पड़ा।","lang":"hi","body":"The big animals came down the row and reached his stall and made faces. \"What is THAT?\" Laughter is fine when it is with you. This was the other kind. And in the jostling and the mocking, somebody kicked the jar over, and it broke on the stones, and the whole market laughed harder.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ksew-market.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ksew-market|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ksew-market-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ksew-market:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Dog Sniffs Everybody","text":"कुत्ता इंसाफ़ माँगने बाज़ार के बुज़ुर्गों के पास गया। उन्होंने कंधे उचका दिए। \"बस कुत्ते का ही तो मर्तबान है।\" बस। इस एक शब्द ने उस लात से भी ज़्यादा चोट पहुँचाई।","lang":"hi","body":"The dog went to the elders of the market for justice. They shrugged. \"It is only the dog's jar.\" Only. That word did more damage than the kick had.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ksew-market.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ksew-market|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ksew-market-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ksew-market:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Dog Sniffs Everybody","text":"वह अँधेरा होने तक चलता रहा और इंसानों की बस्ती में आ पहुँचा, और सहमे कानों के साथ अलाव की रोशनी के किनारे खड़ा हो गया। एक आदमी ने अपने खाने से सिर उठाया, उसे ठीक से देखा — दिन भर में वही पहला जीव था जिसने उसे सचमुच देखा था — और थोड़ा खिसक कर जगह बनाई। \"बैठो। काफ़ी है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He walked until dark and came to the houses of people, and stood at the edge of the firelight with his ears uncertain. A man looked up from his supper, looked at him properly — the first creature all day to look at him properly — and moved over. \"Sit. There is enough.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ksew-market.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ksew-market|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ksew-market-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ksew-market:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Dog Sniffs Everybody","text":"और बस, हमेशा-हमेशा के लिए यही तय हो गया। कुत्ता वहीं रह गया। उसे चूल्हे की गरमाहट मिली, बचा-खुचा खाना मिला, रखवाली के लिए बच्चे मिले, और मिला एक नाम, जो खेत के उस पार से प्यार से पुकारा जाता। जानवरों का बाज़ार तो बचा रहा, पर उन्होंने वह सबसे वफ़ादार दिल खो दिया जो कभी वहाँ खड़ा हुआ था।","lang":"hi","body":"And that was that, for all time. The dog stayed. He got the fireside, the leftovers, the children to guard, a name called warmly across a field. The animals kept their market, and lost the most loyal heart that had ever stood in it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ksew-market.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ksew-market|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ksew-market-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ksew-market:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Dog Sniffs Everybody","text":"मगर कहानी का वह अंत, जिसका इंतज़ार खासी बच्चे करते हैं, वह यह है। जब मर्तबान टूटा, तो अचार छलक पड़ा — हँसने के लिए भीड़ लगाकर खड़े हर जानवर के पैरों पर। और गंध न तो झूठ बोलती है और न ही मिटती है, कम से कम उसकी जैसी नाक के लिए तो बिल्कुल नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"But here is the ending Khasi children wait for. When the jar broke, the pickle splashed — onto the feet of every animal who had crowded in to laugh. And smells do not lie and do not fade, not to a nose like his.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ksew-market.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ksew-market|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.root-bridges-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.root-bridges:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bridge That Is Alive","text":"सोहरा के आस-पास मेघालय की दक्षिणी ढलानें, धरती पर इंसानों के बसने वाली सबसे ज़्यादा बारिश वाली जगह हैं। वहाँ वैसी बारिश नहीं होती जैसी वहाँ होती है जहाँ तुम रहते हो। नदियाँ ऐसे उफ़नती हैं जैसे कोई जाग उठा हो, और वे किसी पुल को ऐसे बहा ले जा सकती हैं जैसे तुम कोई बिस्कुट उठा लेते हो।","lang":"hi","body":"The southern slopes of Meghalaya, around Sohra, are the rainiest inhabited place on earth. It does not rain there the way it rains where you live. The rivers rise like something waking up, and they can take a bridge the way you take a biscuit.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-root-bridges.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.root-bridges|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.root-bridges-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.root-bridges:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bridge That Is Alive","text":"जो कि एक बड़ी समस्या है, क्योंकि वार खासी और वार जयंतिया लोगों के गाँव उन गहरी घाटियों में बसे हैं, जहाँ बच्चे नदी पार करके स्कूल जाते हैं और किसान नदी पार करके बाज़ार। बाँस बह जाता है। लकड़ी एक ही मौसम में सड़ जाती है। लोहा जंग लगकर खुद ही खत्म हो जाता है। जिससे भी पुल बनाया जा सकता है, यह मौसम उस हर चीज़ को नष्ट कर देता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Which is a problem, because the villages of the War Khasi and War Jaintia people sit deep in those gorges, and children cross rivers to school and farmers cross rivers to market. Bamboo washes away. Timber rots in a season. Iron rusts and eats itself. Everything you can build a bridge from, this weather destroys.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-root-bridges.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.root-bridges|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.root-bridges-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.root-bridges:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bridge That Is Alive","text":"हर उस चीज़ को जिससे कुछ बनाया जा सके। इसलिए वे पुल बनाने के बजाय उन्हें उगाते हैं। नदी किनारे रबर-अंजीर का एक पेड़ लगाया जाता है — एक ऐसा पेड़ जो अपनी डालियों से लंबी, सब्र भरी जड़ें नीचे उतारता है। और गाँव उन जड़ों को सिखाने-सँवारने लगता है: सुपारी के खोखले तनों से सहेजकर निकाली जाती हैं, हर साल नदी के पार थोड़ी और आगे बढ़ाई जाती हैं, बाँधी जाती हैं, बुनी जाती हैं, और आपस में एक-दूसरे में लपेटी जाती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Everything you can build from. So they grow them instead. A rubber-fig tree is planted by the bank — a tree that throws down long, patient roots from its branches. And the village begins to train those roots: coaxed through hollowed-out betel palm trunks, guided across the river a little further each year, tied, woven, wound back into each other.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-root-bridges.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.root-bridges|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.root-bridges-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.root-bridges:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bridge That Is Alive","text":"वे इसे जिंगकिएंग ज्री कहते हैं — यानी जड़ों से बना एक ज़िंदा पुल। और इसके लिए क्या कीमत चुकानी पड़ती है: पंद्रह साल, बीस साल, कभी-कभी उससे भी ज़्यादा, तब जाकर जड़ें इतनी मोटी होती हैं कि किसी इंसान का बोझ संभाल सकें। जो यह पेड़ लगाता है, हो सकता है वह कभी इस पुल से होकर न गुज़रे।","lang":"hi","body":"They call it a jingkieng jri — a living root bridge. And here is the price of it: fifteen years, twenty, sometimes more, before the roots are thick enough to carry a person. The one who plants the tree may never cross on it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-root-bridges.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.root-bridges|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.root-bridges-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.root-bridges:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bridge That Is Alive","text":"एक दादी एक बच्चे के साथ खड़ी हैं, और एक नई जड़ को पुल के ताने-बाने में लपेट रही हैं। \"तो फिर यह किसका पुल है?\" बच्चा पूछता है। \"तुम्हारा,\" वे कहती हैं। \"और तुम इसे किसी ऐसे इंसान के लिए सँवार रहे हो जो अभी पैदा भी नहीं हुआ है। इसमें कुछ भी अजीब नहीं है। अगर सच में समझा जाए, तो पुल का असली मतलब यही होता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A grandmother stands with a child, winding a young root onto the weave. \"Whose bridge is this, then?\" the child asks. \"Yours,\" she says. \"And you are working on it for someone who is not born yet. That is not strange. That is just what a bridge is, taken seriously.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-root-bridges.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.root-bridges|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.root-bridges-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.root-bridges:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bridge That Is Alive","text":"और एक बार जब यह बोझ सँभालने लायक हो जाता है, तो फिर कभी नहीं रुकता। जड़ों का पुल हर साल और मज़बूत होता जाता है — जिस भी बाढ़ का यह सामना करता है, इसकी पकड़ उतनी ही मज़बूत होती जाती है; हर मौसम के साथ यह और मोटा होता जाता है। उन घाटियों में नीचे ऐसे पुल हैं जो अनगिनत पीढ़ियों से लोगों का भार उठाते आ रहे हैं, और आज भी बढ़ रहे हैं। नोंगरियात में एक मशहूर दो मंजिला पुल है, एक के ऊपर एक, जैसे किसी घर ने पुल बनने की ठान ली हो।","lang":"hi","body":"And once it carries, it never stops. A root bridge gets stronger every year — every flood it survives, it grips harder; every season, it thickens. There are bridges down in those gorges that have carried people for generations beyond counting, still growing. At Nongriat there is a famous one with two decks, one above the other, like a house that decided to be a bridge.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-root-bridges.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.root-bridges|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.root-bridges-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.root-bridges:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bridge That Is Alive","text":"जड़ों से बने किसी पुल पर इंजीनियर का नाम नहीं होता। उस पर पूरे गाँव की कई पीढ़ियों की छाप होती है — हर पीढ़ी नई जड़ों को बाँधती है, छाँटती है, मरम्मत करती है और आगे सौंप देती है। यह दुनिया की सबसे धैर्य से रची जाने वाली वास्तुकला है, और आज भी, बारिश में इसे वे लोग गढ़ रहे हैं जो बखूबी जानते हैं कि अच्छी चीज़ों के बनने में कितना वक्त लगता है।","lang":"hi","body":"No engineer signs a root bridge. A village does, over lifetimes — each generation tying in new roots, trimming, mending, handing it on. It is the patientest architecture on earth, and it is being practised right now, in the rain, by people who know exactly how long good things take.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-root-bridges.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.root-bridges|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wangala-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wangala:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Hundred Drums Say Thank You","text":"मेघालय का पश्चिमी हिस्सा गारो लोगों का है — जो खुद को आचिक कहते हैं, यानी पहाड़ों के लोग। उनके पहाड़ सही मायने में उनकी माताओं के हैं: एक गारो बच्चे को अपनी माँ का वंश-नाम मिलता है, और परिवार का सिलसिला माँ से बेटी की ओर बढ़ता है, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे पूर्व में खासी लोगों के यहाँ होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The western half of Meghalaya belongs to the Garo people — who call themselves A·chik, the people of the hills. Their hills are their mothers' in the plainest sense: a Garo child takes the mother's clan, and the family line runs from mother to daughter, as it does among the Khasi to the east.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wangala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wangala|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wangala-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wangala:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Hundred Drums Say Thank You","text":"साल भर पहाड़ी खेतों में मेहनत की जाती है, और पतझड़ खत्म होते-होते आखिरकार फ़सल घर आ जाती है — टोकरियों में अनाज भर जाता है, और तंगी के महीनों को एक बार फिर मात मिल जाती है। और अब एक ऐसा नियम आता है जो खुद खेतों जितना ही पुराना है: नई फ़सल में से कोई भी तब तक खुलकर नहीं खाता, जब तक उसे देने वाले का धन्यवाद न कर दिया जाए।","lang":"hi","body":"All year the hill fields are worked, and by late autumn the harvest is finally in — grain in the baskets, the lean months beaten one more time. And now comes a rule as old as the fields: nobody eats freely of the new crop until thanks have been given to the one who gave it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wangala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wangala|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wangala-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wangala:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Hundred Drums Say Thank You","text":"यह धन्यवाद मिसी सालजोंग के लिए होता है, वे महान दाता, जो मौसम और बीज देते हैं। गाँव के मुखिया — यानी नोकमा — अपने घर में पहली भेंट चढ़वाते हैं: पहले फल, पहला अनाज, खुद कुछ भी लेने से पहले उन्हें वापस लौटाना। यह क्रम बहुत मायने रखता है। पहले भेंट, फिर दावत। उल्टा कभी नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"The thanks go to Misi Saljong, the great giver, who lends the seasons and the seed. The headman — the nokma — sees the first offerings made in his house: first fruits, first grain, given back before anything is taken. The order matters. Gift, then feast. Never the other way.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wangala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wangala|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wangala-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wangala:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Hundred Drums Say Thank You","text":"और फिर वांगला शुरू होता है, और वांगला कोई शांत त्योहार नहीं है। लोग इसे सौ ढोलों का त्योहार कहते हैं, और वे कोई बढ़ा-चढ़ाकर नहीं कह रहे — दामा, यानी लंबे अंडाकार ढोल, दर्जनों और सैकड़ों की तादाद में बाहर निकल आते हैं, और पुरुष कतारों में खड़े होकर ढोल बजाते हैं, और आवाज़ पहाड़ियों से टकराकर ऐसे गूँजती है मानो पहाड़ खुद जवाब दे रहे हों।","lang":"hi","body":"And then Wangala begins, and Wangala is not quiet. They call it the festival of a hundred drums, and they are not exaggerating — the dama, the long oval drums, come out by the dozen and the dozen dozen, and the men drum standing in lines, and the sound rolls off the hills like the hills answering back.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wangala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wangala|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wangala-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wangala:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Hundred Drums Say Thank You","text":"नाचने वाले पंखों वाली पगड़ियाँ पहनते हैं जो घास की तरह हिलती हैं, और कतारें एक साथ आगे बढ़ती हैं — कदम, झुकाव, मोड़ — बच्चे और बड़े, कतारों में पूरा गाँव, जहाँ ढोल की गड़गड़ाहट के ऊपर बाँसुरी और झाँझ की धुन गूँजती है। यह कई दिनों तक चलता है। धन्यवाद, अगर सही तरीके से किया जाए, तो उसमें थोड़ा वक्त लगता ही है।","lang":"hi","body":"The dancers wear feathered turbans that nod like grass, and the lines move together — step, dip, turn — young and old, the whole village in rows, with the flutes and gongs riding on top of the drum-thunder. It goes on for days. Thanks, done properly, takes a while.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wangala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wangala|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wangala-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wangala:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Hundred Drums Say Thank You","text":"अपने पहले वांगला में एक बच्ची ने वही सवाल पूछा जो बच्चे हमेशा पूछते हैं: चावल तो हमारा है — हमने खेत साफ़ किया, हमने घास-फूस निकाली, हमने इसे काटा। तो इसका पहला हिस्सा भेंट के रूप में क्यों जाता है?","lang":"hi","body":"A child at her first Wangala asked the question children always ask: the rice is ours — we cleared the field, we weeded it, we cut it. Why does the first of it go away as a gift?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wangala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wangala|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wangala-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wangala:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Hundred Drums Say Thank You","text":"आजकल हर साल नवंबर में गारो पहाड़ियों में एक बड़ा जमावड़ा होता है जहाँ कई गाँवों के ढोलियों की कतारें मिलती हैं — सचमुच एक ही जगह पर सौ ढोल, जो पूर्वोत्तर के सबसे शानदार नज़ारों और आवाज़ों में से एक है। लोग इसके लिए दूर-दूर से आते हैं, ढोलों के बिल्कुल करीब खड़े होते हैं, और उन्हें ज़रा भी पछतावा नहीं होता।","lang":"hi","body":"These days there is a great gathering in the Garo hills each November where lines of drummers from many villages meet — a hundred drums genuinely all in one place, one of the great sights and sounds of the Northeast. People travel a long way for it, and stand very close to the drums, and regret nothing.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wangala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wangala|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.behdienkhlam-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.behdienkhlam:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chasing the Sickness Out of Town","text":"खासी पहाड़ियों के पूरब में पनार लोग रहते हैं — यानी जयंतिया लोग, जिनकी अपनी बोली और अपने तौर-तरीके हैं। और यह साफ़-साफ़ कहना ज़रूरी है: खासी और पनार आपस में सगे हैं, एक-दूसरे की नकल नहीं। उनका यह बड़ा त्योहार जोवाई शहर का है, मानसून का है, और एक बहुत पुराने दुश्मन का है।","lang":"hi","body":"East of the Khasi hills live the Pnar — the Jaintia people, with their own speech and their own ways, and it is worth saying clearly: Khasi and Pnar are kin, not copies. Their great festival belongs to the town of Jowai, to the monsoon, and to a very old enemy.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-behdienkhlam.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.behdienkhlam|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.behdienkhlam-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.behdienkhlam:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chasing the Sickness Out of Town","text":"वह दुश्मन है ख्लाम — यानी महामारी, बीमारी, और वह बुखार जो बरसात के मौसम में पहाड़ी शहरों में घुस आया करता था, जब रास्ते कीचड़ से भर जाते थे और बादल हफ़्तों तक छतों पर डेरा डाले रहते थे। बीमारी को आते हुए कोई नहीं देख सकता। पुराने ज़माने में, आप बस उसे पहुँचते हुए ही देख सकते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"The enemy is khlam — plague, sickness, the fevers that used to walk into hill towns in the wet season when the paths were mud and the clouds sat on the roofs for weeks. You cannot see sickness coming. In the old days you could only watch it arrive.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-behdienkhlam.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.behdienkhlam|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.behdienkhlam-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.behdienkhlam:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chasing the Sickness Out of Town","text":"पनार लोगों का जवाब है बेहदिएनख्लाम, और इसके नाम में ही पूरी योजना छिपी है: 'बेह दिएन ख्लाम' — यानी महामारी को खदेड़ना, उसे पीट-पीटकर शहर से बाहर निकालना। इसे पनार लोगों के अपने धर्म, नियामत्रे को मानने वाले परिवार मनाते हैं, बुआई के कुछ हफ़्तों बाद, जब धान ज़मीन में पड़ चुका होता है और बारिश अपना काम कर रही होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"The Pnar answer is Behdienkhlam, and the name is the plan: beh dien khlam — to chase away the plague, to beat it out of town. It is kept by the families of the Niamtre, the Pnar's own faith, in the weeks after the sowing, when the rice is in the ground and the rain is doing its work.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-behdienkhlam.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.behdienkhlam|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.behdienkhlam-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.behdienkhlam:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chasing the Sickness Out of Town","text":"नौजवान घर-घर जाते हैं, और बाँस के लंबे-लंबे डंडों से छतों को पीटते हैं — जानबूझकर ज़ोरदार खट-खट का शोर मचाते हुए — हर एक घर पर बीमारी से कहते हुए: यहाँ नहीं, बाहर निकलो, इस छत पर पहरा है। किसी का भी घर छूटता नहीं है। खदेड़ने का काम या तो सबके लिए किया जाता है, या फिर बिल्कुल नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"Young men go from house to house, and with long bamboo poles they beat on the rooftops — a tremendous knocking racket, on purpose — telling the sickness at every single house: not here, out you go, this roof is watched. Nobody's house is skipped. Chasing is a thing you do for everybody or not at all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-behdienkhlam.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.behdienkhlam|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.behdienkhlam-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.behdienkhlam:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chasing the Sickness Out of Town","text":"इस बीच कई दिनों से 'रोत' तैयार किए जा रहे होते हैं: बाँस और रंगीन कागज़ के ऊँचे-ऊँचे मीनार, हर मोहल्ला अपना मीनार खड़ा करता है, हर साल पिछले साल से भी ज़्यादा शानदार। उस बड़े दिन पर, उन्हें कंधों पर उठाकर पूरे शहर में ले जाया जाता है, और वे ऐसे झूमते हैं जैसे पेड़ों ने चलना सीख लिया हो।","lang":"hi","body":"Meanwhile the rots have been building for days: tall towers of bamboo and coloured paper, each neighbourhood raising its own, each year's finer than last year's. On the great day they are carried on shoulders through the town, swaying like trees that have learned to walk.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-behdienkhlam.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.behdienkhlam|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.behdienkhlam-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.behdienkhlam:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chasing the Sickness Out of Town","text":"और उन्हें नीचे ऐतनार नाम के एक कीचड़ भरे ताल तक ले जाया जाता है, और वहाँ — बारिश में, भीड़ में, घुटनों तक कीचड़ में — उठाने वाले छपछपाते और ज़ोर लगाते हुए उन्हें नचाते हैं, जबकि पूरा कस्बा किनारों से जयकारे लगाता है। त्योहार का शांत हिस्सा घरों के अंदर बीतता है, जहाँ परिवार अपनी भेंट चढ़ाते हैं; पर शोर-शराबे वाला हिस्सा सचमुच बहुत ही ज़ोरदार होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And they are carried down to a muddy pool called Aitnar, and there — in the rain, in the crowd, in mud to the knee — the carriers dance them, wading and heaving, while the whole town roars from the banks. The quiet half of the festival happens indoors, where families make their offerings; the loud half is very loud indeed.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-behdienkhlam.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.behdienkhlam|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.behdienkhlam-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.behdienkhlam:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chasing the Sickness Out of Town","text":"आखिरी दिन दातलाकॉर की बारी आती है: लकड़ी की एक गेंद, कस्बे की दो टीमें, और बिना किसी रेफ़री का एक ऐसा खेल जो आधा फ़ुटबॉल है और आधी ज़बरदस्त छीना-झपटी। कहते हैं कि जो भी तरफ़ जीतती है, फ़सल घाटी के उसी हिस्से में सबसे अच्छी होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"On the last day comes datlawakor: a wooden ball, two sides of the town, and a game with no referee that is half football and half glorious struggle. Whichever side wins, they say, the harvest will favour their end of the valley.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-behdienkhlam.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.behdienkhlam|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chemtatrawta-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chemtatrawta:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · It All Started With a Lobster","text":"मिज़ोरम में, जब सब कुछ एक साथ गड़बड़ हो जाता है और कोई नहीं बता पाता कि गलती किसकी है, तब कोई बुज़ुर्ग आह भरते हुए कहते हैं: यह तो फिर वही झींगे वाली बात हो गई। और उनका मतलब इसी कहानी से होता है। यह चेमतातरौता नाम के एक आदमी की कहानी है — जिसका कमोबेश मतलब है अपना दाओ तेज़ करने वाला आदमी, क्योंकि चेम पहाड़ों का वह बड़ा काम आने वाला चाकू होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"In Mizoram, when everything has gone wrong at once and nobody can say whose fault it is, somebody old will sigh and say: this is the lobster all over again. And this is the story they mean. It is about a man called Chemtatrawta — which means, more or less, the man sharpening his dao, for a chem is the big working knife of the hills.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chemtatrawta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chemtatrawta|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chemtatrawta-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chemtatrawta:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · It All Started With a Lobster","text":"एक सुबह चेमतातरौता झरने के किनारे बैठकर ठीक यही कर रहा था, अपने ही काम से काम रखते हुए एक गीले पत्थर पर अपनी चेम की धार तेज़ कर रहा था। और उथले पानी में से एक झींगे ने — जो इस किस्से को शायद अलग तरह से सुनाए, पर छोड़िए — आगे बढ़कर उसके हाथ पर ज़ोर से चिमटी काट ली।","lang":"hi","body":"Chemtatrawta sat by the stream one morning doing exactly that, sharpening his chem on a wet stone, minding absolutely nobody's business. And a lobster in the shallows — who tells this part differently, but never mind — reached out and pinched him, hard, on the hand.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chemtatrawta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chemtatrawta|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chemtatrawta-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chemtatrawta:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · It All Started With a Lobster","text":"वह चीखते हुए उछल पड़ा और उसने हवा में अंधाधुंध वार किया, और बाँस का एक पूरा झुरमुट कटकर गिर पड़ा। बाँस जा गिरा एक जंगली मुर्गी की पीठ पर, जो पर फड़फड़ाते हुए गुस्से में अपनी ज़मीन से उड़ी — और सीधे चींटियों के टीले में जा घुसी, उसे किसी फटी हुई बोरी की तरह लात मारकर बिखेर दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"He leapt up with a shout and slashed out wildly, and down came a stand of bamboo. The bamboo fell on the back of a jungle fowl, who exploded off her scratching-ground in a fury of feathers — straight through an ants' nest, kicking it open like a burst sack.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chemtatrawta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chemtatrawta|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chemtatrawta-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chemtatrawta:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · It All Started With a Lobster","text":"चींटियाँ, जो ऐसी बातों को दिल पर ले लेती हैं, कतार बनाकर बाहर निकलीं और जो भी पहली बड़ी चीज़ उन्हें दिखी, उसे काट खाया — और वह था एक सोता हुआ जंगली सूअर। सूअर किसी भूस्खलन की तरह धड़धड़ाता हुआ उठा और पास वाले केले के पेड़ को चीरता हुआ भागा — जहाँ एक चमगादड़ उल्टा लटका सो रहा था और अंजीरों के सपने देख रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"The ants, who take these things personally, marched out and bit the first large thing they found, which was a sleeping wild boar. The boar came up like a landslide and charged through the nearest plantain tree — where a fruit bat was asleep, upside down, dreaming of figs.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chemtatrawta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chemtatrawta|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chemtatrawta-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chemtatrawta:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · It All Started With a Lobster","text":"चमगादड़ नींद से अंधा होकर उड़ा और सीधे हाथी के कान में जा घुसा। हाथी — जो कान के अंदर होने वाली गड़बड़ के अलावा दुनिया की हर चीज़ में बड़ा बहादुर था — गाँव के किनारे से सरपट भागा, उसने एक बूढ़ी औरत की बाड़ गिरा दी, उसकी कपास को पैरों तले रौंद डाला और मचान पर सूख रहे पानी के तुम्बों को चकनाचूर कर दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"The bat flew off blind with sleep and went straight into the ear of the elephant. The elephant — who is enormously brave about everything except surprises inside his ear — bolted through the edge of the village, flattened an old woman's fence, trampled her cotton flat and smashed the water-gourds drying on her rack.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chemtatrawta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chemtatrawta|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chemtatrawta-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chemtatrawta:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · It All Started With a Lobster","text":"तो अब क्या था: एक बूढ़ी औरत जिसके पास न बाड़ बची, न कपास और न पानी भरने का कोई बर्तन, एक गाँव जिसका रास्ता कीचड़ बन चुका था, एक सहमा हुआ चमगादड़, हज़ारों ग़ुस्सैल चींटियाँ, एक चोट खाई मुर्गी, बाँस का गिरा हुआ झुरमुट, और नदी किनारे बैठा एक आदमी जो अपनी कटी हुई उँगली चूस रहा था। और यह सब दोपहर के खाने से पहले ही हो गया।","lang":"hi","body":"So now: an old woman with no fence, no cotton and nothing to carry water in, a village with its path churned to mud, one shocked bat, several thousand furious ants, a bruised hen, a felled bamboo grove, and one man by the stream sucking his pinched hand. All before lunch.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chemtatrawta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chemtatrawta|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chemtatrawta-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chemtatrawta:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · It All Started With a Lobster","text":"गाँव के मुखिया ने वही किया जो मिज़ो गाँव ऐसे बड़े बखेड़े में हमेशा से करते आए हैं: उन्होंने सबको बुलाया और सबके सामने, एक-एक करके पूरी पूछताछ की।","lang":"hi","body":"The village chief did what Mizo villages have always done with a proper mess: he called everyone in and held an inquiry, in order, out loud.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chemtatrawta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chemtatrawta|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chemtatrawta-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chemtatrawta:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · It All Started With a Lobster","text":"\"हाथी, तुमने तुम्बे क्यों फोड़े?\" \"क्योंकि चमगादड़ मेरे कान में घुस गया था।\" \"चमगादड़, तुम उसके कान में क्यों घुसे?\" \"क्योंकि सूअर ने मेरा पेड़ गिरा दिया था।\" \"सूअर?\" \"चींटियों ने मुझे काटा था।\" \"चींटियाँ?\" \"मुर्गी ने हमारे बिल पर लात मारी थी।\" \"मुर्गी?\" \"बाँस मुझ पर आ गिरा था।\" \"बाँस—\" और यहाँ सब मुड़कर चेमतातरावता को देखने लगे, जिसका चेहरा शर्म से लाल हो गया।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Elephant, why did you smash the gourds?\" \"Because the bat flew into my ear.\" \"Bat, why did you fly into his ear?\" \"Because the boar knocked down my tree.\" \"Boar?\" \"Ants bit me.\" \"Ants?\" \"The fowl kicked our nest.\" \"Fowl?\" \"The bamboo fell on me.\" \"Bamboo—\" and here everyone turned to Chemtatrawta, who turned rather red.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chemtatrawta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chemtatrawta|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chemtatrawta-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chemtatrawta:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · It All Started With a Lobster","text":"\"झींगे ने मुझे चिमटी काट ली थी,\" उसने कहा। और एक बर्तन में नदी से लाए गए झींगे ने अपनी मूँछें हिलाईं और पूरे दिन की सबसे सच्ची बात कही: \"मेरी नदी में एक बड़ा सा हाथ आया था। मैंने बिना देखे ही चिमटी काट ली।\" थोड़ी देर सन्नाटा रहा, और फिर पूरा गाँव एक साथ ठहाका मारकर हँस पड़ा, क्योंकि इस कड़ी के हर एक जीव ने बिल्कुल वही काम किया था।","lang":"hi","body":"\"The lobster pinched me,\" he said. And the lobster, brought up from the stream in a pot, waved his whiskers and said the only honest thing said all day: \"A great hand came into my stream. I pinched before I looked.\" There was a silence, and then the whole village laughed at once, because every single creature in the chain had done exactly the same thing.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chemtatrawta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chemtatrawta|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-door-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-door:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chhura Minds the Door","text":"मिज़ोरम का सबसे प्यारा इंसान कभी था ही नहीं, या फिर हर जगह मौजूद था, बात तो एक ही है। उसका नाम है छूरा — पूरा नाम छूरबुरा — और वह एक बेवकूफ़ है। कोई दुष्ट बेवकूफ़ नहीं, कोई उदास बेवकूफ़ नहीं: एक लाजवाब बेवकूफ़! गाँव आपस में इस बात पर बहस करते हैं कि वह किस गाँव का था, और इससे ही सब समझ आ जाता है। कोई इस बात पर बहस नहीं करता कि किसी बेवकूफ़ को कौन झेले। वे तो इस बात पर लड़ते हैं कि वह किसे मिले।","lang":"hi","body":"Mizoram's best-loved man never existed, or existed everywhere, which comes to the same thing. His name is Chhura — Chhurbura, in full — and he is a fool. Not a wicked fool, not a sad one: a magnificent one. Villages argue about which village he came from, which tells you everything. Nobody argues over who has to keep a fool. They argue over who gets to.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-door|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-door-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-door:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chhura Minds the Door","text":"एक दिन छूरा के परिवार को पड़ोस के गाँव में एक दावत का न्योता मिला — एक बढ़िया वाली दावत, जिसमें सूअर का गोश्त भी था। किसी न किसी को तो पीछे रुकना ही था, क्योंकि पहाड़ों में घर खुला छोड़कर जाने का रिवाज़ नहीं था। \"छूरा,\" उसकी पत्नी ने बहुत सोच-समझकर शब्द चुनते हुए कहा, जैसा कि उसने इतने समय में सीखा था, \"यहीं रुको। दरवाज़े का ध्यान रखना। चाहे कुछ भी हो जाए, दरवाज़ा छोड़कर मत जाना।\"","lang":"hi","body":"One day Chhura's family was invited to a feast in the next village — a proper one, with a pig in it. Somebody had to stay back, because in the hills you did not leave a house standing open. \"Chhura,\" said his wife, choosing her words with the care his wife had learned to use, \"stay here. Mind the door. Do not leave the door, whatever happens.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-door|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-door-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-door:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chhura Minds the Door","text":"छूरा दरवाज़े के पास बैठ गया। उसने उसका ध्यान रखा। दरवाज़ा बहुत अच्छा था और उसने बड़े मन से उसका ध्यान रखा। एक घंटा बीत गया। दरवाज़े ने कुछ नहीं किया, जो कि दरवाज़ों का मुख्य काम होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Chhura sat by the door. He minded it. It was a good door and he minded it thoroughly. An hour passed. The door did nothing, which is the main activity of doors.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-door|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-door-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-door:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chhura Minds the Door","text":"और तभी हवा का रुख बदला, और घाटी के नीचे से दावत की हल्की मगर साफ़ खुशबू आने लगी। गोश्त, धुएँ और भुनी हुई चीज़ों की खुशबू। छूरा खड़ा हुआ। वह फिर बैठ गया। उसने दरवाज़े को देखा। उसे बस एक हिदायत दी गई थी, और वह ऐसा आदमी था जो बातों को बड़ी गंभीरता से लेता था — यह तो कभी उसकी परेशानी थी ही नहीं। उसकी परेशानी यह थी कि वह उस बात का मतलब क्या निकालता था।","lang":"hi","body":"And then the wind changed, and down the valley, faint but unmistakable, came the smell of the feast. Pork and smoke and roasting things. Chhura stood up. He sat down. He looked at the door. He had been given one instruction, and he was a man who took instructions seriously — that was never his problem. His problem was what he took them to mean.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-door|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-door-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-door:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chhura Minds the Door","text":"उसने दरवाज़े को उसके कब्ज़ों से उतारा, उसे लकड़ी के एक विशाल बस्ते की तरह अपनी पीठ पर रस्सियों से बाँध लिया, और पहाड़ी की चोटी के रास्ते चल पड़ा, मोड़ों पर बड़ी सावधानी से चलते हुए ताकि दरवाज़े के कोने कहीं टकरा न जाएँ।","lang":"hi","body":"He lifted the door off its pegs, roped it flat onto his back like an enormous wooden rucksack, and set off over the ridge, taking the turns carefully on account of his corners.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-door|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-door-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-door:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chhura Minds the Door","text":"जैसे ही वह अंदर आया, दावत में सन्नाटा छा गया। उसकी पत्नी ने उसे देखा, फिर दरवाज़े को देखा, और बरसों के तजुर्बे वाले शांत भाव से बोली — \"छुड़ा। यह दरवाज़ा दावत में क्यों आया है?\" और छुड़ा ने, सचमुच हैरान होकर कि यह बात भी बतानी पड़ रही है, उससे कहा: \"तुमने ही तो कहा था कि इसे छोड़ना मत। मैंने इसे एक पल के लिए भी नहीं छोड़ा। दरवाज़े से ही पूछ लो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The feast fell quiet as he came in. His wife looked at him, and looked at the door, and said — with the calm of long experience — \"Chhura. Why is the door at the feast?\" And Chhura, honestly baffled that it needed saying, told her: \"You said not to leave it. I have not left it for one moment. Ask the door.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-door|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-door-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-door:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chhura Minds the Door","text":"पूरा परिवार भागता हुआ घर पहुँचा, जहाँ उनका घर दिन भर पहाड़ों के हर जीव-जंतु के लिए खुला पड़ा रहा था। मुर्गियाँ चावल में घुसी थीं। बकरी अजीब सा मुँह बनाए बिस्तर पर बैठी थी। घर को ठीक-ठाक करने में रात हो गई, और छुड़ा ने भी दरवाज़ा उठाए-उठाए मदद की, जिसे उसने तब तक अलग करने से मना कर दिया जब तक वह वापस अपने कब्ज़ों पर नहीं चढ़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"The family ran all the way home, where the house had stood open all day to every creature in the hills. The hens were in the rice. The goat was on the bed, wearing an expression. It took till nightfall to put the house right, and Chhura helped, carrying the door, which he refused to be parted from until it was back on its pegs.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-door|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-door-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-door:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Chhura Minds the Door","text":"और कोई भी उससे ज़्यादा देर नाराज़ नहीं रह पाता था — छुड़ा की यही तो ख़ास बात है, और यही वजह है कि पीढ़ियों से पूरा समाज उसे अपनी कहानियों में ज़िंदा रखे हुए है। उसकी गलतियाँ कभी आलस भरी या बदनीयत नहीं होती थीं। वह तो बस आपकी हर बात को पकड़कर ऐसी दिशा में निकल पड़ता था, जहाँ जाने का आपने कभी सोचा भी न हो।","lang":"hi","body":"And nobody could stay cross with him — that is the thing about Chhura, and the reason a whole people has kept him fed with stories for generations. His mistakes were never lazy and never mean. He simply took every word you said and walked off with it in a direction you had not imagined words could go.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-door|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-nahaia-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-nahaia:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Field That Hummed","text":"छुड़ा का एक भाई था जिसका नाम नहाइया था, और नहाइया दूसरी तरह से मशहूर था: चालाक। लगभग दस प्रतिशत ज़रूरत से ज़्यादा चालाक, जो कि सबसे ख़तरनाक बात है। जहाँ छुड़ा आपकी बातों को किसी अजीब दिशा में ले जाता था, वहीं नहाइया आपकी चीज़ों को अपने घर की तरफ ले जाता था।","lang":"hi","body":"Chhura had a brother called Nahaia, and Nahaia was the other kind of famous: clever. Too clever, by about ten per cent, which is the most dangerous amount. Where Chhura took your words somewhere strange, Nahaia took your things somewhere his.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-nahaia.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-nahaia|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-nahaia-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-nahaia:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Field That Hummed","text":"उन दोनों ने उस साल नए खेत साफ़ किए — दोनों के लिए एक-एक 'लो', यानी ढलान पर काटकर बनाया गया पहाड़ी खेत, जैसा कि इन पहाड़ों में खेती की जाती है। और जब साफ़-सफ़ाई पूरी हो गई, तो नहाइया अपनी ज़मीन पर टहला और अचानक ठिठक कर रुक गया। उसके खेत के बीचों-बीच पेड़ के एक बड़े से खोखले तने में, चावल की टोकरी जितना बड़ा जंगली मधुमक्खियों का छत्ता लटका था, जो अपनी ही धुन में धीमी गूँज से गूँज रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"The two of them cleared new fields that year — a lo each, a hill field cut from the slope, which is how farming is done in these mountains. And when the clearing was finished, Nahaia walked his own land and stopped dead. In the great hollow stump in the middle of his field hung a wild bees' nest the size of a rice basket, roaring quietly to itself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-nahaia.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-nahaia|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-nahaia-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-nahaia:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Field That Hummed","text":"\"नहाइया को डंक खाने का कोई शौक़ नहीं था। इसलिए वह बड़ा सीधा-सच्चा मुँह बनाकर अपने भाई के पास गया। \\\"छुरा। मुझे बड़ा दुख हो रहा है, पर मैं तुमसे अपना खेत बदलने को तैयार हूँ। मेरी ज़मीन ज़्यादा अच्छी है — तुम ख़ुद सुन सकते हो। मेरा खेत ज़िंदगी की गुनगुनाहट से गूँजता है। मुझे उस गुनगुनाहट की बहुत याद आएगी।\\\" और छुरा, जो लोगों का भरोसा कर लेता था, उसी वक़्त खेत बदलने को तैयार हो गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Nahaia was not fond of stings. So he went to his brother wearing his sincerest face. \"Chhura. It pains me, but I will swap fields with you. Mine is the better land — you can hear it. My field hums with life. I will miss that hum terribly.\" And Chhura, who believed people, swapped on the spot.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-nahaia.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-nahaia|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-nahaia-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-nahaia:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Field That Hummed","text":"\"छुरा अपने नए खेत में घूमा और उसे गुनगुनाहट सुनाई दी, और वह आवाज़ के पीछे-पीछे पेड़ के एक ठूंठ तक पहुँचा, और ऊपर देखा तो सिर के ऊपर हज़ारों मधुमक्खियाँ — खुआइ, यानी पहाड़ों की जंगली मधुमक्खियाँ — अपने काम में लगी हुई थीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Chhura walked his new field and heard the hum and followed it to the stump, and looked up at several thousand bees — khuai, the wild honeybees of the hills — going about their business over his head.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-nahaia.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-nahaia|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-nahaia-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-nahaia:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Field That Hummed","text":"\"वह पूरी दोपहर उन्हें देखता रहा, जो पैरों पर सुनहरी धूल लपेटे आ-जा रही थीं। उसने न तो उन पर चिल्लाया और न ही छत्ते को छेड़ा, क्योंकि किसी मूर्ख को भी यह बात साफ़ समझ आती — शायद किसी मूर्ख को तो और भी अच्छे से — कि वे कामगार अपने काम में जुटे थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He watched them all afternoon, coming and going with their legs dusted gold. He did not shout at them or poke the nest, because it was obvious even to a fool — especially to a fool, perhaps — that they were workers at work.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-nahaia.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-nahaia|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-nahaia-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-nahaia:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Field That Hummed","text":"\"फिर, एक ठंडी और धुंध भरी सुबह, जब मधुमक्खियाँ अपने छत्ते में सुस्त और अलसाई थीं, वह हरी पत्तियों के धीमे धुएँ के साथ चुपके से आया, ज़ोर से उनका शुक्रिया अदा किया — जिसका मधुमक्खियों ने कोई जवाब दिया हो ऐसा कोई लिखित सबूत नहीं है — और उनके लिए उनका हिस्सा छोड़कर, छत्ते का एक बड़ा सा हिस्सा ले लिया। वह मटके भर-भरकर शहद घर लाया। घाटी का सबसे मीठा शहद, लोगों ने कहा, और लोग बिल्कुल सच कह रहे थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then, on a cold misty morning when the bees were slow and sleepy in their nest, he came quietly with a smudge of green-leaf smoke, thanked them out loud — which the bees are not recorded as acknowledging — and took a fat share of the comb, leaving them theirs. He carried home honey by the potful. The sweetest in the valley, people said, and people were right.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-nahaia.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-nahaia|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-nahaia-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-nahaia:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Field That Hummed","text":"\"ख़बर सुनते ही नहाइया दौड़ता हुआ पहुँचा। वह मटकों को देखते हुए अपनी ही चालाकी का हिसाब जोड़ने लगा, और हिसाब में पाया कि वह तो घाटे में रहा। \\\"वह,\\\" आख़िरकार उसने कहा, \\\"मेरा खेत था।\\\" \\\"हाँ, था तो,\\\" छुरा ने हँसते हुए हामी भरी। \\\"किसी भाई का दिया सबसे ज़्यादा गुनगुनाने वाला खेत।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"Nahaia arrived at a run, having heard. He stood looking at the pots, doing the arithmetic of his own cleverness, and finding it came out owing. \"That,\" he said at last, \"was my field.\" \"It was,\" agreed Chhura pleasantly. \"The hummingest field a brother ever gave me.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-nahaia.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-nahaia|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chhura-nahaia-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chhura-nahaia:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Field That Hummed","text":"\"और फिर — क्योंकि छुरा का दिल ही उसकी वह इकलौती चीज़ थी जिसे किसी ने कभी मूर्ख नहीं कहा — उसने छत्ते का एक टुकड़ा काटा और उसके हाथ में थमा दिया। भाई तो भाई होते हैं, और शहद बाँटकर खाने के लिए होता है, उनके साथ भी जो चाहते थे कि तुम्हें डंक लग जाएँ।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And then — because Chhura's heart was the one thing about him nobody ever called foolish — he cut a piece of comb and handed it over. Brothers are brothers, and honey is for sharing, even with the ones who meant you to be stung.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chhura-nahaia.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chhura-nahaia|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ngaitei-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ngaitei:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ngaitei and the River","text":"एक गहरी हरी नदी के ऊपर बसे गाँव में न्गाइतेई नाम की एक लड़की अपनी दादी के साथ रहती थी — यानी अपनी 'पी' के साथ, जैसा कि मिज़ो बच्चे कहते हैं। उसके पिता बहुत पहले उसी नदी में खो गए थे, इतना पहले कि उसे उनकी कोई याद भी नहीं थी। उसकी पी का एक ही सीधा सा नियम था: किनारे से अपना घड़ा भरो, और सीधे ऊपर आ जाओ। जहाँ पानी शांत हो, वहाँ कभी मत ठहरना।","lang":"hi","body":"In a village above a deep green river lived a girl called Ngaitei, with her grandmother — her pi, as Mizo children say. Her father had been lost to that river long before she could remember him. Her pi's one rule was simple: fill your pot at the edge, and come straight up. Never linger where the water is quiet.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ngaitei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ngaitei|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ngaitei-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ngaitei:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ngaitei and the River","text":"एक दोपहर न्गाइतेई के टखनों के इर्द-गिर्द पानी ने उसे थाम लिया। झटके से नहीं — बल्कि एक हाथ की तरह, जो बेरहम तो नहीं था, पर छोड़ भी नहीं रहा था। और वह उस हरे पानी में नीचे उतरती चली गई, वहाँ तक जहाँ रोशनी किसी खास जगह से नहीं आती, और उस सन्नाटे में उसके पिता की आवाज़ शामिल थी। उन्हें अपनी बेटी की बहुत याद आई थी। नदी का यह देश जिसे प्यार करता है, उसे अपने पास रख लेता है, और उसने न्गाइतेई को भी अपने पास रख लेने का फैसला कर लिया था।","lang":"hi","body":"One afternoon the water around Ngaitei's ankles held on. Not roughly — like a hand, not unkind, but not letting go. And she went down into the green, down to where the light comes from nowhere in particular, and the quiet had her father's voice in it. He had missed her. The river-country keeps what it loves, and it had decided to keep her too.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ngaitei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ngaitei|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ngaitei-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ngaitei:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ngaitei and the River","text":"अँधेरा होने से पहले उसकी दादी किनारे पर आईं, न तो वे चीखीं और न ही बल्लियाँ लिए आदमियों को बुलाने दौड़ीं। वे पानी के बिल्कुल किनारे खड़ी हो गईं और उसमें झाँकते हुए बोलीं, बिल्कुल वैसे जैसे कोई किसी ऐसे रिश्तेदार से बात करता है जिसका वह आदर तो करता है पर उससे सहमत नहीं होता। \"वही मेरा सब कुछ है। तुम्हारे पास तो तुम्हारा अपना देश है और तुम्हारे साथी भी हैं। उसे ऊपर भेज दो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Her grandmother came to the bank before dark, and did not scream and did not run for the men with poles. She stood at the very lip of the water and spoke into it, the way you speak to a relative you respect and disagree with. \"She is all I have. You have your country and your company. Send her up.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ngaitei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ngaitei|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ngaitei-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ngaitei:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ngaitei and the River","text":"और नदी ने — यह एक मिज़ो नदी थी, पुराने खयालों वाली, लेन-देन के हिसाब में पक्की — उसे एक शर्त के साथ ऊपर भेज दिया, उस आवाज़ में जो गहरे पानी की होती है: वह मेरी कोई चीज़ अपने पास नहीं रखेगी। सतह के इस पार की कोई भी चीज़ उसके साथ किनारे के ऊपर नहीं जाएगी। दादी मान गईं, और न्गाइतेई को अपने ही कपड़े में लपेटकर घर ले आईं, और ज़िंदगी फिर चलने लगी।","lang":"hi","body":"And the river — this is a Mizo river, old-fashioned, correct about debts — sent her up, with one condition, spoken in the way deep water speaks: she keeps nothing of mine. Nothing that belongs to this side of the surface goes up the bank with her. The grandmother agreed, and carried Ngaitei home wrapped in her own cloth, and life went on.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ngaitei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ngaitei|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ngaitei-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ngaitei:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ngaitei and the River","text":"बारिशें आईं। और नदी चढ़ने लगी। वह अपने रोज़ के पत्थरों को पार कर ऊपर आई, फिर नहाने की जगह को पार किया, और फिर — धीरे-धीरे, सब्र के साथ, एक-एक गली नापते हुए, बिना किसी गुस्से के, जो गुस्से से भी कहीं ज़्यादा गंभीर था — सीधे गाँव के अंदर तक आ पहुँची। वह किसी चीज़ की तलाश में थी। जो पानी किसी चीज़ को ढूँढ रहा होता है, उसमें एक अजीब सी खामोशी होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"The rains came. And the river rose. It came up past its usual stones, then past the bathing place, then — slowly, patiently, street by street, not angry, which was somehow more serious than angry — into the village itself. It was looking for something. Water that is looking for something has a particular quiet.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ngaitei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ngaitei|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ngaitei-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ngaitei:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ngaitei and the River","text":"दादी अपने दरवाज़े पर खड़ी थीं, पानी सीढ़ी तक आ पहुँचा था, और उन्होंने नदी की तरह सोचना शुरू किया। हम दोनों में तय हुआ था। मैं अपनी बात निभाती हूँ। तो फिर इस घर में ऐसा क्या है, जो हमारा नहीं है?","lang":"hi","body":"The grandmother stood in her doorway with the water at the step, and made herself think like a river. We agreed. I keep my word. So what, in this house, is not ours?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ngaitei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ngaitei|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ngaitei-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ngaitei:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ngaitei and the River","text":"न्गाइतेइ अपनी चटाई के पास गई और तकिए के नीचे से उसे निकाल लाई: लकड़ी की एक कंघी, पुरानी होकर काली पड़ चुकी। उसके पिता की कंघी, पहले के दिनों की। वह उसे अपनी चादर में लपेटकर किनारे से ऊपर लाई थी, क्योंकि उसके पास अपने पिता की बस वही एक निशानी बची थी, और उसने किसी को कुछ नहीं बताया था, क्योंकि जिन चीज़ों को हम छोड़ नहीं पाते, उनके साथ हम ऐसा ही करते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Ngaitei went to her sleeping mat and brought it out from under the pillow: a wooden comb, dark with age. Her father's comb, from before. She had carried it up the bank inside her wrap, because it was all of him she had, and she had told nobody, because that is what we do with the things we cannot give up.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ngaitei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ngaitei|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ngaitei-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ngaitei:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ngaitei and the River","text":"वे दोनों मिलकर उसे पानी के किनारे तक ले गईं, और दादी ने बड़े प्यार से, कोई मीठा बोल कहकर उसे पानी की सतह पर रख दिया, बिल्कुल वैसे जैसे कोई बाड़ के पार कोई कीमती चीज़ थमाता है। कंघी एक बार घूमी और डूब गई। और नदी थम गई। एक पल के लिए रुकी, जैसे कोई लंबा काम पूरा होने पर इंसान ठहर जाता है — और अपने घर लौट गई, नहाने के घाट को पार करती हुई, पत्थरों को पीछे छोड़ती हुई, वापस अपने पाट में।","lang":"hi","body":"They carried it to the water's edge together, and her grandmother put it on the surface gently, with a kind word, the way you hand something precious across a fence. The comb turned once and went under. And the river stopped. Stood a moment, the way a person stands when a long errand is finally done — and went home, past the bathing place, past the stones, back into its bed.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ngaitei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ngaitei|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mauruangi-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mauruangi:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Mauruangi and the Silk-Cotton Tree","text":"मौरुआंगी की माँ अब नहीं रही थीं। कैसे गईं, मिज़ो की पुरानी कहानियाँ यह बात बड़े कड़वे ढंग से बताती हैं, और आज रात हम बस इतना ही कहेंगे कि वे चली गईं, और नदी ने उन्हें अपने पास रख लिया। उसके पिता ने दूसरा ब्याह कर लिया, और नई पत्नी की अपनी भी एक बेटी थी, और उसी दिन से उस घर में दो तरह के चावल बनने लगे: एक चावल, और दूसरा जो बचा-खुचा रह जाता था।","lang":"hi","body":"Mauruangi's mother was gone. How, the old Mizo tellings say harshly, and tonight we will say only that she was gone, and that the river had her. Her father married again, and the new wife had a daughter of her own, and from that day there were two kinds of rice in that house: rice, and what was left of it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mauruangi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mauruangi|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mauruangi-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mauruangi:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Mauruangi and the Silk-Cotton Tree","text":"सौतेली बहन हाँडी से खाती थी। मौरुआंगी के हिस्से आती खुरचन और चावल धोने का पानी, भारी-भरकम काम, और चूल्हे का वह कोना जहाँ आँच बुझ चुकी होती थी। यह एक पुराना अन्याय है; कई कहानियों में यह इसलिए दर्ज है क्योंकि कई बचपनों ने इसे झेला था।","lang":"hi","body":"The stepsister ate from the pot. Mauruangi got the scrapings and the water the rice was washed in, and the heavy work, and the cold end of the fire. It is an old unfairness; many tales carry it because many childhoods did.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mauruangi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mauruangi|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mauruangi-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mauruangi:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Mauruangi and the Silk-Cotton Tree","text":"मगर सौतेली माँ की समझ में एक बात नहीं आ रही थी: मौरुआंगी बिल्कुल नहीं मुरझाई। उसकी आँखें चमकती थीं, गाल गोल-मटोल थे, और वह पानी भरने की पगडंडी पर गाती हुई जाती थी। जिसे सिर्फ़ जूठन खाने को मिलती थी, वह लड़की पूनम के चाँद-सी दमक रही थी। सौतेली माँ को लगा, यह तो एक तरह की ढिठाई थी।","lang":"hi","body":"But here is what the stepmother could not understand: Mauruangi did not fade. Her eyes were bright, her cheeks were round, she sang on the path to the water. A girl fed on scraps, glowing like the harvest moon. It was, the stepmother felt, somehow insolent.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mauruangi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mauruangi|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mauruangi-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mauruangi:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Mauruangi and the Silk-Cotton Tree","text":"यह राज़ नदी में छुपा था। हर रोज़, जब मौरुआंगी अपना घड़ा लेकर नीचे आती, गहरे पानी से एक बड़ी-सी मांगुर मछली ऊपर उठती और उसे खाना खिलाती — अपने मुँह से बढ़िया चावल, चूल्हे से उतरे हुए जैसे गर्म। \"मुँह खोलो, नन्हीं बच्ची,\" वह कहती। और उसकी आवाज़ ऐसी थी जिसे मौरुआंगी पहचानती थी, उस ज़माने से भी पहले से जो उसे याद था। नदी के पास उसकी माँ थी; अब आप जान ही गए होंगे कि नदी ने उसकी माँ के साथ क्या किया था।","lang":"hi","body":"The secret lived in the river. Every day, when Mauruangi came down with her pot, a great catfish rose out of the deep water and fed her — good rice, from its own mouth, warm as if from a hearth. \"Open your mouth, little one,\" it would say. And its voice was a voice she knew, from before remembering. The river had her mother; now you know what the river had done with her.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mauruangi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mauruangi|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mauruangi-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mauruangi:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Mauruangi and the Silk-Cotton Tree","text":"सौतेली माँ ने जासूसी के लिए अपनी बेटी को भेजा, और राज़ घर पहुँच गया। फिर उस मछली का क्या हुआ, यह पुरानी कहानियों में तो साफ़-साफ़ बताया गया है, पर यह कहानी नहीं बताएगी। मछली जा चुकी थी। बस इतना ही। मौरुआंगी उसी किनारे पर बैठी रही जहाँ वह मछली उभरा करती थी, और पानी अब सिर्फ़ पानी था।","lang":"hi","body":"The stepmother sent her own daughter to spy, and the secret came home, and what was done about the fish the old tellings say plainly and this one will not. The fish was gone. That is all. Mauruangi sat on the bank where it used to rise, and the water was just water.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mauruangi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mauruangi|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mauruangi-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mauruangi:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Mauruangi and the Silk-Cotton Tree","text":"और तभी, ठीक उसी किनारे से एक पेड़ निकल आया। एक फुनचावंग — यानी सेमल का पेड़, वही जो एक भी पत्ता लाने से पहले लाल फूलों से पहाड़ियों को दहका देता है। वह उतनी ही तेज़ी से बढ़ा जितनी तेज़ी से दूर असम में तेजिमोला के लिए बेल बढ़ी थी, और उस पर बिना मौसम के फूल खिल उठे, ठीक उस जगह के ऊपर जहाँ एक लड़की छाँव की आस में बैठी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"And then, from that very bank, a tree came up. A phunchawng — the silk-cotton tree, the one that sets the hills on fire with red flowers before it bothers with a single leaf. It grew as fast as the vine had grown for Tejimola far away in Assam, and it flowered out of season, directly over the place where a girl sat needing shade.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mauruangi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mauruangi|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mauruangi-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mauruangi:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Mauruangi and the Silk-Cotton Tree","text":"जो कोई भी उस पेड़ के नीचे सुस्ताता, उसका पेट भर जाता — असल में पेट में नहीं, बल्कि उस जगह, जहाँ पेट की ख़बर पहुँचती है। मौरुआंगी वहीं बैठकर रोती और वहीं गाती, और वह पेड़ उस पर वैसे ही लाल फूल गिराता जैसे कोई माँ सिर थपथपाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Whoever rested under that tree came away fed — not in the stomach, exactly, but in the place the stomach reports to. Mauruangi did her crying there and her singing there, and the tree dropped red flowers on her the way a mother pats a head.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mauruangi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mauruangi|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mauruangi-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mauruangi:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Mauruangi and the Silk-Cotton Tree","text":"एक दिन एक लाल — यानी सरदार, क्योंकि मिज़ो भाषा में यही शब्द है — वहाँ से घोड़े पर गुज़रे और उन्होंने फूलों से लदे पेड़ के नीचे एक लड़की को उसका नाम लेकर शुक्रिया गाते सुना। वे रुक गए। \"तुम्हें कौन खिलाता है, बच्ची?\" उन्होंने पूछा, क्योंकि वे वह घर देख सकते थे जहाँ से वह आई थी और उन्होंने अपना हिसाब लगा लिया था।","lang":"hi","body":"One day a lal — a chief, for that is the Mizo word — came riding past and heard a girl under a flowering tree, singing thanks to it by name. He stopped. \"Who feeds you, child?\" he asked, because he could see the house she came from and had done his own arithmetic.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mauruangi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mauruangi|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mauruangi-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mauruangi:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · Mauruangi and the Silk-Cotton Tree","text":"लाल ने उसकी पूरी बात सुनी, और देर तक उस पेड़ को देखते रहे, फिर उन्होंने उसे अपने घर चलने को कहा — मालकिन बनकर, कोई नौकरानी बनकर नहीं; कहानियाँ मानती हैं कि वह खुशी-खुशी चली गई। और अपने नए दरवाज़े के पास, उसने सबसे पहले फुनचावंग का एक बीज बोया। शायद वह आज भी वहाँ खिलता होगा, बिन मौसम ही, जब भी किसी को उसकी ज़रूरत होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"The lal heard her out, and looked a long time at the tree, and asked her to come to his house — as its lady, not its servant; the tellings agree she went gladly. And by her new door, the first thing she planted was a phunchawng seed. It is probably flowering there still, out of season, whenever somebody needs it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mauruangi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mauruangi|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sichangneii-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sichangneii:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Winged One","text":"मिज़ो कहानियों में सिचांगनेई की बात आती है — पंखों वाली और चमकदार, आसमान के देश की बेटी। कोई उसे आसमान की परी कहता है, कोई पंछी-स्त्री; कहानियाँ इतनी पुरानी हैं कि उनमें अलग-अलग बातें होना लाज़मी है। पर इस बात पर सब एकमत हैं कि वह अपनी बहनों के साथ पहाड़ों के एक ताल पर उतरी थी, और इस आम दुनिया के आम पानी में नहाने के लिए उसने अपने पंख घास पर उतारकर रख दिए थे।","lang":"hi","body":"The Mizo tellings speak of Sichangneii — winged and shining, a daughter of the sky country. Some say sky-maiden, some say bird-woman; the tellings are old enough to disagree. What they agree on is that she came down, with her sisters, to a pool in the hills, and set her wings on the grass to bathe in the ordinary water of the ordinary world.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sichangneii.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sichangneii|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sichangneii-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sichangneii:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Winged One","text":"पहाड़ों का एक नौजवान पेड़ों के पीछे से सांस साधे यह सब देख रहा था। और जब वे बहनें उठीं, उन्होंने अपने पंख पहने और आसमान में उड़ गईं, जैसे चिंगारियाँ लौटकर आग में जा रही हों — तब भी पंखों की एक जोड़ी घास पर ही पड़ी रह गई, क्योंकि वह दबे पाँव आगे बढ़ा और उन्हें उठा ले गया था।","lang":"hi","body":"A young man of the hills was watching from the trees with his breath held. And when the sisters rose and dressed in their wings and went up like sparks going home to a fire — one pair of wings still lay on the grass, because he had crept out and taken them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sichangneii.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sichangneii|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sichangneii-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sichangneii:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Winged One","text":"उसने उन पंखों को अपनी छत के छप्पर में गहराई में छुपा दिया। और सिचांगनेई, जो उड़ नहीं सकती थी, वहीं रह गई। यहाँ कहानी को उसके साथ भी इंसाफ करना होगा, और वह करती भी है: बाकी हर बात में वह बहुत भला था। वह उसके लिए मेहनत करता, उसके साथ मिलकर गाता, उसने उसके लिए एक ऊँचा घर बनाया। उसने उससे ब्याह कर लिया। बच्चे हुए, हँसी-खुशी का माहौल रहा, और ज़्यादातर दिन आसमान उनके लिए सिर्फ मौसम भर था।","lang":"hi","body":"He hid the wings deep in the thatch of his roof. And Sichangneii, who could not fly, stayed. Here the telling must be fair to him, because it is: he was kind in every other thing. He worked for her, sang with her, built the house tall. She married him. There were children, and there was laughter, and most days the sky was just weather.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sichangneii.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sichangneii|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sichangneii-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sichangneii:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Winged One","text":"लेकिन साफ़ शामों में वह दरवाज़े पर खड़ी होकर बाज़ों को ढलती रोशनी में ऊपर, और ऊपर उड़ते देखती, जब तक कि वे आँखों से ओझल न हो जाते। और उसका पति अपने हाथों को किसी न किसी काम में उलझाए रखता, क्योंकि जो सच वह जानता था सो जानता था, और वह छप्पर हर पल उन दोनों के ठीक सिर के ऊपर था।","lang":"hi","body":"But on clear evenings she would stand in the doorway and watch the hawks going up the last light, all the way up, until they were nothing. And her husband would find something to do with his hands, because he knew what he knew, and the thatch was directly over both of them the whole time.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sichangneii.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sichangneii|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sichangneii-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sichangneii:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Winged One","text":"\"सालों बाद, बच्चे वहाँ खेल रहे थे जहाँ बच्चों को नहीं खेलना चाहिए था—ऊपर छत के नीचे। और उन्हें वह सुंदर चीज़ मिल गई। वे बड़े गर्व से उसे नीचे अपनी माँ के पास लाए: देखो हमारे घर में क्या छिपा हुआ था! और सिचांगनेई बिल्कुल शांत खड़ी रह गईं, अपने ही पंखों को थामे हुए, यह महसूस करते हुए कि पंख आज भी उन्हें याद रखे हुए थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Years in, the children were playing where children should not, up under the roof — and they found the beautiful thing. They brought it down to their mother, proud as anything: look what was hidden in our house. And Sichangneii stood very still, holding her own wings, feeling them remember her.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sichangneii.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sichangneii|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sichangneii-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sichangneii:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Winged One","text":"\"न तो वे चिल्लाईं, और न ही रोईं, और किस्सों में यह भी नहीं कहा जाता कि वे ज़्यादा देर झिझकीं भी। आसमान उनकी माँ का देस था, और उन्हें उससे दूर रखा गया था—और किसी को बाँधकर रखना प्यार करना नहीं होता, चाहे यह कितने भी प्यार से क्यों न किया गया हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"She did not shout, and she did not weep, and the tellings do not say she even hesitated long. The sky was her mother's country, and she had been kept from it — and keeping is not the same as loving, however kindly it is done.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sichangneii.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sichangneii|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sichangneii-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sichangneii:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Winged One","text":"\"उन्होंने पंख पहन लिए। उन्होंने घर के तीन चक्कर लगाए—किस्सों में यह बात आज भी कही जाती है, छप्पर के ठीक ऊपर तीन धीमे चक्कर, बिना किसी चीज़ को छुए और बिना कुछ छोड़े—और फिर वे ऊपर उड़ गईं, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे उन बरसों पहले उनकी बहनें गई थीं, और नीला आसमान उन्हें अपने में समेट ले गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"She put the wings on. She circled the house three times — the tellings keep that detail, three slow circles, low over the thatch, touching nothing and leaving nothing out — and then she went up, the way her sisters had gone all those years before, and the blue took her in.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sichangneii.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sichangneii|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.liandova-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.liandova:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Brothers and the Great Snake","text":"\"लियानदोवा और उसका छोटा भाई तुआईसिआला अनाथ थे, और पुराने पहाड़ी गाँवों में एक अनाथ की ज़िंदगी किसी और के चूल्हे के पास की ठंडी ज़मीन जैसी होती थी। वे कटे हुए खेतों से गिरे दाने चुनते, उन्हें वही दिया जाता जो किसी को नहीं चाहिए होता था, और बाकी बच्चे उन्हें ऐसे नामों से चिढ़ाते थे जिन्हें यह कहानी दोहराएगी नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Liandova and his little brother Tuaisiala were orphans, and in the old hill villages an orphan's life was a cold seat by somebody else's fire. They gleaned the cut fields, they were given what nobody wanted, and the other children had names for them that this story does not repeat.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-liandova.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.liandova|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.liandova-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.liandova:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Brothers and the Great Snake","text":"\"मगर लियानदोवा के हाथ में जो कुछ भी आता, वह सबसे पहले उसके भाई के मुँह में जाता। हमेशा। कोई भुनी हुई जड़, सूखी मछली का एक टुकड़ा, किसी नन्हीं चिड़िया का एक पंख—हर बार लियानदोवा से पहले तुआईसिआला ही खाता, और अगर सिर्फ एक ही निवाला होता, तो लियानदोवा कह देता कि उसे भूख नहीं है। जिन भाइयों के पास और कुछ नहीं होता, उनके पास यह साथ होता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"But whatever came into Liandova's hands went first to his brother's mouth. Always. A roasted root, a scrap of dried fish, one wing of a small bird — Tuaisiala ate before Liandova did, every single time, and if there was one mouthful only, Liandova was not hungry, he said. Brothers who have nothing else have this.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-liandova.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.liandova|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.liandova-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.liandova:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Brothers and the Great Snake","text":"जब भी गाँव में कोई दावत होती, तो दोनों भाइयों को बचा-खुचा खाना और अलाव की रोशनी का सबसे दूर वाला कोना मिलता था। कोई इतना बेरहम नहीं था कि उन्हें वहाँ से भगा दे, और कोई इतना मेहरबान भी नहीं था कि उन्हें पास बुला ले—और यह अपने आप में एक अलग ही तरह की बेरुखी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"When the village held its feasts, the brothers got the leavings and the far edge of the firelight. Nobody was cruel enough to send them away and nobody was kind enough to call them close, which is its own particular kind of cold.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-liandova.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.liandova|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.liandova-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.liandova:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Brothers and the Great Snake","text":"फिर उस बड़े साँप वाला दिन आया। गाँव से बहुत दूर दाना-तिनका बीनते हुए, दोनों भाइयों को एक अजगर मिला—बूढ़ा, सुस्त, बहुत ही विशाल, छत की शहतीर जितना मोटा और अपने ख़तरनाक दिन बहुत पीछे छोड़ चुका। जहाँ पूरे मौसम में बड़े-बड़े शिकारियों को कुछ नहीं मिला था, वहाँ दो भूखे बच्चे एक ऐसा शिकार घसीटते हुए घर लाए, जिस पर यकीन करने के लिए आधा गाँव उमड़ पड़ा।","lang":"hi","body":"Then came the day of the great snake. Out gleaning far from the village, the brothers found a python — old, slow, enormous, thick as a roof-beam and long past its dangerous years. Where grown hunters had found nothing all season, two hungry boys came home dragging a catch it took half the village to believe.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-liandova.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.liandova|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.liandova-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.liandova:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Brothers and the Great Snake","text":"और उसके अंदर—यह वह हिस्सा है जिसे सुनाते वक्त लोग ज़रा पास झुक जाते हैं—उन्हें वह सब मिला जो उस बूढ़े अजगर ने अपने सौ सालों के जीवन में निगला था: दार, यानी पीतल के वे घंटे जिनकी खनक इन पहाड़ियों में दौलत मानी जाती है, और पुराने ज़माने के वैसे मोती जैसे किसी सरदार की पत्नी पहनती है। गाँव के सबसे ग़रीब लड़के एक ख़ज़ाने के सामने खड़े थे।","lang":"hi","body":"And inside it — this is the part the tellings lean close to say — they found what the old python had swallowed in its hundred years of swallowing: dar, the brass gongs, whose voices are wealth in these hills, and beads of the old kind, the kind a chief's wife wears. The poorest boys in the village stood in front of a fortune.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-liandova.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.liandova|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.liandova-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.liandova:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Brothers and the Great Snake","text":"पहाड़ों पर बात बड़ी तेज़ी से ऊपर तक फैलती है। शाम होते-होते, वे लोग जिन्होंने कभी दोनों भाइयों को आग के पास नहीं बुलाया था, उनकी झोपड़ी के सामने टहलने लगे, मौसम की बातें करने लगे, और बड़े प्यार से याद करने लगे कि वे तो हमेशा से इन लड़कों का कितना भला चाहते थे। आपने भी लोगों को ऐसा करते देखा होगा। यह देखना बिल्कुल अच्छा नहीं लगता।","lang":"hi","body":"Word travels uphill fast. By evening, people who had never once called the brothers to a fire were strolling past their hut, remarking on the weather, remembering warmly that they had always thought well of the boys. You have seen this done. It is not beautiful.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-liandova.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.liandova|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.liandova-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.liandova:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Brothers and the Great Snake","text":"लियानदोवा के पास घंटे थे, मोती थे, और एक ऐसी याददाश्त थी जो सब कुछ बहुत अच्छी तरह याद रखती थी। और अब उसे एक फ़ैसला लेना था, क्योंकि मिज़ो की पहाड़ियों में दौलत का एक ही सबसे बड़ा इस्तेमाल होता है: इज़्ज़त की दावत, जहाँ एक आदमी पूरे गाँव को खाना खिलाता है और इसके लिए उसे बड़ा माना जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Liandova had gongs, beads, and a memory that worked perfectly. And now he had a decision, because wealth in the Mizo hills has one great use: the feast of honour, where a man feeds the whole village and is counted great for it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-liandova.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.liandova|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.liandova-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.liandova:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Brothers and the Great Snake","text":"लियानदोवा ने जो दावत दी, वह ऐसी थी जिसे ये पहाड़ियाँ आज भी याद रखती हैं—घंटों की गूँज, गर्मागर्म भाप उड़ाते चावल, हर घर का भरा हुआ पेट, और वे लोग जिन्होंने कभी उसका मज़ाक उड़ाया था, वे नज़रें गड़ाए सिर्फ़ अपने खाने पर ध्यान देकर खा रहे थे। और इन सबमें सबसे आगे, जिसे सबसे पहले बिठाया गया और सबसे पहले परोसा गया, वह था नन्हा तुआईसिआला, जो अपनी मुस्कान रोक ही नहीं पा रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"The feast Liandova gave is the kind the hills remember — the gongs sounding, the rice steaming, every household fed, the ones who had mocked him eating with their eyes carefully on their food. And at the head of it all, seated first, served first, little Tuaisiala, who could not quite stop grinning.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-liandova.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.liandova|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.liandova-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.liandova:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Brothers and the Great Snake","text":"किसी को भी उसका नाम लेकर ताना नहीं दिया गया। यह लियानडोवा की दौलत का आख़िरी और सबसे बढ़िया हिस्सा था: वह उस दिन चाहता तो सौ अपमान ख़रीद सकता था, पर इसके बजाय उसने पूरा गाँव ख़रीद लिया।","lang":"hi","body":"Nobody's name was thrown back at them. That was the last of Liandova's wealth and the best of it: he could have bought a hundred humiliations that day, and he bought a village instead.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-liandova.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.liandova|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chapchar-kut-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chapchar-kut:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of the Waiting","text":"मिज़ो पहाड़ियों में खेती का साल एक बहुत बड़ी मेहनत से शुरू होता है: उस साल के 'लो' यानी पहाड़ी खेत के लिए बाँस के जंगल का एक हिस्सा काटा जाता है। और फिर — कुछ भी नहीं। साफ़ की गई ज़मीन को जलाने और बोने से पहले कटे हुए बाँसों का सूखना ज़रूरी होता है। सूखने के इसी ठहराव को चापचार कहते हैं। हाथ ख़ाली, काम नामुमकिन, और हर कोई बस मौसम के इंतज़ार में।","lang":"hi","body":"The farming year in the Mizo hills begins with an enormous effort: a patch of bamboo forest is cut for the year's lo, the hill field. And then — nothing. The cut bamboo must lie and dry before the clearing can be burned and sown. That drying pause is called chapchar. Hands empty, work impossible, everyone simply waiting on the weather.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chapchar-kut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chapchar-kut|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chapchar-kut-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chapchar-kut:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of the Waiting","text":"और ठीक इसी ठहराव के बीच मिज़ो लोगों ने बहुत पहले अपने सबसे बड़े त्योहार को जगह दी: चापचार कुट, यानी इंतज़ार के वक़्त का 'कुट' — त्योहार। इसकी शुरुआत की कहानी आमतौर पर यूँ बताई जाती है कि शिकारियों की एक टोली ख़ाली हाथ घर लौटी, और मुखिया ने बेकार बैठे दिनों में गाँव को उदास होने देने के बजाय दावत का ऐलान कर दिया — और वह दावत इतनी अच्छी रही कि उन्होंने इसे हमेशा के लिए अपना लिया।","lang":"hi","body":"And into exactly that pause the Mizo people long ago put their greatest festival: Chapchar Kut, the kut — the festival — of the waiting time. The story usually told about how it began is that a hunting party came home empty-handed, and the chief, rather than let the village sit glum in its idle days, called for a feast — and the feast was so good they kept it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chapchar-kut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chapchar-kut|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chapchar-kut-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chapchar-kut:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of the Waiting","text":"चापचार कुट की जान चेराव है, और चेराव देखने के लिए तो पूरे देश का सफ़र किया जा सकता है। ज़मीन पर बाँस के लंबे-लंबे डंडे जोड़ों में बिछाए जाते हैं, और बजाने वाले उनके सिरों पर घुटनों के बल बैठकर उन्हें आपस में टकराते हैं — खुला, बंद, खुला, बंद — एक ऐसी लय में जो आती हुई बारिश की तरह तेज़ होती जाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"The heart of Chapchar Kut is the cheraw, and the cheraw is worth crossing the country for. Long bamboo poles are laid in pairs on the ground, and the clappers kneel at their ends and clap them — open, shut, open, shut — in a rhythm that quickens like rain arriving.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chapchar-kut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chapchar-kut|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chapchar-kut-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chapchar-kut:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of the Waiting","text":"और टकराते हुए उन्हीं बाँसों के बीच नर्तक क़दम रखते हैं। बंद होते फ़ासलों के अंदर-बाहर, ताल पर, चटख बुने हुए पुआन पहने लड़कियाँ चिड़ियों की तरह नफ़ासत से क़दम बढ़ाती हैं, जबकि बाँस हर टखने के ठीक एक उँगली पीछे खटाक से बंद होते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"And between those clapping bamboos, dancers step. In and out of the closing gaps, on the beat, girls in the bright woven puan stepping neat as birds, while the poles snap shut a finger's width behind each ankle.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chapchar-kut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chapchar-kut|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chapchar-kut-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chapchar-kut:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of the Waiting","text":"यहाँ खुआल्लम भी है — मेहमानों का नाच, जिसे कंधों पर चादर ओढ़े झूमती हुई कतारों में नाचा जाता है, वो नाच जिसके ज़रिये बाहर से आए लोगों को भी इस घेरे में शामिल कर लिया जाता है। इन पहाड़ियों में किसी त्योहार को इस बात से परखा जाता है कि कोई अजनबी कितनी पूरी तरह से अपना बन जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"There is khuallam too — the dance of the guests, danced in swaying lines with cloth draped over the shoulders, the dance with which visitors are drawn into the circle. A festival in these hills is judged by how completely a stranger stops being one.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chapchar-kut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chapchar-kut|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chapchar-kut-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chapchar-kut:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of the Waiting","text":"चापचार कुट कुछ दशकों के लिए धीमा पड़ गया था — इन पहाड़ियों के धर्म बदले और शासक भी बदले, और कुछ समय के लिए यह पुराना त्योहार सूखते बाँस की तरह शांत पड़ा रहा। फिर, हमारे बुज़ुर्गों के ही देखते-देखते, मिज़ो लोग इसे पूरे मन से वापस ले आए, क्योंकि हर समाज को अपनी बहार सँभाल कर रखने का पूरा हक़ है।","lang":"hi","body":"Chapchar Kut faded for some decades — the hills changed faiths and changed rulers, and for a while the old festival lay as quiet as the drying bamboo. Then, within living memory, Mizos brought it back, deliberately, because a people is allowed to keep its own springtime.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chapchar-kut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chapchar-kut|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chapchar-kut-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chapchar-kut:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Festival of the Waiting","text":"इसलिए आज मिज़ोरम में ज़्यादातर ईसाई हैं, और फिर भी हर मार्च आइज़ोल में चापचार कुट उसी तरह धूमधाम से भर जाता है — एक दिन चर्च के गीत, तो अगले दिन चेराव, एक ही तस्वीर में इतवार के ख़ास कपड़े और पुरानी बुनाई, न किसी को कोई झिझक और न किसी से कोई एक चुनने को कहा जाता है। यह किसी के विश्वास का मुक़ाबला नहीं है। यह तो बस इन पहाड़ियों का अपने पूरे साल को याद करना है।","lang":"hi","body":"So today Mizoram is largely Christian, and Chapchar Kut fills Aizawl every March all the same — church choirs one day, cheraw the next, Sunday best and ancient weave in the same photograph, nobody embarrassed and nobody asked to choose. It is not a rival to anyone's faith. It is the hills remembering their year.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chapchar-kut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chapchar-kut|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unakoti-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unakoti:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Less Than a Crore","text":"त्रिपुरा के जंगलों से भरे उत्तर में एक ऐसी पहाड़ी ढलान है, जिसे देखकर लोग बात करते-करते रुक जाते हैं। खड़ी चट्टानों से उभरे चेहरे — इतने विशाल, घर से भी ऊँचे, जिनमें शिव का मुकुट पहने एक भव्य सिर भी है — और अनगिनत छोटी नक्काशीदार आकृतियाँ, जिनमें से कुछ पर से झरने ऐसे बहते हैं मानो पहाड़ खुद अपने देवताओं को नहला रहा हो।","lang":"hi","body":"In the forested north of Tripura there is a hillside that stops people mid-sentence. Out of the living rock, faces — enormous ones, taller than a house, a great crowned head of Shiva among them — and smaller carvings beyond counting, with waterfalls running over some of them as though the hill were washing its own gods.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unakoti|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unakoti-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unakoti:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Less Than a Crore","text":"इस जगह का नाम उनाकोटी है, और यह नाम असल में एक गिनती है: एक कोटि यानी एक करोड़ से एक कम। निन्यानवे लाख, निन्यानवे हज़ार, नौ सौ निन्यानवे। नाम कहता है कि कोई था, जिसकी गिनती ठीक एक से एक करोड़ होने से रह गई। वह कौन था, इसके बारे में दो कहानियाँ कही जाती हैं, और आप दोनों सुन सकते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The place is called Unakoti, and the name is a number: one less than a koti — a crore, ten million. Ninety-nine lakh, ninety-nine thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine. Somebody, the name says, fell exactly one short of a crore. Two stories are told about who, and you may have them both.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unakoti|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unakoti-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unakoti:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Less Than a Crore","text":"पहली कहानी: शिव जी काशी जा रहे थे, और उनके साथ एक करोड़ देवी-देवता भी चल रहे थे — मानो पूरा आसमान ही सफ़र पर निकल पड़ा हो। इन पहाड़ियों में रात हो गई, तो सबने वहीं डेरा डाल दिया। शिव जी ने कहा, \"हम सुबह की पहली किरण के साथ निकलेंगे। सब के सब। एक साथ।\" और वो एक करोड़ मुसाफ़िर मान गए, जम्हाई ली, और सो गए।","lang":"hi","body":"The first: Shiva was travelling to Kashi, and with him went a crore of gods and goddesses — a whole sky on the move. Night caught them in these hills, and they made camp. \"We leave at first light,\" said Shiva. \"All of us. Together.\" And the crore of travellers agreed, and yawned, and slept.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unakoti|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unakoti-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unakoti:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Less Than a Crore","text":"सुबह की पहली किरण फूटते ही बस एक मुसाफ़िर जागा: शिव जी। एक करोड़ में से सिर्फ़ एक। बाकी सब उस मीठी पहाड़ी हवा में सोते ही रहे, बिल्कुल वैसे जैसे तुम अपने भाई-बहनों के घर सोते हो जब कोई तुम्हें जगाता नहीं। और शिव जी ने देर तक उन सबको देखा — और अकेले ही काशी के लिए आगे बढ़ गए।","lang":"hi","body":"At first light, one traveller woke: Shiva. One, out of a crore. The rest slept on in the sweet hill air, the way you sleep at your cousins' house when nobody wakes you. And Shiva looked at them all for a long moment — and went on to Kashi alone.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unakoti|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unakoti-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unakoti:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Less Than a Crore","text":"लोग कहते हैं कि इसीलिए पहाड़ी पर बने इन चेहरों पर ऐसा गहरा, बेफ़िक्र सुकून है: वे मूर्तियाँ नहीं हैं, वे तो सोए हुए लोग हैं। और उनाकोटी में कोई भी आपसे यह वादा नहीं करेगा कि वे बस किसी और भी चमकदार सुबह का इंतज़ार नहीं कर रहे हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"That is why, people say, the faces on the hill have that deep, unbothered calm: they are not statues, they are sleepers. And nobody at Unakoti will promise you they are not simply waiting for a louder morning.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unakoti|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unakoti-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unakoti:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Less Than a Crore","text":"दूसरी कहानी एक कारीगर की है: कल्लू, वहीं का एक मूर्तिकार, जिसका बहुत मन था कि वह शिव और पार्वती जी के साथ उनके पर्वत पर जाए। उसने विनती की, मुझे भी अपने साथ ले चलिए। और उसके सामने एक कारीगर की परीक्षा रखी गई: एक ही रात में पूरे एक करोड़ रूप तराशो। भोर होने से पहले काम पूरा करो, और साथ चलो।","lang":"hi","body":"The second story belongs to a craftsman: Kallu, a local sculptor, who longed to travel with Shiva and Parvati to their mountain. Take me with you, he begged. And he was set a maker's test: carve a full crore of images in a single night. Finish before the dawn, and come.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unakoti|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unakoti-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unakoti:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Less Than a Crore","text":"कल्लू धुन के पक्के इंसान की तरह मूर्तियाँ तराशने लगा। रात भर चट्टानों से चेहरे खिलते रहे — बड़े-बड़े, छोटे-छोटे, हज़ारों देवता, उसके हाथों के नीचे पूरी पहाड़ी भरती चली गई। फिर पेड़ों के ऊपर से भोर की रोशनी छा गई, और गिनती एक करोड़ से एक कम रह गई। सिर्फ़ एक। कम।","lang":"hi","body":"Kallu carved like a man on fire. Faces bloomed out of the rock all night — great ones, small ones, gods by the thousand, the hill filling under his hands. And the dawn came up over the trees, and the count stood at one less than a crore. One. Less.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unakoti|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unakoti-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unakoti:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Less Than a Crore","text":"तो वह नहीं जा सका। लेकिन ज़रा देखिए कि वह किस चीज़ को पीछे छोड़कर नहीं जा सका: एक ऐसी पहाड़ी जिसे उसने देवताओं से भर दिया था, किसी भी हाथ से किया गया एक रात का सबसे महान काम। कहानियों में इस बात पर सहमति नहीं है कि वह दुखी हुआ या उसने बस फिर से अपनी छेनी उठा ली — और इस बात का पक्का पता न होने में ही ज़िंदगी की एक पूरी सीख छुपी है।","lang":"hi","body":"So he could not go. But look what he could not go from: a hillside he had covered with gods, the greatest night's work any hands ever did. The tellings do not agree on whether he grieved or simply picked up his chisel again — and there is a whole life's lesson in not being sure which.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unakoti|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.twipra-name-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.twipra-name:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Beside the Water","text":"अगरतला की एक लड़की का भाई विदेश में रहता था, जिसने सरसराते फ़ोन पर उससे एक सीधा सा सवाल पूछा: त्रिपुरा का असल में मतलब क्या है? और उसे अहसास हुआ कि उसे तो पता ही नहीं। तो उसने वही सही काम किया जो करना चाहिए था — अपने दादा-दादी से पूछा। कमरे में दोनों ही मौजूद थे, और यहीं से यह कहानी शुरू होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"A girl in Agartala had a cousin abroad who asked her, over a crackling phone line, a simple question: what does Tripura actually mean? And she realised she did not know. So she did the correct thing, which was to ask a grandparent. She happened to have two in the room, which is where this story comes from.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-twipra-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.twipra-name|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.twipra-name-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.twipra-name:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Beside the Water","text":"उसकी दादी ने कोकबोरोक में जवाब दिया, क्योंकि कोकबोरोक उनकी भाषा है — बोरोक लोगों यानी त्रिपुरियों की बोली। \"खुद इस नाम को ध्यान से सुनो, बच्ची। 'त्वी' का मतलब है पानी। इन पहाड़ियों की हर नदी इसे अपने साथ बहाती है — नदियों के नाम लो तो तुम कह रही हो त्वी, त्वी, त्वी। त्विप्रा: यानी पानी के किनारे की ज़मीन। यह हम हैं। हमने तो अपने नाम भी बोली और लोगों के नाम पर रखे हैं: 'कोक' का मतलब है बोली, और 'बोरोक' का मतलब है लोग। कोकबोरोक — यानी लोगों की बोली।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Her grandmother answered in Kokborok, because Kokborok is her language — the tongue of the Borok people, the Tripuris. \"Listen to the name itself, child. Twi is water. Every river in these hills carries it — say the river names and you are saying twi, twi, twi. Twipra: the land beside the waters. That is us. We even named ourselves for speech and people: kok is speech, Borok are the people. Kokborok — the speech of the people.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-twipra-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.twipra-name|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.twipra-name-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.twipra-name:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Beside the Water","text":"उसके दादाजी ने अपना गला साफ़ किया, जिसका मतलब हर भाषा में यही होता है कि \"एक दूसरा जवाब भी है।\" \"राजाओं का इतिहास कुछ और ही कहता है। राजमाला — यानी राजाओं की माला, वह पुरानी पद्य गाथा जिसे सदियों तक दरबारी पंडितों ने संजोया — शाही वंश को पीछे, बहुत पीछे तक ले जाती है, और उन कथाओं में यह नाम बहुत पुराने किसी राजा से आता है, या फिर खुद देवी से, त्रिपुरा सुंदरी से, जिनका स्थान दक्षिण में माताबाड़ी में है। एक शाही नाम, एक शाही घराने से।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Her grandfather cleared his throat, which in every language means \"there is another answer.\" \"The kings' chronicle says otherwise. The Rajmala — the garland of kings, the old verse chronicle the court pandits kept for centuries — traces the royal line back and back, and in those tellings the name comes from a king of long ago, or from the goddess herself, Tripura Sundari, whose seat is at Matabari in the south. A royal name, from a royal house.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-twipra-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.twipra-name|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.twipra-name-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.twipra-name:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Beside the Water","text":"लड़की ने एक बार इधर देखा, एक बार उधर। एक तरफ़ पानी और लोग; दूसरी तरफ़ राजा और एक देवी। और फ़ोन पर इंतज़ार करता उसका भाई।","lang":"hi","body":"The girl looked from one to the other. Water and people on one side; kings and a goddess on the other. And the phone line to her cousin waiting.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-twipra-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.twipra-name|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.twipra-name-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.twipra-name:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Beside the Water","text":"तो उसने यही किया। \"दादी कहती हैं: हमारी अपनी ज़ुबान में, पानी के किनारे की ज़मीन। दादाजी कहते हैं: राजाओं का इतिहास इसे पुराने शाही वंश और देवी से जोड़ता है। और वे दोनों यहीं बैठे सिर हिला रहे हैं, इसलिए मैं किसी एक को नहीं चुन रही।\"","lang":"hi","body":"So that is what she did. \"Grandmother says: the land beside the waters, in our own words. Grandfather says: the kings' chronicle ties it to the old royal line and the goddess. And they are both sitting here nodding, so I am not choosing.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-twipra-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.twipra-name|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.twipra-name-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.twipra-name:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Beside the Water","text":"“और सच कहें तो बात यहीं पर आ ठहरती है, और विद्वान बड़े चाव से लंबे समय से इस पर बहस करते आ रहे हैं। जिन जगहों को कई लोगों ने प्यार किया हो, उनके नाम की भी अक्सर एक से ज़्यादा कहानियाँ बन जाती हैं—प्यार करने वाले हर रुख से एक अलग कहानी।”","lang":"hi","body":"And that is honestly where the matter stands, and scholars have argued it happily for a very long time. Places that many peoples have loved tend to end up with more than one name-story, one from each direction of loving.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-twipra-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.twipra-name|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.twipra-name-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.twipra-name:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Beside the Water","text":"“वैसे बता दें कि परदेस वाले चचेरे भाई को पानी वाला जवाब सबसे ज़्यादा पसंद आया, और दादाजी ने ऐसा जताया जैसे उन्हें कोई फ़र्क़ नहीं पड़ा, और दादीजी ने तो कुछ भी जताने का नाटक नहीं किया, क्योंकि उन्होंने यह फ़ैसला साफ़-साफ़ सुन लिया था और उन्हें यह बिल्कुल सही लगा। त्वी, उन्होंने फिर से कहा, किसी से ख़ास तौर पर नहीं। पानी।”","lang":"hi","body":"The cousin abroad, for the record, liked the water answer best, and the grandfather pretended not to mind, and the grandmother did not pretend anything, because she had heard the verdict perfectly well and considered it correct. Twi, she said again, to nobody in particular. Water.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-twipra-name.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.twipra-name|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kharchi-fourteen-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kharchi-fourteen:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Week of the Fourteen Gods","text":"“त्रिपुरा की राजधानी से थोड़ी ही दूर, पुराने अगरतला में एक ऐसा मंदिर है जहाँ कुछ ऐसा है जो और कहीं नहीं मिलता: चतुर्दश देवता, यानी त्रिपुरा के चौदह भगवान, जिन्हें देवताओं के एक ही परिवार की तरह साथ रखा गया है—राजाओं के ज़माने से इस धरती के ख़ास रखवाले।”","lang":"hi","body":"In Old Agartala, a little way out of Tripura's capital, stands a temple that holds something found nowhere else: the Chaturdasha Devata, the Fourteen Gods of Tripura, kept together as one family of the divine — the special guardians of the land since the days of its kings.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kharchi-fourteen.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kharchi-fourteen|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kharchi-fourteen-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kharchi-fourteen:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Week of the Fourteen Gods","text":"“उनकी देखरेख करने वाले हैं चंताई—त्रिपुरी समुदाय के पुजारी, जिनकी यह सेवा पुराने राज-काज के दिनों से चली आ रही है, उस ज़माने से भी पहले जब मंदिर तक कोई सड़क भी नहीं जाती थी। माणिक्य वंश के राजाओं ने, जिन्होंने सदियों तक त्रिपुरा पर राज किया, इस पूजा को पूरे राज्य की अपनी पूजा बनाए रखा; अब वह राज-पाट एक राज्य बन चुका है, और पूजा बस वैसे ही चली आ रही है।”","lang":"hi","body":"Their keepers are the Chantai — priests from the Tripuri community, whose office has come down from the old royal days, long before the temple had a road to it. The kings of the Manikya line, who ruled Tripura for centuries, kept this puja as the kingdom's own; the kingdom has become a state, and the puja has simply carried on.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kharchi-fourteen.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kharchi-fourteen|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kharchi-fourteen-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kharchi-fourteen:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Week of the Fourteen Gods","text":"“और याद रखने वाली बात यह है: इन चौदहों में से हर एक के दो-दो नाम हैं। एक कोकबोरोक नाम, जो पहाड़ियों से आया है—बुज़ुर्ग सबसे बड़े देवता को सुब्रई राजा कहते हैं—और एक संस्कृत नाम, जो मैदानी परंपरा से आया है। दो भाषाएँ, जो एक ही वेदी पर प्रार्थना कर रही हैं, इतने पुराने समय से जिसका कोई हिसाब भी नहीं।”","lang":"hi","body":"And here is the detail to keep: the fourteen have two names each. A Kokborok name, from the hills — the elders speak of the eldest as Subrai Raja — and a Sanskrit name from the plains tradition. Two languages, praying at one altar, for as long as anyone can measure.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kharchi-fourteen.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kharchi-fourteen|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kharchi-fourteen-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kharchi-fourteen:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Week of the Fourteen Gods","text":"\"हर साल जुलाई में उनका हफ़्ता आता है: खारची पूजा। उन चौदहों को बाहर लाया जाता है और एक जुलूस में नदी तक ले जाया जाता है, और वहाँ उन्हें नहलाया जाता है — बड़े जतन और आदर के साथ, जैसे आप अपने किसी प्यारे दादा-दादी को नहलाएँ — और फिर वे चमकते हुए वापस घर लाए जाते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Every July comes their week: Kharchi Puja. The fourteen are brought out and carried in procession to the river, and there they are bathed — carefully, with honour, the way you would bathe a beloved grandparent — and carried home again shining.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kharchi-fourteen.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kharchi-fourteen|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kharchi-fourteen-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kharchi-fourteen:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Week of the Fourteen Gods","text":"\"कई बड़े-बुजुर्ग आपको बताएँगे कि यह हफ़्ता खुद धरती माँ के स्नान का भी होता है — कि बुवाई के मौसम के बाद ज़मीन थक जाती है और काम से मैली हो जाती है, और खारची उसे भी साफ़-सुथरा कर देती है। एक ऐसा त्योहार जहाँ उस ज़मीन की भी देखभाल की जाती है जिस पर आप खड़े हैं: यह बात सचमुच सोचने और महसूस करने लायक है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Many elders will tell you the week is also a washing for the earth herself — that after the sowing season the land is tired and stained with work, and Kharchi cleanses her too. A festival where the ground you stand on is one of the ones being cared for: that is worth sitting with.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kharchi-fourteen.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kharchi-fourteen|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kharchi-fourteen-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kharchi-fourteen:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Week of the Fourteen Gods","text":"\"और मंदिर के चारों ओर पूरे हफ़्ते भर एक मेला लगा रहता है — राज्य के सबसे बड़े मेलों में से एक। पहाड़ों के परिवार और मैदानों के परिवार, कोकबोरोक और बंगाली, दुकानें, झूले और चाशनी का धुआँ, हर कोई बड़े प्यार से एक-दूसरे के रास्ते में आ-जा रहा होता है। और वे चौदह इसके बीचों-बीच ऐसे बैठे होते हैं जैसे किसी शादी में घर के बड़े-बुजुर्ग।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And around the temple, for the whole week, a mela — one of the great fairs of the state. Hill families and plains families, Kokborok and Bengali, stalls and wheels and sugar-smoke, everybody in everybody's way in the friendliest possible manner. The fourteen sit at the centre of it like grandparents at a wedding.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kharchi-fourteen.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kharchi-fourteen|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kharchi-fourteen-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kharchi-fourteen:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Week of the Fourteen Gods","text":"\"कभी यह राजा की अपनी पूजा हुआ करती थी, जिसका सारा ख़र्च राजमहल से आता था। आज पूरी सरकार खुद इस हफ़्ते का सम्मान करती है, और भीड़ इतनी होती है जितनी किसी राजा ने कभी नहीं देखी होगी। रक्षक, आख़िरकार, उन सिंहासनों से भी ज़्यादा समय तक टिके रहते हैं जिन्होंने पहली बार उनके आगे सिर झुकाया था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Once it was the king's own puja, paid from the palace. Today the state itself honours the week, and the crowds are larger than any king ever saw. Guardians, it turns out, outlast the thrones that first bowed to them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kharchi-fourteen.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kharchi-fourteen|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.garia-puja-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.garia-puja:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The God Who Comes Up Your Steps","text":"\"जब त्रिपुरा की पहाड़ियों में नया साल आता है — अप्रैल के बीच में, वही बड़ा बदलाव जो पूरी घाटी और पहाड़ों की दुनिया एक साथ मनाती है — तब त्रिपुरी, जमातिया और रियांग समुदाय गरिया के दिन मनाते हैं, और गरिया ऐसे देवता नहीं हैं जिनके पास आप जाते हैं। गरिया खुद आपके पास आते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"When the new year turns in the hills of Tripura — mid-April, the same great turning the whole valley-and-hill world shares — the Tripuri, Jamatia and Reang communities keep the days of Garia, and Garia is not a god you go to. Garia comes to you.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-garia-puja.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.garia-puja|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.garia-puja-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.garia-puja:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The God Who Comes Up Your Steps","text":"\"वे साल भर की हर ज़रूरी चीज़ देने वाले देवता हैं — फ़सल, मवेशी, बच्चे और घर की बरकत — और अपने दिनों में वे एक सीधा-सादा और सुंदर रूप धरते हैं: बाँस की एक छड़ी, जिसे सजाया-सँवारा और पूजा जाता है, और जिनकी अपनी शोभायात्रा निकलती है। इन पहाड़ों में बाँस से ही घर बनता है, खेत की बाड़ लगती है और पानी ढोया जाता है। तो ज़ाहिर है कि बरकत देने वाले देवता इसमें बड़े आराम से विराजते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He is the giver of the year's essentials — the harvest, the herds, the children, the luck of the house — and for his days he takes a humble and beautiful form: a bamboo staff, dressed and honoured, carried by his own procession. In these hills bamboo builds the house, fences the field and carries the water. Of course the giver of plenty is at home in it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-garia-puja.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.garia-puja|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.garia-puja-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.garia-puja:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The God Who Comes Up Your Steps","text":"\"शोभायात्रा एक आँगन से दूसरे आँगन जाती है — एक बार में एक आँगन, कोई भी घर छोटा नहीं — ढोल, बाँसुरी और गरिया नर्तकों के साथ, जो जिस भी आँगन में कदम रखते हैं, वहीं नाचते हैं। आशीर्वाद नाचते हुए हर घर तक अलग से पहुँचाया जाता है। इस पावन अवसर का हिस्सा बनने के लिए किसी को कहीं जाने की ज़रूरत नहीं; यह अपनापन ख़ुद चलकर आता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The procession goes from courtyard to courtyard — an aangan at a time, no house too small — with drums and flute and the Garia dancers, who dance in every yard they enter. The blessing is danced into each household separately. Nobody has to travel to be included; being included travels.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-garia-puja.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.garia-puja|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.garia-puja-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.garia-puja:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The God Who Comes Up Your Steps","text":"\"हर परिवार उनका स्वागत उन चीज़ों से करता है जो रसोई और खेत दे सकते हैं — चावल, फल, एक अंडा, कपास — सीधी-सादी चीज़ें, वही चीज़ें जो उनके दिए पूरे साल में मिलती हैं, और साल की शुरुआत में ही उन्हें वापस भेंट कर दी जाती हैं। यह चक्र इससे साफ़ और क्या हो सकता है: जो वे देते हैं, वही उन्हें लौटाया जाता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Each family welcomes him with what the kitchen and the field can give — rice, fruit, an egg, cotton — simple things, the things his year actually provides, offered back to him at the start of it. The circle could not be drawn plainer: what he gives is what he is given.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-garia-puja.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.garia-puja|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.garia-puja-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.garia-puja:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The God Who Comes Up Your Steps","text":"\"खासकर जमातिया लोगों में, गरिया के दिन बड़े आदर और नियम से मनाए जाते हैं — समाज के अपने पुरोहित, पारंपरिक गीत, और पुराने तौर-तरीक़े जिन्हें बड़े जतन से सँभाला गया है। जो नाच शायद आपने किसी मेले के मंच पर देखा हो, वह तो बस उसी बात की सजी-संवरी गूँज है जो परिवार अपने घरों में पूरे दिल से करते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Among the Jamatia people especially, Garia's days are kept with great seriousness — the community's own priests, the proper songs, the old order of things held carefully. The dance you may have seen on a stage at a festival is the polished echo of something families do at home with their whole hearts.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-garia-puja.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.garia-puja|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.garia-puja-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.garia-puja:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The God Who Comes Up Your Steps","text":"\"ढोल की थाप, एक बार सुन लो, तो मन में बस जाती है — यह शोभायात्रा के पहुँचने से पहले ही गली में गूँजने लगती है, मानो आशीर्वाद ने किसी धावक की तरह अपनी आवाज़ पहले ही आगे भेज दी हो, और बच्चे इंतज़ार में दरवाज़ों से बाहर उमड़ पड़ते हैं। हर एक घर में यूँ इंतज़ार किया जाना: देवता का हफ़्ता सचमुच सफल हो जाता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The drumming, once heard, stays with you — it comes up the lane before the procession does, so that the blessing sends its sound ahead like a runner, and children spill out of doorways to wait. Being waited for at every single house: that is a god's week well spent.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-garia-puja.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.garia-puja|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.garia-puja-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.garia-puja:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The God Who Comes Up Your Steps","text":"\"और जब नर्तक अगले आँगन की ओर बढ़ जाते हैं और ढोल की आवाज़ गली में दूर मद्धम पड़ जाती है, तो हर घर में वही शांत हिसाब-किताब रह जाता है: ज़रा-से चावल दिए, और बदले में पूरा साल माँग लिया। और गरिया ने कभी इस लेन-देन के भाव पर कोई ऐतराज़ किया हो, ऐसा तो कभी सुनने में नहीं आया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And when the dancers have gone on to the next courtyard and the drums have faded down the lane, each house is left with the same quiet arithmetic: a little rice given, a whole year asked for. Garia has never been reported to object to the exchange rate.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-garia-puja.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.garia-puja|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rignai-loom-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rignai-loom:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Loom Tied to the Weaver","text":"त्रिपुरा की पहाड़ियों में जगह-जगह बरामदों में आपको एक ऐसा करघा दिखेगा जिसमें न कोई ढांचा है, न पाए, और न ही कहीं कोई मशीन। धागों का एक सिरा दीवार या किसी खंभे से बंधा होता है। दूसरा सिरा एक पट्टा होता है — और वह पट्टा बुनकर की अपनी पीठ के पीछे से निकलता है। वह पीछे की ओर झुकती है, और धागे तन जाते हैं। वह करघे पर सिर्फ बैठी नहीं है। वह खुद उसका हिस्सा है।","lang":"hi","body":"On verandas all over the hills of Tripura you will find a loom with no frame, no legs, and no machine anywhere in it. One end of the threads is tied to the wall or a post. The other end is a strap — and the strap goes around the weaver's own back. She leans away, and the threads come taut. She is not sitting at the loom. She is part of it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rignai-loom.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rignai-loom|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rignai-loom-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rignai-loom:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Loom Tied to the Weaver","text":"यह बैकस्ट्रैप लूम यानी कमर-करघा है, और पूरे पूर्वोत्तर के पहाड़ी लोग इसके माहिर हैं। त्रिपुरा में यह बोरोक समुदायों — त्रिपुरी, रियांग, जमातिया और उनके पड़ोसियों — की महिलाओं का हुनर है, जो माँ से बेटी तक तभी से चला आ रहा है जब से माँ और बेटियाँ हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"This is the loin-loom, the backstrap loom, and the hill peoples of the whole Northeast are its masters. In Tripura it is the women's art of the Borok communities — Tripuri, Reang, Jamatia and their neighbours — passed from mother to daughter for as long as there have been mothers and daughters.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rignai-loom.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rignai-loom|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rignai-loom-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rignai-loom:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Loom Tied to the Weaver","text":"इससे धागा-दर-धागा जो बनकर निकलता है, वह है रिग्नाई — बुना हुआ परिधान जो इन पहाड़ियों की औरतें पहनती हैं — और रिशा, बुना हुआ दुपट्टा। ऐसी धारियाँ, चौकोर आकृतियाँ और बॉर्डर जिनके रंग पूरी घाटी के पार से चमक उठें: लाल, काले, नारंगी, और कभी-कभार दिखने वाला वह खास हरा रंग जो अपनी अलग ही धाक जमाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"What comes off it, thread by thread, is the rignai — the woven wrap the women of these hills wear — and the risha, the woven breast-cloth and stole. Stripes and diamonds and borders in colours that carry across a valley: reds, blacks, oranges, the occasional green that means business.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rignai-loom.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rignai-loom|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rignai-loom-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rignai-loom:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Loom Tied to the Weaver","text":"और ये डिज़ाइन कोई महज़ सजावट नहीं हैं। ये अपनी पहचान हैं। हर समुदाय अपनी रिग्नाई खुद बुनता है — अपने रंग, अपनी सजावट — ताकि कपड़े की पहचान रखने वाली कोई भी औरत बाज़ार में खड़ी होकर पढ़ सके कि सामने वाली औरत कहाँ से है, बिल्कुल वैसे जैसे कोई नाम पढ़ा जाता है। यह डिज़ाइन धागों में लिखा हुआ एक पता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And the patterns are not decoration. They are belonging. Each community weaves its own rignai — its own colours, its own arrangements — so that a woman who knows cloth can stand in a market and read where every other woman is from, the way you read a name. The pattern is an address written in thread.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rignai-loom.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rignai-loom|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rignai-loom-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rignai-loom:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Loom Tied to the Weaver","text":"लड़कियाँ छोटी उम्र में ही अपनी माँ के पास बैठकर सीखती हैं — पहले देख-देखकर, फिर धागा लपेटकर, और फिर वह दिन आता है जब पट्टा पहली बार उनकी अपनी पीठ पर बंधता है और अचानक पूरा करघा इस बात पर निर्भर हो जाता है कि वे कितनी स्थिरता से बैठती हैं। \"कपड़ा तुम्हारे मिज़ाज को भाँप लेता है,\" माँ कहती है। \"ज़रा भी हिली-डुलीं, तो यह उसे याद रखेगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Girls learn young, beside their mothers — first watching, then winding thread, then the day the strap goes around their own back for the first time and the whole loom suddenly depends on how still they sit. \"The cloth feels your mood,\" a mother will say. \"Fidget, and it remembers.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rignai-loom.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rignai-loom|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rignai-loom-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rignai-loom:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Loom Tied to the Weaver","text":"\"रिशा सिर्फ़ एक कपड़ा भर नहीं है—किसी मेहमान के कंधों पर डाला जाए तो यह एक सम्मान है, ज़िंदगी के बड़े पड़ावों पर दिया जाए तो यह एक ऐसा आशीर्वाद है जिसे आप हाथों में थाम सकते हैं। जब त्रिपुरा किसी का आदर-सत्कार करना चाहता है, तो वह अक्सर कपड़ों के ज़रिए ही करता है, और वह कपड़ा किसी न किसी माँ ने अपने शरीर से बाँधकर रखे करघे पर बुना होता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A risha is more than clothing, too — laid across a guest's shoulders it is an honour, given at life's big doorways it is a blessing you can hold. When Tripura wants to honour somebody, it very often does it in cloth, and the cloth was woven by somebody's mother on a loom tied to her own body.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rignai-loom.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rignai-loom|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rignai-loom-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rignai-loom:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Loom Tied to the Weaver","text":"\"और चूँकि यह करघा सिमटकर ना के बराबर रह जाता है—बस कुछ लकड़ियों और धागों की एक गठरी जिसे आप दीवार पर टाँग सकते हैं—तो जहाँ-जहाँ बुनकर गए, यह भी उनके साथ हर जगह पहुँचा। न किसी कारख़ाने की ज़रूरत, न किसी मशीन के खोने का डर। एक पट्टी और दीवार के सहारे कोई भी महिला दुनिया के किसी भी बरामदे में पाँच सौ साल पुरानी परंपरा सजा सकती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And because the loom folds up into almost nothing — a bundle of sticks and thread you can hang on a wall — it has travelled everywhere the weavers have. No workshop required, no machine to lose. A woman with a strap and a wall can set up five hundred years of tradition on any veranda on earth.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rignai-loom.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rignai-loom|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.matabari-turtles-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.matabari-turtles:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother's House by the Turtle Lake","text":"\"त्रिपुरा के हरे-भरे दक्षिणी हिस्से में बसे उदयपुर में राज्य का सबसे प्यारा मंदिर है: त्रिपुर सुंदरी, इस पावन धरती की सुंदर देवी का मंदिर। सब लोग इस जगह को माताबाड़ी कहते हैं—यानी माँ का घर—और इसे बिलकुल वैसे ही माना जाता है: किसी स्मारक की तरह नहीं, बल्कि एक घर की तरह, जिसमें माँ अपने घर पर ही मौजूद हों।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In Udaipur, in the green south of Tripura, stands the state's most beloved temple: Tripura Sundari, the beautiful goddess of the land. Everyone calls the place Matabari — the Mother's house — and that is exactly how it is treated: not as a monument, as a house, with the Mother at home in it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-matabari-turtles.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.matabari-turtles|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.matabari-turtles-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.matabari-turtles:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother's House by the Turtle Lake","text":"\"इसकी गिनती शक्तिपीठों में होती है—देवी माँ के वे महान पावन धाम जो इस देश के पूरे नक़्शे पर फैले हुए हैं, जिनमें से हर जगह यह माना जाता है कि माँ विशेष रूप से विराजमान हैं। त्रिपुरा का यह धाम बेहद आदरणीय धामों में से एक है, और यहाँ राज्य के बाहर दूर-दूर से तीर्थयात्री आते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It is counted among the Shakti Pithas — the great seats of the Goddess spread across the whole map of this land, each one a place where the Mother is held to be specially present. Tripura's seat is one of the honoured ones, and pilgrims come from far beyond the state.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-matabari-turtles.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.matabari-turtles|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.matabari-turtles-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.matabari-turtles:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother's House by the Turtle Lake","text":"\"और जिस पहाड़ी पर यह मंदिर खड़ा है, उसकी बनावट ऐसी है जिसे लोग बड़े चाव से दिखाते हैं: नीची, गोल और धान के खेतों के बीच से ऊपर उठती हुई कछुए की पीठ जैसी। वे इसे कूर्म पीठ यानी कछुआ पीठ कहते हैं—इस बात को याद रखिएगा, क्योंकि कछुए वाली यह बात आगे चलकर बहुत सच साबित होने वाली है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And the hill it stands on has a shape people love to point out: low, rounded, humped like a tortoise's back rising from the paddy. Kurma Pitha, the tortoise seat, they call it — remember that, because the tortoise theme is about to become extremely real.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-matabari-turtles.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.matabari-turtles|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.matabari-turtles-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.matabari-turtles:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother's House by the Turtle Lake","text":"मंदिर के पास ही कल्याण सागर है — सुख और कल्याण की झील — और इसमें कछुए रहते हैं। बड़े-बड़े कछुए। खूब पुराने कछुए। ऐसे कछुए जो घाट की सीढ़ियों के पास बड़े इत्मीनान और बेफ़िक्री से सतह पर आ जाते हैं, जैसे उन्हें कभी किसी ने सताया ही न हो — और सच में कभी नहीं सताया: उस झील में कभी कोई जाल नहीं फेंका गया, कभी कोई काँटा नहीं डाला गया, कभी भी नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"Beside the temple lies Kalyan Sagar — the lake of wellbeing — and in it live turtles. Big ones. Old ones. Turtles that surface beside the ghat steps with the unhurried confidence of creatures who have never once been troubled, because they never once have: no net has ever been cast in that lake, no hook, not ever.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-matabari-turtles.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.matabari-turtles|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.matabari-turtles-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.matabari-turtles:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother's House by the Turtle Lake","text":"तीर्थयात्री और बच्चे सीढ़ियों पर बैठकर उन्हें खाना खिलाते हैं — मुरमुरे और दरवाज़े से खरीदी आटे की गोलियाँ — और वे बड़े-बड़े खोल हरे पानी में तैरते हुए ऐसे ऊपर आते हैं, मानो कोई धीमा सा आशीर्वाद उभर रहा हो। घाट पर बैठी एक बच्ची ने अपने पिताजी से वही सीधा सा सवाल पूछा: \"यहाँ कोई कभी मछली क्यों नहीं पकड़ता?\"","lang":"hi","body":"Pilgrims and children crouch on the steps and feed them — puffed rice, flour balls bought at the gate — and the great shells come gliding up out of the green like slow blessings surfacing. A child at the ghat asked her father the obvious question: why does nobody ever fish here?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-matabari-turtles.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.matabari-turtles|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.matabari-turtles-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.matabari-turtles:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother's House by the Turtle Lake","text":"फिर यहाँ का पेड़ा भी तो है — दूध की वह मिठाई जो माताबाड़ी में बनाई और चढ़ाई जाती है, और पूरे राज्य में मशहूर है; यहाँ के प्रसाद का अपना ही अनोखा स्वाद होता है जिसे लोग पत्तों और कागज़ में लपेटकर घर ले जाते हैं, और हर पुड़िया के साथ माँ के घर का एक छोटा सा हिस्सा भी साथ चला जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Then there is the pera — the milk sweet made and offered at Matabari, famous across the state; prasad here has its own taste that people carry home wrapped in leaf and paper, and a little of the Mother's house travels with every parcel.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-matabari-turtles.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.matabari-turtles|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.matabari-turtles-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.matabari-turtles:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mother's House by the Turtle Lake","text":"दीवाली पर इस मंदिर में त्रिपुरा का एक बहुत बड़ा मेला लगता है — हर तरफ दीये ही दीये, खचाखच भरा आँगन, और झील हर लौ की परछाईं को दुगना करके लौटाती है। पहाड़ों के परिवार और मैदानों के परिवार एक ही चौखट पर साथ-साथ खड़े होते हैं, और माँ का घर आख़िर होता ही इसीलिए है।","lang":"hi","body":"At Diwali the temple holds one of the great fairs of Tripura — lamps everywhere, the courtyard full, the lake throwing every flame back double. Hill families and plains families side by side at the same threshold, which is what a mother's house is for.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-matabari-turtles.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.matabari-turtles|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bizhu-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bizhu:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Flowers on the Water at Dawn","text":"त्रिपुरा के लोगों में चकमा समुदाय भी शामिल है — एक ऐसा समुदाय जो त्रिपुरा, मिज़ोरम और उससे भी आगे तक फैला हुआ है। उनकी अपनी भाषा है, अपनी लिपि है, और उनका बौद्ध धर्म है जिसे उन्होंने इतिहास की हर हलचल और विस्थापन के बीच भी सँभाल कर रखा। और जब अप्रैल का महीना आधा बीतता है, तो उसके साथ आता है चकमा नया साल: बिझु।","lang":"hi","body":"Among the peoples of Tripura are the Chakma — a community spread across Tripura, Mizoram and beyond, with their own language, their own script, and their Buddhist faith carried through every move their history forced on them. And when mid-April comes, the Chakma new year comes with it: Bizhu.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bizhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bizhu|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bizhu-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bizhu:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Flowers on the Water at Dawn","text":"इस त्योहार की शुरुआत पूरे साल के सबसे प्यारे काम से होती है, और यह काम बच्चों का होता है। फूल बिझू के दिन — यानी फूलों वाले दिन — भोर होने से पहले ही, हल्के अँधेरे में बच्चे उठ जाते हैं और झोलियाँ भर-भरकर फूल इकट्ठे करते हैं। फिर नदी या तालाब की ओर दौड़ते हैं, और दिन की पहली रोशनी के साथ ही फूलों को पानी में बहा देते हैं — एक प्यारी-सी बधाई की तरह, पुराने साल का शुक्रिया अदा करते हुए और उसे फूलों से सजाकर विदा करते हुए।","lang":"hi","body":"It opens with the loveliest job in the festival calendar, and it belongs to the children. Before dawn on Phool Bizhu — the flower day — they are up in the half-dark, gathering flowers by the armful. Down to the river or the pond, and the flowers go onto the water with the day's first light — set afloat as a greeting, the old year thanked and sent off garlanded.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bizhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bizhu|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bizhu-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bizhu:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Flowers on the Water at Dawn","text":"फूल दरवाज़ों पर भी सजते हैं, घर के मंदिर में भी, और जहाँ भी कान दिखें, कानों के पीछे भी। नाश्ते से पहले ही, जब अपने ही बच्चे पूरे घर को फूलों से सजा देते हैं—चकमा लोगों के नए साल की शुरुआत कुछ ऐसे ही होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Flowers go on the doorways too, and on the house shrine, and behind ears wherever there are ears. A house dressed in flowers by its own children, before breakfast: that is how a Chakma year begins.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bizhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bizhu|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bizhu-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bizhu:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Flowers on the Water at Dawn","text":"सबसे बड़ा दिन होता है मूल बिझू, और इस दिन की सबसे खास चीज़ है एक पकवान, जिसे 'पाजोन' कहते हैं — धीमी आँच पर पकने वाला एक ऐसा व्यंजन, जिसमें इस मौसम की मिलने वाली हर एक सब्ज़ी डाली जाती है। तीन तरह की नहीं, न ही पाँच तरह की। परिवार सब्ज़ियों की गिनती पर वैसे ही गर्व करते हैं जैसे बाकी रसोइये अपने गुप्त नुस्खों पर; साल ने जितना कुछ दिया है, उतना ही सब कुछ उस पतीले में जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The great day is Mul Bizhu, and its centrepiece is a dish called pajon — a slow pot into which goes every vegetable the season can offer. Not three kinds. Not five. Families take pride in the count the way other cooks take pride in secrecy; the more the year has given, the more goes in the pot.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bizhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bizhu|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bizhu-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bizhu:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Flowers on the Water at Dawn","text":"और यह रहा वह नियम जो बिझू को सचमुच बिझू बनाता है: उस दिन दरवाज़ा कभी बंद नहीं होता। कोई भी अंदर आ सकता है, और जो भी अंदर आए उसे पाजोन खिलाया जाता है — पड़ोसी, अजनबी, या तीन घर छोड़कर रहने वाला वह बच्चा भी जो आपको कभी पसंद नहीं आया, हर कोई। मूल बिझू के दिन किसी मेहमान को मना करना तो सोचा भी नहीं जा सकता।","lang":"hi","body":"And here is the rule that makes Bizhu Bizhu: on that day the door does not shut. Anyone may come in, and everyone who comes in is fed pajon — neighbour, stranger, the child from three houses down you have never liked, everyone. Refusing a guest on Mul Bizhu is simply not a thing that is done.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bizhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bizhu|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bizhu-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bizhu:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Flowers on the Water at Dawn","text":"बुज़ुर्ग इस पूरे जश्न के केंद्र में होते हैं — उनका आशीर्वाद लिया जाता है, उन्हें आदर-सम्मान दिया जाता है, और कई परिवारों में छोटे बड़े ही प्यार और आदर से बड़ों को नहलाते हैं। और इस बड़े दिन के बाद आता है एक शांत तीसरा दिन: आराम और आशीर्वाद का एक सुकून भरा दिन, जो त्योहार को झटके से ख़त्म करने के बजाय हौले से समेट लेता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The elders are at the centre of it all — blessings collected, respects paid, the old bathed in honour by the young in many families. And after the great day comes a quieter third: a gentle day, for rest and blessings, easing the festival closed instead of slamming it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bizhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bizhu|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bizhu-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bizhu:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Flowers on the Water at Dawn","text":"अब उस पूरी लड़ी को पूरा कीजिए जिसे आप देखते आ रहे हैं: असम में बिहू, बोडो लोगों में बैसागु, त्रिपुरा की पहाड़ियों में गरिया पूजा के दिन — और चकमा लोगों में बिझू, सब अप्रैल के इसी मोड़ पर आते हैं, सब त्योहारों के एक ही बड़े परिवार के हिस्से हैं जो इन पहाड़ियों से लेकर सरहदों के पार तक फैला हुआ है। एक ही वसंत, कई सारे नाम, और हर नाम अपनी ही आवाज़ में नए साल का स्वागत करता एक पूरा समाज है।","lang":"hi","body":"Now finish the pattern you have been collecting: Bihu in Assam, Bwisagu among the Bodos, Garia's days in the Tripura hills — and Bizhu among the Chakma, all in the same April turning, all cousins of one great festival family that stretches from these hills across borders far beyond. One spring, many names, and every name is a people greeting the year in their own voice.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bizhu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bizhu|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Eastern Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sandrembi-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sandrembi:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sandrembi and the Grey Dove","text":"मणिपुर के एक मैतेई गाँव में एक ही छत के नीचे दो लड़कियाँ रहती थीं: सांद्रेम्बी, और उसकी सौतेली बहन चैसरा। वह कुछ ऐसा घर था जहाँ एक लड़की को नया फानेक मिलता — वह पोशाक जो मैतेई औरतें पहनती हैं — और दूसरी लड़की को सिलाई-रफ़ू का काम। सांद्रेम्बी के हिस्से में सिलाई-रफ़ू ही आता था।","lang":"hi","body":"In a Meitei village in Manipur lived two girls under one roof: Sandrembi, and her stepsister Chaisra. It was the sort of house where one girl got the new phanek — the wrap that Meitei women wear — and the other girl got the mending. Sandrembi got the mending.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sandrembi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sandrembi|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sandrembi-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sandrembi:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sandrembi and the Grey Dove","text":"सांद्रेम्बी की अपनी माँ अब नहीं रही थीं। लेकिन घर के पीछे वाले तालाब में एक कछुआ था जो पहले कभी वहाँ नहीं दिखा था — और जिसे सांद्रेम्बी का नाम, उसकी माँ की आवाज़, और वह सब कुछ पता था जो एक माँ जानती है। सांद्रेम्बी हर शाम तालाब पर जाती और उसे अपने पूरे दिन का हाल सुनाती।","lang":"hi","body":"Sandrembi's own mother was gone. But in the pond behind the house there was a tortoise who had not been there before — and who knew Sandrembi's name, and her mother's voice, and everything a mother knows. Sandrembi went to the pond every evening and told her the whole day.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sandrembi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sandrembi|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sandrembi-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sandrembi:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sandrembi and the Grey Dove","text":"एक सुबह उस देश के राजा पानी के किनारे से गुज़रे, जब दोनों लड़कियाँ मछलियाँ पकड़ने की टोकरियाँ लेकर बाहर निकली हुई थीं। चैसरा तुरंत धक्का देकर सबसे आगे आ गई। सांद्रेम्बी ने राजा पर बिल्कुल ध्यान नहीं दिया — वह अपनी पकड़ी हुई आधी मछलियाँ एक बूढ़ी औरत को देने में व्यस्त थी जिसे एक भी मछली नहीं मिली थी, और ऐसा करना उसके लिए बिल्कुल सहज बात थी।","lang":"hi","body":"One morning the king of that country came by the water while the girls were out with their fishing baskets. Chaisra pushed to the front at once. Sandrembi did not notice him at all — she was busy giving half her catch to an old woman who had caught nothing, which was a thing she simply did.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sandrembi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sandrembi|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sandrembi-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sandrembi:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sandrembi and the Grey Dove","text":"राजा ने यह देख लिया। राजा लोग जितना ज़ाहिर करते हैं, उससे कहीं ज़्यादा देख लेते हैं। और जब उन्होंने सांद्रेम्बी का हाथ माँगा, तो वह सबसे पहले तालाब के पास गई। \"जाओ,\" पानी में से कछुए ने कहा। \"और जब तुम रानी बन जाओ, तब भी वही लड़की बनी रहना जिसने मछलियाँ बाँटी थीं। मैंने तुमसे हमेशा बस यही चाहा है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The king noticed. Kings notice more than they let on. And when he asked for Sandrembi, she went first to the pond. \"Go,\" said the tortoise from the water. \"And when you are a queen, stay the girl who shared the fish. That is all I have ever wanted of you.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sandrembi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sandrembi|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sandrembi-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sandrembi:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sandrembi and the Grey Dove","text":"सांद्रेम्बी एक अच्छी रानी बनी, और चैसरा की माँ से यह देखा नहीं गया। जलन ने वही किया जो जलन करती है: उसने कोई रास्ता ढूँढ़ ही लिया। एक सुबह रानी अचानक गायब हो गई, और चैसरा उसके कपड़े पहनकर उसकी जगह बैठ गई — और महल के ऊपर एक सलेटी कबूतर गोल-गोल चक्कर लगाने लगा और वहाँ से जाने का नाम ही नहीं ले रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"Sandrembi was a good queen, and Chaisra's mother could not bear it. Jealousy did what jealousy does: it found a way. One morning the queen was simply gone, and Chaisra sat in her place wearing her clothes — and over the palace a grey dove flew in circles and would not leave.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sandrembi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sandrembi|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sandrembi-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sandrembi:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sandrembi and the Grey Dove","text":"राजा को कुछ गड़बड़ होने का एहसास पहले ही हो गया, इससे पहले कि वे समझ पाते कि बात क्या है। रानी के कपड़े पहने वह औरत तालाब वाला छोटा-सा गीत नहीं गुनगुनाती थी। वह बूढ़ी औरतों को मछलियाँ नहीं भिजवाती थी। वह रानी जैसी दिखती तो थी, पर बस वैसे ही जैसे कोई तस्वीर किसी इंसान जैसी दिखती है।","lang":"hi","body":"The king felt the wrongness before he could name it. The woman in the queen's clothes did not hum the little pond song. She did not send fish to old women. She looked like the queen the way a picture looks like a person.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sandrembi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sandrembi|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sandrembi-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sandrembi:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sandrembi and the Grey Dove","text":"और हर रोज़ वह स्लेटी कबूतरी उनकी खिड़की पर आती, गाती, और भगाने पर भी न भागती।","lang":"hi","body":"And every day the grey dove came to his window, and sang, and would not be shooed.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sandrembi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sandrembi|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sandrembi-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sandrembi:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sandrembi and the Grey Dove","text":"यह वही तालाब वाला गीत था। वही, जिसे उनकी रानी चावल साफ़ करते हुए गुनगुनाया करती थीं। उन्होंने अपनी कलाई आगे बढ़ाई और कबूतरी उस पर उतर आई, थमी हुई साँस जैसी हल्की, और उसने उन्हें अपनी उसी जानी-पहचानी नज़र से देखा।","lang":"hi","body":"It was the pond song. The one his queen used to hum with her hands in the rice. He held out his wrist and the dove came down onto it, light as a held breath, and looked at him with an eye he knew.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sandrembi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sandrembi|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sandrembi-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sandrembi:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sandrembi and the Grey Dove","text":"वे कबूतरी को उसके पुराने घर के पीछे वाले तालाब पर ले गए। गहरे पानी में कछुई ऊपर तैर आई और कबूतरी उससे मिलने नीचे उतरी, और पानी में माँ तथा किनारे पर प्यार के बीच, उसका असली रूप फिर लौट आया — और सुबह की धूप में सान्द्रेम्बी घास पर खड़ी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"He carried the dove to the pond behind her old house. The tortoise rose in the dark water and the dove came down to meet her, and between the mother in the water and the love on the bank, the shape came right again — and Sandrembi stood on the grass in the morning sun.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sandrembi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sandrembi|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sandrembi-9":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sandrembi:9","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sandrembi and the Grey Dove","text":"चैसरा और उसकी माँ घर चली गईं। पुरानी कहानियों में उनके साथ जो हुआ उसके बारे में और भी बहुत कुछ कहा गया है, और वह बड़ा कठोर है, इसलिए मैं उसे उस तरह नहीं सुनाता। वे घर चली गईं। बस इतना काफ़ी है।","lang":"hi","body":"Chaisra and her mother went home. The old tellings say much more about what happened to them, and it is harsh, and I do not tell it that way. They went home. That is enough.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sandrembi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sandrembi|h9","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khamba-thoibi-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khamba-thoibi:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Khamba, Thoibi and the Great Bull","text":"विशाल लोकतक झील के किनारे मोइरांग बसा है, जो पुराने दिनों में अपने आप में एक अलग राज्य था, जिसके अपने देवता थे — थांगजिंग — और अपने गायक। ये गायक पेना बजाते हैं, एक छोटी सारंगी जिसकी आवाज़ मच्छर जैसी और याददाश्त हज़ार साल पुरानी है। यही वह कहानी है जिसे वे सबसे ज़्यादा गाते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"On the shore of the great Loktak lake stands Moirang, which in the old days was a kingdom of its own, with its own god — Thangjing — and its own singers. The singers play the pena, a little fiddle with a voice like a mosquito and a memory a thousand years long. This is the story they sing most.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khamba-thoibi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khamba-thoibi|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khamba-thoibi-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khamba-thoibi:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Khamba, Thoibi and the Great Bull","text":"खम्बा के न तो पिता थे और न माँ। उसकी बस एक बहन थी, खम्नू, जिसने न के बराबर साधनों में और बिना किसी ढील के उसे पाला-पोसा। वह बड़ा होकर गरीब ज़रूर रहा, पर नेक था, और इतना ताकतवर कि अपनी पीठ पर नाव उठा ले — और मोइरांग में लोगों की नज़र इस बात पर ज़रूर पड़ी।","lang":"hi","body":"Khamba had no father and no mother. He had one sister, Khamnu, who raised him on next to nothing and absolutely no nonsense, and he grew up poor, polite, and strong enough to carry a boat on his back — which in Moirang people noticed.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khamba-thoibi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khamba-thoibi|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khamba-thoibi-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khamba-thoibi:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Khamba, Thoibi and the Great Bull","text":"थोइबी मोइरांग की राजकुमारी थी, और वह खम्बा से झील के किनारे मिली, बिल्कुल वैसे ही जैसे मणिपुर की आधी कहानियाँ शुरू होती हैं। पहले उन्होंने यूँ ही इधर-उधर की बातें कीं। फिर उन्होंने हर चीज़ पर बातें कीं। कहानी के इस हिस्से को सुनाने में पेना गाने वालों को पूरी एक शाम लग जाती है, और वे इसमें ज़रा भी जल्दबाज़ी नहीं करते।","lang":"hi","body":"Thoibi was the princess of Moirang, and she met Khamba at the lake, the way half the stories in Manipur begin. They talked about nothing much. Then they talked about everything. That part of the story takes the pena singers a whole evening, and they do not hurry it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khamba-thoibi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khamba-thoibi|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khamba-thoibi-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khamba-thoibi:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Khamba, Thoibi and the Great Bull","text":"लेकिन एक और आदमी थोइबी से ब्याह करना चाहता था — नोंगबान, जो अमीर था और जिसे जीतने की आदत थी। इसलिए बात मुकाबले पर आ पहुँची, क्योंकि मोइरांग में फैसले मुकाबलों से होते थे, और मोइरांग अपने खेलों को बड़ी संजीदगी से लेता था: आप जीते, आप हारे, आपने सिर झुकाया, और फिर बाद में सबने साथ बैठकर खाया।","lang":"hi","body":"But another man wanted to marry Thoibi — Nongban, who was rich, and used to winning. So it came to a contest, because Moirang settled things with contests, and Moirang took its sport seriously: you won, you lost, you bowed, and you ate together after.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khamba-thoibi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khamba-thoibi|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khamba-thoibi-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khamba-thoibi:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Khamba, Thoibi and the Great Bull","text":"थांगजिंग के त्योहार पर दोनों के बीच कुश्ती हुई। ढोल-नगाड़े, उड़ती धूल, और पूरा शहर अपने पैरों पर खड़ा था। नोंगबान ताकतवर था और उसे यह बात अच्छी तरह पता थी। खम्बा भी ताकतवर था पर वह बिल्कुल शांत खड़ा रहा, इंतज़ार करता रहा, और जैसे ही सही पल आया, उसने पकड़ बनाई, अपनी कमर घुमाई, और नोंगबान को पानी से भरे घड़े की तरह घास पर टिका दिया — मज़बूती से, और बिना एक बूँद छलकाए।","lang":"hi","body":"At the festival of Thangjing they wrestled. Drums, dust, the whole town on its feet. Nongban was strong and knew it. Khamba was strong and stood very still, and waited, and when the moment came he took the grip, turned his hips, and set Nongban down on the grass like a full water pot — firmly, and spilling nothing.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khamba-thoibi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khamba-thoibi|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khamba-thoibi-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khamba-thoibi:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Khamba, Thoibi and the Great Bull","text":"नोंगबान उठा और उसने अपने कपड़े झाड़े। लेकिन अभी एक इम्तिहान बाकी था, और वह कोई खेल नहीं था। मोइरांग के ऊपर पहाड़ियों में काओ नाम का एक सांड रहता था — बहुत विशाल, सालों से जंगली, और हर उस रस्सी और शेखी बघारने वाले हर उस बहादुर आदमी के बस से बाहर, जो उसे पकड़ने ऊपर गया था।","lang":"hi","body":"Nongban got up and dusted himself off. But there was one test left, and it was not a game. In the hills above Moirang there was a bull called Kao — enormous, wild for years, and too much for every rope and every loud brave man who had gone up after him.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khamba-thoibi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khamba-thoibi|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khamba-thoibi-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khamba-thoibi:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Khamba, Thoibi and the Great Bull","text":"खम्बा पेड़ों के किनारे खड़ा हुआ और सांड को देखने लगा, और सांड ने मुड़कर उसे देखा। और खम्बा उस पहाड़ी पर अपने साथ कुछ ऐसा लेकर आया था, जो उससे पहले कोई और कभी नहीं लाया था।","lang":"hi","body":"Khamba stood at the edge of the trees and looked at the bull, and the bull turned and looked at him. And Khamba was carrying something up that hill that nobody else had ever brought.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khamba-thoibi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khamba-thoibi|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khamba-thoibi-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khamba-thoibi:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Khamba, Thoibi and the Great Bull","text":"\"वह धीरे-धीरे बाहर आया, हाथ खुले हुए, कहीं कोई रस्सी नहीं दिख रही थी। और उसने अपने पिता का नाम पुकारा, और वो पुराने पुकारने वाले शब्द कहे जो उसकी बहन ने उसे सिखाए थे, वही शब्द जो उस बैल ने बछड़े के रूप में हर सुबह सुने थे। बड़े-बड़े कान घूमे। वह विशाल सिर नीचे झुक गया। काओ याद करते हुए चुपचाप खड़ा रहा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He walked out slow, hands open, no rope showing. And he spoke his father's name, and the old calling words his sister had taught him, the ones the bull had heard every morning as a calf. The great ears turned. The great head came down. Kao stood still, remembering.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khamba-thoibi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khamba-thoibi|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khamba-thoibi-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khamba-thoibi:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · Khamba, Thoibi and the Great Bull","text":"\"खम्बा ढीली रस्सी थामे उसे मोइरांग ले आया, किसी पुराने दोस्त की तरह उसके साथ-साथ चलते हुए। और पूरा नगर इतना शांत था कि झील की आवाज़ तक सुनाई दे रही थी — और फिर इतना शोर मच गया कि कुछ भी सुनाई नहीं दे रहा था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Khamba led him down into Moirang on a slack rope, walking beside him like an old friend, and the town was so quiet you could hear the lake — and then so loud you could not hear anything at all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khamba-thoibi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khamba-thoibi|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khamba-thoibi-9":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khamba-thoibi:9","title":"Read it in Hindi · Khamba, Thoibi and the Great Bull","text":"\"पूरे मोइरांग के सामने खम्बा और थोइबी की शादी हुई। थोइबी ने अब तक का सबसे सुंदर फनेक पहना था, और ऐसी दावत हुई जिसमें नोंगबान सहित सभी को खाना खिलाया गया। चावल परोसे जाने से पहले ही पेना गायक नए गीत रचने लगे थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Khamba and Thoibi were married in front of the whole of Moirang, with Thoibi in the finest phanek ever woven, and a feast that fed everybody including Nongban. The pena singers were composing before the rice was served.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khamba-thoibi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khamba-thoibi|h9","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.loktak-ima-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.loktak-ima:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Holds Everything Up","text":"\"पहाड़ियों से देखने पर लोकतक आसमान के उस टुकड़े जैसा लगता है जो घाटी में गिरा और वहीं ठहर गया। यह पूर्वोत्तर की सबसे बड़ी झील है, और इस पर हर तरफ हरे-भरे छल्ले और गद्दे बिखरे हैं — मैतेई भाषा में इन्हें फुमदी कहते हैं। तैरते हुए मैदान। घास, मिट्टी और जड़ें, जो आपस में मिलकर नाव की तरह बन गई हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"From the hills, Loktak looks like a piece of sky that fell into the valley and decided to stay. It is the biggest lake in the Northeast, and it is scattered all over with rings and cushions of green — phumdi, the Meitei word for them. Floating meadows. Grass and soil and roots, woven into rafts.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-loktak-ima.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.loktak-ima|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.loktak-ima-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.loktak-ima:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Holds Everything Up","text":"\"सना नाम की एक लड़की अपनी दादी के साथ रहने के लिए नाव से गई, जिनकी झोपड़ी इन्हीं में से एक पर बनी थी — तैरते हुए मैदान पर एक तैरती हुई झोपड़ी, जिसके दरवाज़े के पास सब्जियों की तैरती हुई क्यारी थी। हर सुबह उसकी दादी का पूरा घर ज़रा सी अलग जगह पर होता था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A girl called Sana went out by boat to stay with her grandmother, whose hut stood on one of them — a floating hut on a floating meadow, with a floating vegetable patch by the door. Her grandmother's whole house was somewhere slightly different every morning.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-loktak-ima.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.loktak-ima|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.loktak-ima-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.loktak-ima:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Holds Everything Up","text":"\"अबोक,\" सना ने कहा — यानी दादी — \"ये टापू तैरते क्यों हैं? टापुओं को तो नीचे टिके रहना चाहिए ना।\" उसकी दादी अपना जाल बुनती रहीं। \"क्योंकि यह झील ही ऐसी है,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"हम इसे इमा लोकतक कहते हैं। इमा का मतलब होता है माँ। और एक माँ जिससे प्यार करती है, उसे हमेशा थामे रखती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Abok,\" said Sana — grandmother — \"why do the islands float? Islands are supposed to stay down.\" Her grandmother went on mending her net. \"Because of who the lake is,\" she said. \"We call her Ima Loktak. Ima means mother. A mother holds up what she loves.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-loktak-ima.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.loktak-ima|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.loktak-ima-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.loktak-ima:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Holds Everything Up","text":"सना दिन भर इसी बारे में सोचती रही, जबकि मछुआरे चाय के रंग जैसे पानी से अपने जाल बाहर निकाल रहे थे, झोपड़ियों के बीच कोहरा घूम रहा था, और पूरा गाँव बड़ी नर्मी से ऊपर-नीचे हो रहा था, जैसे कोई धीरे-धीरे साँस ले रहा हो।","lang":"hi","body":"Sana thought about that all day, while the fishers lifted their nets out of water the colour of tea, and the mist walked about between the huts, and the whole village rose and fell very gently, like something breathing.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-loktak-ima.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.loktak-ima|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.loktak-ima-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.loktak-ima:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Holds Everything Up","text":"फिर उसकी दादी उसे दक्षिण की ओर ले गईं, झील के उस छोर पर जहाँ तैरता हुआ घास का मैदान इतना पुराना और इतना मोटा है कि अपनी पीठ पर पूरी की पूरी घासभूमि संभाले हुए है। इसे कीबुल लामजाओ कहते हैं — धरती का इकलौता तैरता हुआ राष्ट्रीय उद्यान। और इसी पर रहता है संगाई।","lang":"hi","body":"Then her grandmother took her south, to the end of the lake where the floating meadow is so old and so thick it carries a whole grassland on its back. Keibul Lamjao, it is called — the only floating national park on the earth. And on it lives the sangai.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-loktak-ima.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.loktak-ima|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.loktak-ima-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.loktak-ima:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Holds Everything Up","text":"संगाई एक ऐसा हिरण है जिसके सींग फैली हुई डालियों जैसे होते हैं, और वह दुनिया में यहाँ के सिवा कहीं और नहीं मिलता। वह दूसरे हिरणों की तरह नहीं चलता। वह अपने कदम ऊँचे, कोमल और सँभालकर रखता है, किसी नाचने वाले की तरह हर पैर को उठाते हुए — इसीलिए मणिपुर में इसे नाचने वाला हिरण कहा जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The sangai is a deer with antlers like swept branches, found nowhere else in the world but here. And it does not walk the way other deer walk. It steps high and soft and careful, lifting each foot like a dancer — which is why Manipur calls it the dancing deer.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-loktak-ima.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.loktak-ima|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.loktak-ima-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.loktak-ima:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Holds Everything Up","text":"\"बुज़ुर्ग कहते हैं कि संगाई हमारे और इस धरती के बीच का नाता है,\" दादी ने कहा। \"इस हिरण को नुकसान पहुँचाओ, तो समझो अपने ही किसी हिस्से को चोट पहुँचाई। एक ऐसा भी समय था जब ये इतने कम बचे थे कि इन्हें परिवार के लोगों की तरह उँगलियों पर गिना जा सकता था। मणिपुर ने एक-एक करके इनकी हिफ़ाज़त की और इन्हें वापस लौटाया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"The old people say the sangai is the tie between us and the land,\" said her grandmother. \"Harm the deer, and you have cut something in yourself. There was a time when so few were left you could count them like family members. Manipur guarded them back, one by one.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-loktak-ima.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.loktak-ima|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.loktak-ima-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.loktak-ima:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Holds Everything Up","text":"उन्होंने शाम ढलते एक नर हिरण को घास के मैदान पर सँभल-सँभलकर कदम बढ़ाते देखा। ज़मीन उसके नीचे बस उतनी ही डोल रही थी जितनी कोई नाव डोलती है, और उसके पैर हर पल उस ज़मीन की थाह ले रहे थे। उसने एक बार भी नीचे झुककर नहीं देखा।","lang":"hi","body":"They watched a stag pick his way across the meadow at dusk, the ground swaying under him no more than a boat sways, his feet reading it the whole time. He never once looked down.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-loktak-ima.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.loktak-ima|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sagol-kangjei-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sagol-kangjei:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Game That Rode Out of Manipur","text":"\"इंफाल के बीचों-बीच घास का एक ऐसा मैदान है जिसे लोग दुनिया का सबसे पुराना पोलो ग्राउंड कहते हैं। इसका नाम मापाल कांगजेईबुंग है। और इस पर खेला जाने वाला खेल इतना पुराना है कि कोई हिसाब ही नहीं लगा सकता: सागोल कांगजेई — सागोल यानी टट्टू, और कांगजेई यानी छड़ी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In the middle of Imphal there is a grass field that people call the oldest polo ground in the world. Mapal Kangjeibung, it is named. And the game played on it is older than anybody's counting: sagol kangjei — sagol for the pony, kangjei for the stick.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sagol-kangjei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sagol-kangjei|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sagol-kangjei-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sagol-kangjei:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Game That Rode Out of Manipur","text":"\"मेइतेई लोगों का कहना है कि यह खेल इंसानों से शुरू ही नहीं हुआ। इसकी शुरुआत तो देवताओं से हुई थी। घोड़ों के देवता मारजिंग, जिनके पास समादोन आयांगबा नाम का एक पंखों वाला टट्टू था, वे इस खेल को लेकर आए — और पुरानी कहानियाँ बताती हैं कि धरती पर किसी के सोचने से भी पहले, खुद देवताओं ने सात-सात की टोलियों में इसका सबसे पहला मैच खेला था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The Meitei say the game did not begin with people at all. It began with the gods. Marjing, the god of horses, keeper of a winged pony called Samadon Ayangba, brought the game — and the old accounts say the very first match was played by gods, seven a side, before anyone on earth had thought of it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sagol-kangjei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sagol-kangjei|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sagol-kangjei-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sagol-kangjei:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Game That Rode Out of Manipur","text":"\"फिर लोगों ने इसे खेलना शुरू किया, मणिपुरी टट्टू की पीठ पर — एक छोटा, फुर्तीला और मजबूत जीव, जो एक पत्ते जितनी जगह में भी मुड़ सकता है। मणिपुर में इस टट्टू का बड़ा आदर है, और बोझ ढोने वाले जानवर की तरह तो बिल्कुल नहीं। यह न तो हल जोतने के लिए है और न ही गाड़ी खींचने के लिए। यह तो बस खेल के लिए है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then people played it, on the Manipuri pony — a small, quick, sturdy creature that can turn on a leaf. The pony is honoured in Manipur, and not as a beast of burden. It is not for the plough and not for the cart. It is for the game.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sagol-kangjei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sagol-kangjei|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sagol-kangjei-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sagol-kangjei:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Game That Rode Out of Manipur","text":"\"दोनों तरफ सात-सात खिलाड़ी। बांस की जड़ से तराशी गई गेंद। बेंत की छड़ियाँ, हवा से बातें करती सरपट दौड़, और इस बात पर कोई बहस नहीं कि यह खेल किसका था, क्योंकि यह सबका था — उस मैदान पर राजा भी आम लोगों के साथ खेलते थे, और टट्टू को इस बात से कोई फर्क नहीं पड़ता था कि कौन राजा है और कौन आम इंसान।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Seven a side. A ball cut from bamboo root. Cane sticks, a flying gallop, and no argument about whose game it was, because it was everybody's — kings played commoners on that ground, and the pony did not care which was which.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sagol-kangjei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sagol-kangjei|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sagol-kangjei-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sagol-kangjei:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Game That Rode Out of Manipur","text":"\"फिर, डेढ़ सौ से भी ज्यादा साल पहले, कुछ मेहमान आए — अठारह सौ पचास के दशक में अंग्रेज अफसर — और मैदान के किनारे मुँह बाए खड़े रह गए। उड़ते हुए टट्टुओं पर सवार बड़े-बड़े लोग, एक ऐसा खेल खेल रहे थे जिसमें उनके अपने देश के किसी भी खेल से कहीं ज्यादा रफ्तार थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then, more than a hundred and fifty years ago, visitors came — British officers, in the eighteen-fifties — and stood at the edge of the field with their mouths open. Grown men on flying ponies, playing a game with more speed in it than anything they had ever brought from home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sagol-kangjei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sagol-kangjei|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sagol-kangjei-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sagol-kangjei:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Game That Rode Out of Manipur","text":"बाहर से आए लोगों ने इसे सिखाने को कहा। और शहर के कुछ लोगों ने वही कहा जो लोग हमेशा कहते हैं: यह हमारा है। इसे अपने पास ही रखो।","lang":"hi","body":"The visitors asked to be taught. And some people in the town said what people always say: it is ours. Keep it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sagol-kangjei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sagol-kangjei|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sagol-kangjei-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sagol-kangjei:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Game That Rode Out of Manipur","text":"बाहर से आए लोग इसे अपने साथ ले गए और इसका नाम पोलो रख दिया। उन्होंने क्लब बनाए — पहले इन्हीं पहाड़ियों के पास, फिर कलकत्ता में, फिर इंग्लैंड में — और इंग्लैंड से यह दुनिया के हर महाद्वीप तक फैल गया। दुनिया का हर पोलो मैदान इम्फाल की उसी घास का नाती-पोता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The visitors carried it off and called it polo. They made clubs — first near these hills, then in Calcutta, then in England — and from England it spread to every continent there is. Every polo field on earth is a grandchild of that grass in Imphal.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sagol-kangjei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sagol-kangjei|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sagol-kangjei-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sagol-kangjei:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Game That Rode Out of Manipur","text":"और मापल कांग्जेईबुंग में वे आज भी इसे पुराने तरीके से खेलते हैं, एक-एक तरफ सात खिलाड़ी, मणिपुरी टट्टुओं पर। इम्फाल के ऊपर, मार्जिंग की पहाड़ी पर, पंखों वाले टट्टू की एक विशाल मूर्ति खड़ी है, जो नीचे उस घाटी को देख रही है जहाँ से यह सब शुरू हुआ था।","lang":"hi","body":"And on Mapal Kangjeibung they still play it the old way, seven a side, on Manipuri ponies. Above Imphal, on Marjing's hill, stands a great statue of a winged pony, looking out over the valley where it all started.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sagol-kangjei.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sagol-kangjei|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapta-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapta:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapta","text":"एक मेइतेई गाँव के किनारे, फूस की छत वाली झोपड़ी में एक बूढ़ी औरत रहती थी, और वह फूस काफी पुरानी हो चुकी थी। एक रात ऐसी बारिश हुई जैसी मणिपुर में होती है — यानी यूँ समझो, मानो आसमान ने यहीं आ बसने का फैसला कर लिया हो।","lang":"hi","body":"On the edge of a Meitei village lived an old woman in a hut with a thatch roof, and the thatch had seen better years. One night it rained the way it rains in Manipur — which is to say, as though the sky had decided to move in.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapta|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapta-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapta:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapta","text":"उस रात एक बाघ कुछ ढूँढ़ने पहाड़ियों से नीचे आया, और भीगने से बचने के लिए झोपड़ी के छज्जे के नीचे रुक गया। दीवार के उस पार से उसे अंदर बूढ़ी औरत खुद से बातें करती सुनाई दी, बिल्कुल वैसे, जैसे अकेले रहने वाले लोग करते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"A tiger came down out of the hills that night to see what he could find, and stopped under the eaves of the hut to get out of the wet. Through the wall he could hear the old woman inside, talking to herself, the way people who live alone do.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapta|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapta-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapta:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapta","text":"\"बाघ?\" वह कह रही थी। \"मुझे बाघ से डर नहीं लगता। भालू? हुंह। हाथी? आ जाए वो भी। मुझे तो बस टपटा बर्दाश्त नहीं होता। टपटा हर जगह घुस आता है। तुम जहाँ भी बैठो, टपटा तुम्हें ढूँढ ही लेता है। खाट हटाओ तो टपटा पीछे-पीछे आ जाता है। अरे — लो फिर आ गया — टपटा!\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Tiger?\" she was saying. \"I am not afraid of tiger. Bear? Pff. Elephant? Let him come. It is TAPTA I cannot stand. Tapta gets in everywhere. Tapta finds you wherever you sit. Move the bed and Tapta follows you. Ah — here it comes again — TAPTA!\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapta|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapta-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapta:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapta","text":"बाघ एकदम ठंडा पड़ गया, और यह ठंड बारिश की वजह से नहीं थी। कोई ऐसी चीज़ जो बाघ, भालू और हाथी, सबसे बढ़कर थी। कोई ऐसी चीज़ जो हर जगह घुस जाती थी और जहाँ बैठो वहीं ढूँढ लेती थी। और वह चीज़ अभी, इसी वक़्त बुढ़िया के साथ घर के अंदर मौजूद थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The tiger went very cold, and it was not the rain. Something that outranked tiger, bear AND elephant. Something that got in everywhere and found you wherever you sat. And it was in the house with her, right now.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapta|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapta-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapta:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapta","text":"अब, उसी घोर अंधेरी और भीगी रात में, एक चोर बुढ़िया की गाय चुराने के इरादे से दबे पाँव उसके छप्पर की तरफ़ आया। इतना अँधेरा था कि कुछ सूझ नहीं रहा था। उसने टटोला, तो उसे कोई बड़ी, गरम और रोएँदार चीज़ महसूस हुई, और — क्योंकि चोर जल्दी में था — वह उसे हाँक ले जाने के लिए सीधा उसकी पीठ पर चढ़ बैठा।","lang":"hi","body":"Now, that same black wet night, a thief came creeping to the old woman's lean-to, meaning to steal her cow. It was far too dark to see. He felt about, found something big and warm and furry, and — being a thief in a hurry — climbed straight up onto its back to ride it away.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapta|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapta-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapta:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapta","text":"कोई चीज़ मेरी पीठ पर आ बैठी है, बाघ ने सोचा। अँधेरे में। बिना किसी आहट के। जहाँ भी बैठो यह ढूँढ ही लेती है। \"टपटा ने मुझे पकड़ लिया!\" — और पलक झपकते ही वह बुत बने खड़े रहने से सीधे सरपट भागने लगा।","lang":"hi","body":"Something has LANDED ON MY BACK, thought the tiger. In the dark. Without a sound. It finds you wherever you sit. \"TAPTA HAS GOT ME!\" — and he went from standing still to full gallop in one heartbeat.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapta|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapta-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapta:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapta","text":"और इस तरह वे पूरी रात धुआँधार भागते रहे: चोर दोनों हाथों से जकड़े हुए सोच रहा था कि यह मणिपुर की सबसे तेज़ गाय है — और बाघ गड्ढों को लाँघता हुआ उड़ता जा रहा था और सोच रहा था, टपटा मुझ पर सवार है, टपटा मुझ पर सवार है, और अगर मैं रुका तो यह मुझे खा जाएगा। दोनों में से किसी की भी हिम्मत छोड़ने की नहीं हुई।","lang":"hi","body":"And so they went through the night, flat out: the thief hanging on with both hands thinking, this is the fastest cow in Manipur — and the tiger flying over ditches thinking, Tapta rides me, Tapta rides me, and if I stop it will eat me. Neither one of them dared let go.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapta|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapta-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapta:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapta","text":"पौ फटते ही चोर ने नीचे देखा और उसे धारियाँ नज़र आईं। उसके मुँह से ऐसी आवाज़ निकली जिसे आज तक कोई सही-सही लिख नहीं पाया है, वह सीधा एक गूलर के पेड़ पर चढ़ गया और दोपहर तक वहीं दुबका रहा। बाघ ने जब महसूस किया कि वह भयानक बोझ उसकी पीठ से हट गया है, तो वह और भी तेज़ भागा — और कुछ लोग कहते हैं कि वह आज भी भाग ही रहा है।","lang":"hi","body":"At first light the thief looked down and saw stripes. He made a sound no one has spelled correctly to this day, went straight up into a fig tree, and stayed there until noon. The tiger, feeling the terrible weight leave his back, ran faster — and some say he is running still.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapta|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapta-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapta:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapta","text":"बूढ़ी अम्मा जब जागीं, तो सुबह बिल्कुल शांत और धुली-धुली सी थी। उनकी गाय ठीक वहीं थी जहाँ उसे होना चाहिए था। उन्हें कभी पता ही नहीं चला कि रात भर पहाड़ों के सबसे डरावने शब्द ने उनकी रखवाली की थी — और वह शब्द खुद उन्हीं का था।","lang":"hi","body":"The old woman woke to a quiet, rinsed morning. Her cow was exactly where it should be. She never knew she had been guarded all night by the most frightening word in the hills — which was hers.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapta.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapta|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.phunga-wari-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.phunga-wari:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire Where the Stories Live","text":"मैतेई घर में रसोई के चूल्हे का अपना एक नाम होता है: फुंगा। और इसके इर्द-गिर्द सुनाई जाने वाली कहानियों का भी अपना एक नाम होता है — फुंगा वारी, जिसका सीधा सा मतलब है चूल्हे के पास की कहानियाँ। पेबेट ऐसी ही एक कहानी है। सांद्रेंबी भी एक है। तप्ता भी एक है। ये सब की सब आग के पास ही बसती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"In a Meitei house the kitchen fire has a name of its own: the phunga. And the stories told around it have a name of their own too — phunga wari, which means, exactly, hearthside tales. Pebet is one. Sandrembi is one. Tapta is one. They all live at the fire.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-phunga-wari.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.phunga-wari|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.phunga-wari-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.phunga-wari:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire Where the Stories Live","text":"ठंड के जिस महीने को मैतेई कैलेंडर में वाकचिंग कहते हैं, उसमें शामें लंबी हो जाती हैं और घाटी में कोहरा उतर आता है, और वही मौसम होता है जब फुंगा अपने होने का पूरा मोल चुकाता है। रात का खाना खत्म होते ही बच्चे पास-पास सिमट कर बैठ जाते हैं, सबसे छोटा बच्चा आग की गरमाहट के सबसे क़रीब।","lang":"hi","body":"In the cold month the Meitei calendar calls Wakching, the evenings turn long and the valley fog comes down, and that is the season the phunga earns its keep. Dinner done, the children fold themselves in close, smallest nearest the warmth.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-phunga-wari.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.phunga-wari|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.phunga-wari-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.phunga-wari:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire Where the Stories Live","text":"दादी के कुछ नियम थे, और वे नियम बहुत पुराने थे। किसी को कुछ भी सुनाने से पहले आग को खिलाया जाता है। कहानियाँ रात के खाने के बाद शुरू होती हैं, \"क्योंकि खाली पेट कहानी सुनने बैठो तो बीच में रुकावट आ ही जाती है।\" और कोई यह नहीं पूछता कि कहानी कैसे ख़त्म होती है। जब ख़त्म होनी होती है, तभी ख़त्म होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Grandmother had rules, and the rules were old. The fire is fed before anybody is told anything. Stories come after dinner, \"because a story on an empty stomach gets interrupted.\" And nobody asks how a story ends. It ends when it ends.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-phunga-wari.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.phunga-wari|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.phunga-wari-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.phunga-wari:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire Where the Stories Live","text":"और चूल्हा महज़ कोई सामान या फ़र्नीचर नहीं है। हर सर्दी में, इमोइनु ईरातपा के मौके पर, रसोई का सबसे बढ़िया खाना इमोइनु के आगे परोसा जाता है, जो चूल्हे और सुख-समृद्धि की दयालु देवी हैं — क्योंकि एक मैतेई घर में, आग के पास सचमुच कोई रहता है, उस तरह से जिससे फ़र्क पड़ता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And the hearth itself is not furniture. Every winter, at Emoinu Eratpa, the best of the kitchen is set out for Emoinu, the kindly goddess of the hearth and of plenty — because in a Meitei home, somebody lives at the fire, in the way that matters.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-phunga-wari.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.phunga-wari|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.phunga-wari-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.phunga-wari:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire Where the Stories Live","text":"एक रात सबसे छोटे लड़के को कहानी अभी के अभी सुननी थी, इससे पहले कि आग में लकड़ियाँ डाली जातीं।","lang":"hi","body":"One night the littlest boy wanted the story right now, before the wood was in.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-phunga-wari.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.phunga-wari|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.phunga-wari-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.phunga-wari:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire Where the Stories Live","text":"तो लकड़ियाँ आग में डाली गईं, लपटें ऊपर उठने लगीं, और दादी ने सुनाना शुरू किया — आज रात पेबेट की कहानी, क्योंकि सबसे छोटे वाले को कंटीली झाड़ी वाला हिस्सा बहुत पसंद था। आधी कहानी होते-होते वह अपनी बहन की बाँह से टिककर सो गया, और जब उसे उठाकर बिस्तर पर ले जाया गया, तब भी उसने उसकी आस्तीन को मुट्ठी में भींच रखा था।","lang":"hi","body":"So the wood went in, and the flames sat up, and grandmother began — Pebet tonight, because the littlest liked the part with the thorn bush. Halfway through, he was asleep against his sister's arm, and was carried to bed still holding a fistful of her sleeve.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-phunga-wari.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.phunga-wari|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.phunga-wari-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.phunga-wari:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire Where the Stories Live","text":"\"कहानी इंतज़ार करती है,\" आग को सहेजते हुए दादी ने कहा। \"कल तक यह बिल्कुल वहीं ठहरी रहेगी, जहाँ रुकी है।\" उन्होंने खुद यह कहानी एक फुंगा के पास अपनी दादी से सीखी थी, जिन्होंने इसे किसी और फुंगा के पास सीखा था। कहानी एक ऐसी आग है, जो दूसरों को बाँटने से ही जलती रहती है।","lang":"hi","body":"\"The story waits,\" said grandmother, banking the fire. \"It stops exactly where it stopped, until tomorrow.\" She had learned it at a phunga herself, from her own grandmother, who had learned it at another one. A story is a fire that is fed by being given away.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-phunga-wari.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.phunga-wari|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lai-haraoba-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lai-haraoba:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dance That Remembers the Making","text":"हर साल, जब मौसम आता है, तो मैतेई बस्ती अपने पुराने देवता के थान पर लाई हराओबा मनाती है — जो उमंग लाई में से एक हैं, यानी पवित्र उपवनों के देवता। इस नाम का मतलब है देवताओं का आनंद-उत्सव। डरना नहीं। मौज-मस्ती और उत्सव मनाना।","lang":"hi","body":"Every year, when the season comes, a Meitei neighbourhood holds Lai Haraoba at the shrine of its own old god — one of the umang lai, the deities of the sacred groves. The name means the merrymaking of the gods. Not the fearing. The merrymaking.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lai-haraoba.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lai-haraoba|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lai-haraoba-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lai-haraoba:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dance That Remembers the Making","text":"इबेम्मा नाम की एक बच्ची अपने दादाजी के साथ गई। पेना बजाने वाले पेना बजा रहे थे — वह छोटा-सा सारंगी-जैसा साज़ जिसकी यादें बहुत पुरानी हैं — और माइबी, यानी पुजारिनें, धीमी कतार में नाच रही थीं, और उनके हाथ बार-बार सधी हुई, नपी-तुली छोटी-छोटी मुद्राएँ बना रहे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"A girl called Ibemma went with her grandfather. The pena players were playing — the little fiddle with the long memory — and the maibis, the priestesses, were dancing in a slow line, and their hands were making small, careful, exact shapes, over and over.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lai-haraoba.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lai-haraoba|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lai-haraoba-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lai-haraoba:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dance That Remembers the Making","text":"\"हाथों को देखो,\" दादाजी ने धीरे से फुसफुसाकर कहा। \"अब वे शरीर बना रहे हैं — देखो, पहले सिर, फिर पसलियाँ, और फिर एक-एक करके जोड़। अब घर बन रहा है — खंभे खड़े हो रहे हैं, शहतीरें बिछ रही हैं, और उनके ऊपर छप्पर आ रहा है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Watch the hands,\" her grandfather whispered. \"Now they are making the body — see, the head, then the ribs, then the joints, one by one. Now the house — the posts going up, the beams across, the thatch coming down over it.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lai-haraoba.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lai-haraoba|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lai-haraoba-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lai-haraoba:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dance That Remembers the Making","text":"हाथ चलते रहे। उन्होंने कपास बोई। उसे चुना। फिर कातकर सूत बनाया और सूत से कपड़ा, और वह कपड़ा — एक बेहद खूबसूरत आखिरी इशारे के साथ — किसी के कंधों पर लपेट दिया गया। बीज से लेकर शॉल तक, सजने-संवरने का पूरा सफ़र, बस एक ही नाच के भीतर।","lang":"hi","body":"The hands went on. They planted cotton. They picked it. They spun it into thread, and the thread into cloth, and the cloth went — in one lovely last gesture — around a person's shoulders. The whole of getting dressed, from seed to shawl, inside one dance.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lai-haraoba.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lai-haraoba|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lai-haraoba-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lai-haraoba:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dance That Remembers the Making","text":"इबेम्मा ने देखा कि वे हाथ फिर से वही पूरा सिलसिला दोहराने लगे थे, बड़े धीरज और बारीकी से, ठीक वैसे जैसे कोई ऐसी बात कह रहा हो जिसे वह कभी भुलाना नहीं चाहता।","lang":"hi","body":"Ibemma watched the hands begin the whole sequence again, patient and exact, like somebody saying a thing they refuse to let be forgotten.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lai-haraoba.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lai-haraoba|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lai-haraoba-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lai-haraoba:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dance That Remembers the Making","text":"\"बातों को लिख लेना याद रखने का एक तरीका है,\" दादाजी ने कहा। \"यह दूसरा तरीका है। उससे भी पुराना। इसे किसी को पढ़ना आने की ज़रूरत नहीं — बस इसे नाचते रहो, और कुछ भी नहीं खोएगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Writing things down is one way of remembering,\" said her grandfather. \"This is another. Older. Nobody has to be able to read it — you only have to keep dancing it, and nothing is lost.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lai-haraoba.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lai-haraoba|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lai-haraoba-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lai-haraoba:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dance That Remembers the Making","text":"पूरा मोहल्ला वहाँ मौजूद था — चाय की थरमस लिए आंटियाँ, लड़के जो ऐसे दिखा रहे थे जैसे उन्हें कोई दिलचस्पी न हो पर देख फिर भी रहे थे, और देवता जिन्हें इस सबका आनंद लेने के लिए नीचे बुलाया गया था, क्योंकि त्योहार का मतलब ही यही है: अपने ही लोगों द्वारा देवताओं को खुशियों से सराबोर करना।","lang":"hi","body":"The whole neighbourhood was there — the aunties with flasks of tea, the boys pretending not to be interested and watching anyway, the god invited down to enjoy it all, because that is what the festival is: the gods, being given a good time by their own people.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lai-haraoba.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lai-haraoba|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lai-haraoba-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lai-haraoba:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dance That Remembers the Making","text":"घर लौटते हुए दादाजी ने कहा: \"जब तुम कुछ बोती हो, या कुछ बुनती हो, या कोई छत बनाती हो — तो तुम उन्हीं पावन कामों को धीरे-धीरे कर रही होती हो। माइबियाँ साल में एक बार यही काम बड़ी खूबसूरती से करती हैं, ताकि सबको याद रहे कि यह रोज़मर्रा का काम असल में क्या है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"On the walk home her grandfather said: \"When you plant something, or weave something, or build a roof — you are doing the holy things slowly. The maibis do them beautifully, once a year, so that everyone remembers what the ordinary work is.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lai-haraoba.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lai-haraoba|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ao-six-stones-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ao-six-stones:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Six Stones and the River","text":"\"नागालैंड में किसी आओ बुज़ुर्ग से पूछो कि आओ लोगों की शुरुआत कहाँ से हुई, तो तुम्हें कोई गोल-मोल जवाब नहीं मिलेगा। तुम्हें एक जगह का नाम मिलेगा। दिखू नदी के ऊपर पहाड़ी कगार पर बसा चुंगलीयिमती — और चुंगलीयिमती में, छह पत्थर। आओ लोग उन्हें लोंगतेरोक कहते हैं: यानी छह पत्थर।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Ask an Ao elder in Nagaland where the Ao people began, and you will not get a vague answer. You will get a place. Chungliyimti, on its ridge above the Dikhu river — and at Chungliyimti, six stones. Longterok, the Ao call them: the six stones.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ao-six-stones.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ao-six-stones|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ao-six-stones-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ao-six-stones:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Six Stones and the River","text":"\"कहानियों के अनुसार, इन्हीं पत्थरों के पास धरती से निकलकर सबसे पहले पूर्वज आए — तीन पुरुष और तीन औरतें, ऊपर पहाड़ों की धूप भरी रोशनी में। कहीं और से नहीं। यहीं से। आओ ऐसे लोग हैं जिनकी शुरुआत का बाक़ायदा एक पता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Out of the earth at those stones, the telling goes, came the first ancestors — three men and three women, up into the daylight of the hills. Not from somewhere else. From here. The Ao are a people whose beginning has an address.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ao-six-stones.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ao-six-stones|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ao-six-stones-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ao-six-stones:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Six Stones and the River","text":"\"चुंगलीयिमती में उन्होंने जीने का पूरा सलीका सीखा: कौन-सा बीज कब बोना है, गाँव की चौपाल कैसे बैठती है, कौन-से मौसम का कौन-सा गीत है। उनकी आबादी बढ़ती गई। और पहाड़ की एक धार, चाहे कितनी भी अच्छी हो, उस पर गिने-चुने ही घर और सीमित ही खेत समा सकते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"At Chungliyimti they learned the whole of living: which seed goes in when, how a village council sits, which songs belong to which season. They grew many. And a ridge, however good, only holds so many houses and so many fields.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ao-six-stones.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ao-six-stones|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ao-six-stones-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ao-six-stones:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Six Stones and the River","text":"\"दिखू नदी के उस पार ऐसी पहाड़ियाँ फैली थीं जहाँ कोई नहीं रहता था — हरी-भरी, तह-दर-तह मुड़ी हुईं, और थमी हुई साँस की तरह सूनी। पर दिखू नदी बड़ी तेज़ और ठंडी है, और पार जाने का कोई रास्ता न था। सो उन्होंने एक रास्ता बनाया: बेंत को गूँथकर बना एक पुल, जो इस किनारे से उस किनारे तक झूलता था, बिल्कुल वैसा जैसा इन पहाड़ों में आज भी बनाना जानते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Across the Dikhu river lay hills nobody had taken — green, folded, empty as a held breath. But the Dikhu is quick and cold, and there was no way over. So they made one: a bridge of woven cane, hung from bank to bank, the kind these hills still know how to build.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ao-six-stones.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ao-six-stones|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ao-six-stones-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ao-six-stones:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Six Stones and the River","text":"\"नदी पार करने से पहली शाम, सारे परिवार देर रात तक आग के गिर्द बैठे यह तय करते रहे कि कोई इंसान ऐसी जगह अपने साथ क्या ले जाए जहाँ कुछ भी पहले से तैयार न हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The evening before the crossing, the families sat late around the fires deciding what a person carries into a country where nothing is ready.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ao-six-stones.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ao-six-stones|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ao-six-stones-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ao-six-stones:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Six Stones and the River","text":"\"वे पार निकल गए — पीठ पर बच्चे, कसकर बँधी बीजों की टोकरियाँ, और पूरे कुनबे के भार से धीमी ढोलक की तरह झूलता हुआ पुल। और जो उस पार पहुँचे, उन्हें इस पार जाने से ही अपना नाम मिला। उनकी अपनी बोली में 'आओ' का अर्थ ही है \"वे जो पार चले गए।\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"They crossed — children on backs, seed baskets tied tight, the bridge swaying like a slow drum under a whole people. And those who went over took a name from the going. Ao, in their tongue, carries the sense of \"those who went across.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ao-six-stones.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ao-six-stones|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ao-six-stones-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ao-six-stones:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Six Stones and the River","text":"\"हर कोई पार नहीं गया। कुछ लोग पानी के उसी पुराने किनारे पर रह गए, और उनके बच्चों के बच्चे आज भी वहीं बसते हैं — अपने अलग नामों और अपनी अलग कहानियों वाले दूसरे समुदाय। नदी ने अपनों को परायों से अलग नहीं किया। उसने तो बस यह दर्ज कर लिया कि उस सुबह कौन सा परिवार कहाँ खड़ा था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Not everyone crossed. Some stayed on the old side of the water, and their children's children live there still, other peoples with their own names and their own tellings. The river did not divide family from stranger. It only wrote down where each family stood that morning.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ao-six-stones.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ao-six-stones|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ao-six-stones-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ao-six-stones:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Six Stones and the River","text":"\"नए किनारे पर, आओ लोग पहाड़ियों की धार पर फैल गए और उन्होंने अपने गाँव ऊँचाई पर बनाए, जहाँ हवा साफ़ होती है और दूर से ही दिख जाता है कि कौन आ रहा है। और हर गाँव ने उन पत्थरों की कहानी सँभाले रखी — क्योंकि जो लोग यह जानते हैं कि उनकी शुरुआत कहाँ से हुई थी, उन्हें बिखेरना बहुत मुश्किल होता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"On the new side, the Ao spread along the ridges and built their villages high, where the air is clean and you can see who is coming, and every village kept the story of the stones — because a people who know where they began are very hard to scatter.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ao-six-stones.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ao-six-stones|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.makhel-pear-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.makhel-pear:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree Where Everyone Said Goodbye","text":"\"नागालैंड के अंगामी — और उनके अपने चखेसांग, माओ, पोउमई और दूसरे लोग, जो मिलकर खुद को तेन्यिमिया कहते हैं — एक ऐसे गाँव की बात बताते हैं जहाँ बहुत पहले वे सब एक ही परिवार की तरह रहते थे। उसे माखेल कहते हैं। वह आज के राज्य की सीमा के बस ज़रा उस पार है, मगर नक्शों की लकीरें तो अभी कल की हैं, और यह कहानी बहुत पुरानी है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The Angami of Nagaland — and their kin, the Chakhesang, the Mao, the Poumai and others, who together call themselves Tenyimia — tell of a village where, long ago, all of them lived as one people. Makhel, it is called. It sits just over today's state line, but lines on maps are young, and this story is old.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-makhel-pear.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.makhel-pear|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.makhel-pear-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.makhel-pear:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree Where Everyone Said Goodbye","text":"\"माखेल में वे सब एक ही चूल्हे के लोग थे: एक जैसी बोली, खेती का एक ही ढंग, और ऐसी शादियाँ जो सबकी दादी की आवाज़ पहुँचने जितनी दूरी पर ही हो जाती थीं। और वे खूब फले-फूले — इतने कि बच्चे बढ़ते ही गए और खेत कम पड़ गए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"At Makhel they were one hearth-people: one language, one way of planting, weddings within shouting distance of everybody's grandmother. And they did well — so well that the fields ran out before the children did.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-makhel-pear.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.makhel-pear|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.makhel-pear-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.makhel-pear:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree Where Everyone Said Goodbye","text":"सारे बड़े-बुज़ुर्ग बैठ गए, बिल्कुल वैसे ही जैसे कोई बहुत बड़ी बात होने पर बड़े बैठते हैं। आस-पास की पहाड़ियाँ फैली हुई और खाली थीं, और वे सबका पेट भर सकती थीं — लेकिन तभी, जब लोग एक ही गाँव में न रहकर कई गाँवों में बँट जाएँ। जिसका मतलब था वह बात, जिसे कोई सोच भी नहीं सकता था: एक-दूसरे से बिछड़ना।","lang":"hi","body":"The elders sat, the way elders sit when the news is big. The hills around were wide and empty and could feed everyone — but only if the people stopped being one village and became many. Which meant the unthinkable: parting.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-makhel-pear.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.makhel-pear|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.makhel-pear-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.makhel-pear:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree Where Everyone Said Goodbye","text":"और बिछड़ने का डर उन्हें भूख से भी ज़्यादा डराता था। दूर चलने का डर नहीं — भूल जाने का डर। किसी ने कहा, तीन पीढ़ियाँ बीतने दो, और हमारे बच्चों के बच्चे रास्ते में एक-दूसरे के पास से गुज़र जाएँगे और पहचान भी नहीं पाएँगे कि वे अपने ही लोग हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"And parting frightened them more than hunger did. Not the walking — the forgetting. Give it three generations, somebody said, and our children's children will pass each other on a path and not know they are kin.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-makhel-pear.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.makhel-pear|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.makhel-pear-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.makhel-pear:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree Where Everyone Said Goodbye","text":"उस पेड़ के सामने उन्होंने एक-दूसरे को वचन दिया: हम चाहे जितनी भी दूर चले जाएँ, हम एक ही रहेंगे। यह पेड़ यहाँ खड़ा रहेगा और इस बात को याद रखेगा। और कुछ कहानियों में एक शांत सा वादा और जोड़ा जाता है — कि एक दिन, जब सही वक़्त आएगा, तो ये सारे बिछड़े हुए परिवार फिर से इसी जगह इकट्ठा होंगे।","lang":"hi","body":"Before the tree they made their word: we are one, however far we walk. The tree will stand here and know it. And some tellings add a quiet promise on top — that one day, when the time is right, the scattered families will gather again at this spot.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-makhel-pear.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.makhel-pear|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.makhel-pear-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.makhel-pear:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree Where Everyone Said Goodbye","text":"फिर वे चल पड़े — एक-एक करके सारे कुनबे, अलग-अलग घाटियों की तरफ़, अलग-अलग दर्रों के पार। वक़्त के साथ उनकी बोलियाँ बदलती चली गईं, उनके बुने कपड़ों के तौर-तरीके बदल गए, और एक ही चाँद के उनके गाँवों में अलग-अलग नाम पड़ गए। वे वैसे ही कई अलग-अलग लोग बन गए, जैसे वे आज हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Then they went — clan by clan, up different valleys, over different passes. In time their speech drifted apart, their weaves took different patterns, their villages got different names for the same moon. They became the many peoples they are today.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-makhel-pear.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.makhel-pear|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.makhel-pear-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.makhel-pear:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree Where Everyone Said Goodbye","text":"मगर वह नाशपाती का पेड़ वहीं खड़ा रहा। और अब वह बात आती है जिससे आपके रोंगटे खड़े हो जाएँ: वह पेड़ आज भी खड़ा है। और जब उस पुराने पेड़ की कोई डाली गिरती है, तो वे सारे गाँव जो अपनी जड़ें माखेल से जोड़ते हैं — उन सभी पहाड़ियों पर, अपनी-अपनी अलग भाषाओं में — उस दिन आराम करते हैं, बिल्कुल वैसे जैसे कोई परिवार अपने किसी अपने की खबर पर रुक जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"But the pear tree stood. And here is the part that should raise the hair on your arms: it stands now. And when a branch of that old tree falls, villages that trace themselves to Makhel — across all those hills, in all those languages — keep a day of rest for it, like family marking family news.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-makhel-pear.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.makhel-pear|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.makhel-pear-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.makhel-pear:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tree Where Everyone Said Goodbye","text":"ज़रा सोचिए। एक ऐसा संदेश जिसे न तार की ज़रूरत है और न चिट्ठी की: माखेल के पेड़ की एक डाली टूट गई है, और हफ़्ते भर की पैदल दूरी पर बसी पहाड़ियाँ उसी एक दिन शांत हो जाती हैं, क्योंकि किसी की परदादी की परदादी के ज़माने से भी पहले किया गया एक वादा आज भी निभाया जा रहा है।","lang":"hi","body":"Think of that. A message that needs no wire and no letter: the tree at Makhel has lost a branch, and hillsides a week's walk apart go quiet on the same day, because a promise made before anyone's great-great-grandmother is still being kept.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-makhel-pear.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.makhel-pear|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-rooster-sun-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-rooster-sun:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rooster Who Keeps the Sun's Appointment","text":"कोहिमा के आस-पास अंगामी इलाके में लोग सुनाते हैं कि बहुत समय पहले, सूरज अपने समय का हिसाब भूल गई थी। किसी ने उसे कभी बताया ही नहीं था कि सुबह कब होती है — वह तो बस अंदाज़ा लगाती थी। और एक मौसम, किसी ऐसी बात पर रूठकर और थककर—जिसके बारे में कहानियों में अलग-अलग बातें मिलती हैं—उसने अंदाज़ा लगाना भी छोड़ दिया। वह देर से उगी। फिर और भी देर से। और फिर मानो उगना ही बंद कर दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"In the Angami country around Kohima they tell that once, long ago, the sun lost her timekeeping. Nobody had ever told her when morning was — she had always guessed. And one season, tired and huffy after some slight the tellings disagree about, she stopped guessing. She rose late. Then later. Then hardly at all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-rooster-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-rooster-sun|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-rooster-sun-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-rooster-sun:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rooster Who Keeps the Sun's Appointment","text":"पहाड़ धुंधले पड़ गए और धुंधले ही रहे। खेतों में धान मुँह फुलाए पड़ा रहा। लोग अँधेरे में उठते, अँधेरे में काम करते, और यह भी भूलने लगे कि कौन-सा खाना किस वक़्त का था। कुछ-न-कुछ तो करना ही था, और जानवरों ने — हमेशा की तरह — इस बात पर एक सभा बुलाई।","lang":"hi","body":"The hills went grey and stayed grey. The rice sulked in the fields. People got up in the dark, worked in the dark, and started forgetting which meal was which. Something had to be done, and the animals — as usual — held a meeting about it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-rooster-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-rooster-sun|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-rooster-sun-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-rooster-sun:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rooster Who Keeps the Sun's Appointment","text":"\"वह सोती ही रह गई है,\" बाघ ने कहा। \"मैं उसे जगाता हूँ।\" और वह सबसे ऊँची पहाड़ी पर चढ़ गया और आसमान की तरफ देखकर तब तक दहाड़ा जब तक बाँस थरथराने न लगे। सूरज ने बादलों की चादर अपने सिर पर खींच ली और ज़रा-सी भी नहीं हिली।","lang":"hi","body":"\"She has overslept,\" said the tiger. \"I will wake her.\" And he climbed the highest ridge and roared at the sky until the bamboo rattled. The sun pulled the clouds over her head like a blanket and did not so much as stir.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-rooster-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-rooster-sun|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-rooster-sun-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-rooster-sun:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rooster Who Keeps the Sun's Appointment","text":"घाटी के नीचे से हाथी चिंघाड़ा। भालू फुफकारा। बड़े हॉर्नबिल पक्षी ने अपने पंख ऐसे फड़फड़ाए जैसे पेड़ गिर रहे हों। यह उन पहाड़ों के इतिहास की सबसे शोर भरी सुबह थी, मगर सुबह का कहीं नामोनिशान नहीं हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"The elephant trumpeted from the valley floor. The bear huffed. The great hornbill clapped his wings like falling trees. It was the loudest morning in the history of the hills, and it produced no morning whatsoever.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-rooster-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-rooster-sun|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-rooster-sun-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-rooster-sun:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rooster Who Keeps the Sun's Appointment","text":"सभा में सबसे पीछे मुर्गा खड़ा था, जो छोटा-सा था, और चिल्लाने के बजाय चुपचाप सबकी बातें सुन रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"At the back of the meeting stood the rooster, who was small, and had been listening instead of shouting.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-rooster-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-rooster-sun|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-rooster-sun-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-rooster-sun:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rooster Who Keeps the Sun's Appointment","text":"मुर्गा पहाड़ी की चोटी पर चढ़ा, पूरब की तरफ़ मुँह किया, और सधी हुई आवाज़ में बोला: \"सूरज दादी। किसी ने कभी वक़्त का हिसाब रखने में आपकी मदद नहीं की, और यह हमारी ग़लती थी, आपकी नहीं। अगर मैं आपको आवाज़ दूँ तो कैसा रहेगा? हर सुबह, बिना चूके। आपको फिर कभी अंदाज़ा लगाने की ज़रूरत नहीं पड़ेगी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The rooster climbed to the ridge, faced east, and said, at a reasonable volume: \"Grandmother Sun. Nobody has ever helped you keep the time, and that was our fault, not yours. Suppose I call you? Every morning, without fail. You would never have to guess again.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-rooster-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-rooster-sun|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-rooster-sun-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-rooster-sun:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rooster Who Keeps the Sun's Appointment","text":"काफ़ी देर ख़ामोशी छाई रही। फिर बादल ज़रा से छँटे, बिल्कुल वैसे जैसे कंबल के अंदर लेटा कोई सुनने के लिए उसे हल्का सा उठाता है। \"हर सुबह?\" सूरज ने पूछा। \"बिना चूके?\" \"बिना चूके,\" मुर्गा बोला। \"बस यही मेरा एकमात्र काम होगा, और मैं इसे पूरे गर्व के साथ करूँगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"There was a long pause. Then the clouds thinned, just a little, the way a blanket lifts when someone under it is listening. \"Every morning?\" said the sun. \"Without fail?\" \"Without fail,\" said the rooster. \"It will be the whole of my job, and I will do it proudly.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-rooster-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-rooster-sun|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-rooster-sun-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-rooster-sun:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rooster Who Keeps the Sun's Appointment","text":"और यही तय हुआ। वह आवाज़ देता है; सूरज दादी चली आती हैं। यही वजह है कि मुर्गा एकदम तनकर खड़ा रहता है और अपनी कलगी को एक छोटे लाल झंडे की तरह फहराए रखता है — वह कोई दिखावा नहीं कर रहा, वह तो अपनी ड्यूटी पर तैनात है। और इसीलिए, अंगामी गाँव में, मुर्गे की पहली बाँग ही दिन की असली शुरुआत मानी जाती है, चाहे घड़ियाँ कुछ भी कहें।","lang":"hi","body":"And that was the bargain. He calls; she comes. It is why the rooster stands so straight and wears his comb like a little red flag — he is not showing off, he is on duty. And it is why, in an Angami village, the first crow of the rooster is the real start of the day, whatever any clock says.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-rooster-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-rooster-sun|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-honour-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-honour:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Hornbill Feather Is Earned","text":"नागा पहाड़ियों के पुराने पहनावे में, पंख सिर्फ़ सजावट नहीं था। हॉर्नबिल का पंख, जो काले-सफ़ेद धारियों के साथ किसी दस्तख़त जैसा दिखता था, सिर के साफ़े में लगाया जाता था — और वह भी सिर्फ़ उसकी मर्ज़ी से नहीं जो इसे पहनना चाहे। इसे कमाना पड़ता था, और गाँव में हर किसी को ठीक-ठीक पता होता था कि इसे किसने और कैसे कमाया है।","lang":"hi","body":"In the old dress of the Naga hills, a feather was not decoration. A hornbill feather, black and white and banded like a signature, was worn in the headdress — and not by whoever wanted one. It was earned, and everyone in the village knew exactly who had earned it and how.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-honour.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-honour|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-honour-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-honour:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Hornbill Feather Is Earned","text":"एक लड़के ने अपने दादाजी से इस बारे में पूछा, क्योंकि दादाजी होते ही इसीलिए हैं। \"मोर ज़्यादा चमकदार होते हैं,\" उसने कहा। \"चील ज़्यादा ख़ूँख़ार होती हैं। फिर सम्मान का पंख हॉर्नबिल का ही क्यों है?\" उसके दादाजी ने कहा: \"क्योंकि हॉर्नबिल वो काम करता है जिसे कोई नहीं देखता। आओ। मैं तुम्हें एक घोंसला दिखाता हूँ।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A boy asked his grandfather about it, because grandfathers are for that. \"Peacocks are brighter,\" he said. \"Eagles are fiercer. Why is the honour feather a hornbill's?\" His grandfather said: \"Because of what the hornbill does that nobody watches. Come. I will show you a nest.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-honour.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-honour|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-honour-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-honour:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Hornbill Feather Is Earned","text":"एक बड़े, पुराने पेड़ पर काफ़ी ऊपर एक छेद था, और उस छेद को कीचड़ से इस तरह बंद कर दिया गया था कि बस एक पतली-सी झिरी बची थी। \"माँ अंदर है,\" दादाजी ने कहा। \"उसने अंडों के साथ खुद को अंदर बंद कर लिया है। वह महीनों तक बाहर नहीं आएगी। वह बाहर आ भी नहीं सकती। उसने जान-बूझकर पूरा आसमान छोड़ दिया है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"High in a great old tree there was a hole, and the hole was walled up with mud until only a slit was left. \"The mother is inside,\" said his grandfather. \"She sealed herself in, with the eggs. She will not come out for months. She cannot come out. She has given up the whole sky on purpose.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-honour.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-honour|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-honour-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-honour:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Hornbill Feather Is Earned","text":"और जब वे देख ही रहे थे, वह विशाल नर घाटी से पंख फड़फड़ाता हुआ ऊपर आया — काले और सफ़ेद रंगों वाला एक मीटर लंबा परिंदा, जिसके पंखों की आवाज़ उसे देखने से पहले ही सुनाई दे जाती है — और वह उस झिरी पर आ बैठा, और अपने गले से निकाल-निकालकर एक-एक फल अंदर पहुँचाने लगा। फिर वह और फल ढूँढने उड़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"And as they watched, the great male came beating up the valley — a metre of black and white with a wingbeat you can hear before you see him — and landed at the slit, and passed in fruit, one piece at a time, from his own throat. Then he flew off to find more.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-honour.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-honour|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.hornbill-honour-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.hornbill-honour:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Why the Hornbill Feather Is Earned","text":"\"वह दिन भर यही करता है,\" दादाजी ने कहा। \"हर दिन। महीनों तक। अगर वह रुक जाए, तो वे भूखे मर जाएँगे — न कोई दूसरा मौका मिलेगा और न कोई दूसरा आएगा। बारिश हो, तेज़ हवा हो, या वे मुश्किल हफ़्ते जब फल बहुत कम मिलते हैं: वह फिर भी आता है। कोई ताली नहीं बजाता। जंगल इस पर ध्यान तक नहीं देता।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"He does that all day,\" said the grandfather. \"Every day. For months. If he stops, they starve — there is no second chance and no one else coming. Rain, wind, lean weeks when fruit is scarce: he comes anyway. Nobody applauds. The forest does not even notice.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-hornbill-honour.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.hornbill-honour|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Hills of the Dawn"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]}});
